Remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen Presiding Over the Inauguration of the "Win-Win Politics" Memorial and Celebrating the 20th Anniversary of the End of the Flames of War
The inauguration of the monument, a symbol of national unity, extinguishing the flames of war, bringing peace, as well as celebrating the 20th anniversary of the end of the flames of war in Cambodia, was held solemnly with the participation of senior leaders. High of the Royal Government, civil servants, the armed forces, artists, students and thousands of people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he really enjoyed the historic event of the inauguration of the "Win-Win Politics" monument and the celebration of the 20th anniversary of the end of the Cambodian war.
* The Prime Minister prayed for the achievements of this win-win policy to remain immortal.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the implementation of this win-win policy was very difficult due to the imbalance of forces, especially the Khmer Rouge forces, which initially had only two divisions.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that another challenge was the attempt to use former Khmer Rouge leader Ieng Sary as a political umbrella to mobilize Khmer Rouge troops to surrender to the Royal Government. At this point, Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his gratitude to His Majesty the King for supporting his work in pardoning Ieng Sary at that time.
* Samdech Techo Prime Minister stated that although the win-win policy was initiated by Samdech, it could not have succeeded without the support of Samdech Chea Sim, Samdech Heng Samrin and CPP members. Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked Samdech Chea Sim, Samdech Heng Samrin, members of the Khmer Armed Forces, and all the compatriots who supported the implementation of this win-win policy.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that this win-win policy, if there is only an idea and no operator, can not be successful. At this point, Samdech Samdao to all the people who have participated in the operation until the politics of victory, victory, success. Samdech Techo Hun Sen considered Samdech Tea Banh as his lieutenant in implementing both win-win politics and other important national affairs.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the budget used for the construction of a win-win political monument is mostly the budget of Phnom Penh Capital Hall. Samdech Techo said that the budget for the construction has already spent about 12 million dollars, and some funds have been set aside to continue construction.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the decision to build a win-win political monument in Sangkat Prek Ta Sek, Khan Chroy Changva because the area will become a satellite city of Phnom Penh.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Victory Political Monument is not the home of Samdech but the common achievement of the Cambodian people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the reason for choosing December 29 as the day to celebrate the win-win political anniversary is because today the Prime Minister, the Speaker of the National Assembly and the entire Council of Ministers of the Khmer Rouge came to visit the house of Samdech This world does not exist yet.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia's Peace Island fell into the flames of war due to the coup d'état of General Lon Nol Sereimatak and Tam Cheng Eng in 1970.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the overthrow of the Khmer Rouge on January 7, 1979 was true, but this regime did not completely collapse, only changed positions and ruled, that is, the Khmer Rouge in The forest and the resistance force came to live in the district only.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that what the Paris Agreement wants is for UNTAC to end the flames of war in Cambodia. But UNTAC withdrew on September 24, 1993, without ending the war and leaving Cambodia as a country with two territories, despite spending more than $ 2 billion.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that no one would surrender to the Royal Government without guaranteeing the lives and livelihoods of the surrendering Khmer Rouge forces. Samdech asked the next generation to remember this point.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued that securing jobs and roles for the Khmer Rouge army was another confidence booster for the surrender of the Khmer Rouge forces.
* The Prime Minister added that the third point that gave confidence to the Khmer Rouge forces is to maintain ownership of movable and immovable property.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the implementation of the win-win policy began from the beginning of 1996 until December 29, 1998, starting from the Oral Mountains of Kampong Speu Province.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he wanted to take Anlong Veng district, which was the last area in 1997, but due to the explosion in Phnom Penh, it was postponed until 1998.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that although the Khmer Rouge army in Anlong Veng district had to surrender in April 1998, the war did not end because some Khmer Rouge leaders did not surrender and had to wait until December 29, 1998.
* Samdech Techo stated that the special point of the win-win political practice is that from 1996 to the end of 1998, not a single bullet was used, but by mutual trust between Cambodians and Cambodians without foreign orders. . Because of this trust, this peace has been strong and lasting until now.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the message he conveyed to the Khmer Rouge forces when he entered the Khmer Rouge occupied territories was that the Khmer Rouge surrender was not a surrender but an obligation of the next generation of Cambodians. To put an end to the fires of war that previous generations left behind.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that trust is a special point that makes Cambodia have up to 4 forces to become a single force today.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Sam Kok is not only in China, but also in Cambodia. In this sense, the Prime Minister would like to emphasize that in the history of Cambodia, there was a division of the nation, there were many divisions of control areas.
* The Prime Minister added that after 1970, Cambodia had two territories, one ruled by Lon Nol, with the United States as its base, and partly the resistance forces under Norodom Sihanouk.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that after the fall of the Lon Nol regime in 1975, Cambodia also had many areas of control by leading resistance forces in some areas against the Khmer Rouge regime, which between 1977 and 78 Samdech Build a team to fight as well.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen asks that the situation of a country with a single controlled area remains immortal for this miserable Cambodian society.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that a win-win policy could not end with the Khmer Rouge joining forces with the Royal Government, but the real success was the development efforts by connecting infrastructure, building schools and departments. Doctors, etc. in the Khmer Rouge territory were the tasks of the Royal Government.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that now the Cambodian people are no longer worried about the devastation caused by the flames of war, and the land in the war zone that used to run away is now very expensive.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that after the end of the war 20 years ago, Cambodians had a small income, but 20 years later, Cambodians receive an annual income of more than 1,400 dollars.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in order for Cambodia to achieve its goal of being a high-income country by 2050, it is required to maintain peace and a country with a controlled area.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen asked people not to disturb the lives and crops of the Cambodian people through human rights and democracy.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls on the United States and other countries not to try to make a third mistake on Cambodian soil. Samdech Techo stated that the first US mistake was to support a military coup as a country claiming to be a democracy in 1970, and the second mistake was to support Pol Pot, who killed people without regard for human rights. Support the Khmer Rouge to have a seat at the United Nations for 12 years.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that from the lack of trade volume until now, Cambodia has a trade volume of about $ 25 billion and exports $ 12 billion. Cambodia has gone from a zero-tourist country to a country with nearly 6 million tourists. The Prime Minister emphasized that this is the success of win-win politics that everyone must maintain.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech is not an individual, not a deity. But Samdech and his wife were involved in the event when the country had many eras.
