Minister of Health: Patients in Phnom Penh consume more than 60% of blood, while the nationwide blood demand per day is nearly 200 blocks
(Phnom Penh): About 500 students of the University of Health Sciences have partnered with the National Blood Transfusion Center in collaboration with Vital Drinking Water to celebrate a large voluntary and free blood donation ceremony under the theme "Blood Donation is The gift of life. ”
The ceremony was held on December 28, 2018 at the University of Health Sciences in the presence of Mr. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health and Professor Saphon Vattanak, Rector of the University of Health Sciences.
Also present were Dr. Hok Kim Cheng, President of the National Blood Transfusion Center, Mr. Ou Vannak, Director of Vital Relations and many other dignitaries from the Cambodian Red Cross, Club of Love. Ministry of Health, Association of Volunteer Doctors, Youth, Samdech Techo and representatives of the World Health Organization.
Mr. Mam Bunheng congratulated the noble generosity of the university students, who are generous in donating blood every year, which clearly shows the solidarity of the new generation of young Cambodians that should continue to be practiced. More in our Cambodian society.
Mr. Mam Bunheng said that voluntary and free blood donation is important to save the lives of patients in Cambodia, especially patients in Phnom Penh, who use about 60% of the blood while the need for blood across the country. One day, almost 200 blogs.
He added that blood donation is useful to make blood safer and for blood donors and patients to receive blood as well. In the case of anemia, blood transfusions can take place through family and friends, posing a risk to the safety of donating blood for donors.
Dr. Hok Kim Cheng thanked the students of the University of Health as well as other national and private universities who donated a lot of blood to save the lives of patients.
"Donating blood is not harmful to health, on the contrary, blood donors are heroes who can save lives," he said.
The doctor also reminded the students to drink plenty of water after they donated blood. He said that vital water is a high quality drink that is most suitable for hydrating the body to help produce blood cells. Regeneration of the body.
