This morning, Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit presided over the inauguration of the "Win-Win Politics" memorial and celebrate the 20th anniversary of the end of the war.
(Phnom Penh): On Saturday, March 29, 2018, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen presided over the inauguration of the Memorial Monument. "Win-win politics" and celebrate the 20th anniversary of the end of the war in Cambodia under the "win-win policy" of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
The inauguration of the Victory Monument and the celebration of the 20th anniversary of the end of the war took place over three days from December 29 to 31, with fireworks and concerts at night. Music for the entertainment of the people. In addition, there are many other events, including product exhibitions.
Cambodia has been devastated to ashes, and its people have suffered incalculably due to the magnitude of the flames of war in the last 30 years or so before the light of peace arrived in late 1998 under a win-win policy. Posted by Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Until now, peace, which is an invaluable value for the Cambodian nation, has been around for 20 years. The shadow of peace for 20 years has made Cambodia very prosperous in all areas, people live in harmony with a better life.
The construction of the "Win-Win Politics" monument is a symbol of national unity, an end to the flames of war and peace. This monument was built on an area of 8 hectares, 54 meters high and 36 meters wide, located in Sangkat Prek Ta Sek, Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh, in front of the Moradok Techo Stadium in the Ly Yong Phat Development Zone.
The "Win-Win Politics" monument was inaugurated on February 25, 2016. This monument was built by pure Khmer children and was built based on the content of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's win-win policy.
The grounds of this monument are divided into three areas, including:
Area 3: A harmonious area with construction in the style of the temple of Preah Vihear, Sambor Prei Kuk, Bayon.
