The six men, aged between 35 and 59, used their phones to record their violent behavior while eating a monkey alive on Facebook on November 17. He was identified and arrested by Vietnamese authorities on Thursday this week.
The monkeys are one of the world's most endangered species and are only found in northern Vietnam. One of the six factions bought the monkey from a hunter for $ 49.
Smuggling and eating of rare and endangered species is rampant in Vietnam, with most Vietnamese still believing that they can help improve health and cure diseases. However, the trafficking of these species takes place only on the black market, and it is not easy to publicize the killing and eating of them, as these animals are under the protection of Vietnamese law.
