Announcing the new director of PJ prison, a senior official of the Ministry of Interior asked the new director to strengthen the management of the prison.
(Phnom Penh): A senior official of the Ministry of Interior has asked the new director general of the prison to increase his awareness of his leadership responsibilities in managing and strengthening security on a regular basis by ensuring that all prison officials Really performed their duties professionally, did not commit corruption in accordance with the code of ethics and discipline as prison guards to help them transform themselves into good citizens.
The transfer and inauguration ceremony of the new director of the Phnom Penh Municipal Prison was held on December 28, 2018, presided over by Mr. Pao Hamphan, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior. Mr. Chhim Thida, former director of Stung Treng Provincial Prison, has been transferred to the new position of Director of the Phnom Penh Municipal Prison (PJ), replacing Mr. Pich Yon, who has been transferred to the Ministry of Interior.
Mr. Pao Hamphan, Representative of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, stated that in order to further improve the efficiency of the work, the newly-appointed prison guards should pay more attention to internal and external management. Imprisonment well.
