Discover the "Win-Win Politics" Memorial to be Inaugurated Tomorrow (Phnom Penh): The "Win-Win Politics" Memorial, a Symbol of National Unity, an End to the Flames of War and Peace, will be inaugurated. On December 29, 2018, tomorrow marks the 20th anniversary of the complete cessation of hostilities in Cambodia.
The "Win-Win Politics" monument was built on an area of 8 hectares, 54 meters high and 36 meters wide, located in Sangkat Prek Ta Sek, Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh, in front of the Moradok Techo Stadium in the Ly Yong Phat Development Zone. .
The "Win-Win Politics" monument was inaugurated on February 25, 2016. This monument was built by pure Khmer children and was built based on the content of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's win-win policy.
Next to the monument are two inscriptions. The first inscription shows the success of the win-win politics of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, which has brought the whole nation to complete peace, national unity and complete territorial unity since the end of 1998. The meaning of building a win-win monument to inscribe and preserve all the symbols, relics and achievements related as a memory and a lesson for future generations.
The second plaque shows the groundbreaking of the Victory Monument, the name of the benefactor who built and maintained it, as well as the appeals of all the benefactors who have good intentions for the historic building.
Gate 1: Sculpture on the door to religious harmony: Designs on the three main religions: Buddhism, Islam and Christianity. The symbol of Buddhism is in the center, because Buddhism is the state religion.
Gate 3: Sculptures on the Harmonization of Khmer Historical Period: Designs on the map on culture and national heritage, including selected famous temples in Cambodia from pre-Angkorian to late Angkor, such as: Sambor Prei Kuk , Koh Ker, Preah Vihear, Angkor Wat and Bayon. For the sculpture on Hor Cheang is the image of Indra sitting on a three-headed elephant on Preah Kal.
On the temple, there are three-headed elephants with garuda wings and swans, which emphasize different meanings and meanings.
Swan: The swan is an animal of the birds of heaven and a symbol of prosperity or wealth.
- Guru: Guru is a great symbolic force, fast forward, so they often compare warriors to Guru.
On either side of the entrance of the palace are statues of giant dragons, a famous myth in ancient Khmer society and also a symbol of rebirth or immortality, commonly used for architecture and urban planning, for example, Angkor Thom. Named "Yosothor".
1: Khmer Historical Harmony Area: This project is an ancient Khmer park and Khmer temple construction during the prosperous period. There are 5 temples: Sambor Prei Kuk, Koh Ker, Preah Vihear, Angkor Wat and Bayon.
2: Achievement Area: A park that creates an amusement park required by all public areas and a virtual forest that exhibits materials and achievements of the Cambodian military.
Prey Tep Nimmith is a showcase of Cambodian military achievements and equipment. This will be a place of study for all members of the public who wish to learn about the military, defense and bringing peace to the motherland of Cambodia.
