Agreement on the avoidance of double taxation and the prevention of tax evasion between Cambodia and China, Brunei, Vietnam will come into force on January 1, 2019 (Video Inside) (Phnom Penh): General Department of Taxation The Ministry of Economy and Finance issued a press release stating that the agreement on the avoidance of double taxation and the prevention of tax evasion related to Cambodia-China income tax
With this announcement, the General Department of Taxation also called on the national and international public to implement this agreement in accordance with the guidelines on the rules and procedures for the implementation of the agreement on the avoidance of double taxation and the prevention of tax evasion related to taxes. On the revenue of the General Department of Taxation and other legal standards in force to be highly effective.
An agreement between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of China on the avoidance of double taxation and the prevention of tax evasion related to income tax was signed on October 13, 2016.
An agreement between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of Brunei Darussalam on the avoidance of double taxation and the prevention of tax evasion related to income tax was signed on 27 July 2017.
An agreement between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of Vietnam on the avoidance of double taxation and the prevention of tax evasion related to income tax was signed on March 31, 2018.
