(China): In China, a generous collective symbol has been created to help sell agricultural products made by people in poor areas. The symbol was officially launched last Saturday in Beijing.
China originally created the symbol to help sell home-made products in the southwestern Chinese province of Sichuan. This symbol is the first test in China. The purpose of this symbol is to give products from the provinces and villages that need the most economic expansion have more opportunities to sell their products.
"We will encourage companies, websites and supermarkets to promote products with the 'Poverty Alleviation in Sichuan Province' logo," said Jiang Zhou, director of the Sichuan Provincial Department of Poverty Alleviation and Migration. "The parties involved in promoting this work will receive subsidies from our government."
Currently, the logo is affixed to 12 major goods and services, including groceries, tea, handicrafts, transportation and tourism services. In terms of money, these goods and services have about $ 350 million in orders in Beijing.
"We have set up a commission to promote agricultural products in order to get them to market on a large scale," said Yuan Wenxian, president of the China Association for Poverty Alleviation and Development. "This work mainly helps with products from the poorest areas."
The China Poverty Alleviation and Development Association and the China National Poverty Alleviation Bureau will jointly carry out various projects for the circulation of special agricultural products from some poor areas. Later, the two institutions will try to expand the symbol on other products made in more and more impoverished areas across China to help address rural poverty and social inequality. (China's CCTV)
(China): After the adoption of the new law, the merger will replace the three laws currently in force: the law on joint ventures between Chinese and foreign companies, the law on joint ventures. Investment in money and the law on completely foreign-owned companies.
As China seeks to establish new institutions and open markets in the country, existing laws have not been able to meet demand. And the new law aims to make it more efficient to use foreign capital.
Key mechanisms related to the coordination, protection and management of foreign capital are also set out in the draft law.
The move underscores China's reform of its institutional structure in response to recent developments in the area of economic globalization and changes in international investment law. This is according to a policy proposal by the Chinese government entitled China and the World Trade Organization, which was released in June.
In June, the Chinese government released a list of investment bans with fewer bans on foreign companies. The list reduced the ban from 63 businesses to 48 and lifted restrictions on many sectors.
The new draft law states that China intends to build and improve a system for facilitating foreign investment, as well as create a stable and predictable investment environment.
The draft law also states that local governments should strive to fulfill all types of legal contracts with foreign-invested companies. Otherwise, foreign companies should be compensated for their losses.
The draft law emphasizes the protection of intellectual property rights of foreign investors and foreign companies, as well as encourages voluntary technological cooperation based on individual company policies.
The draft law stipulates that conditions related to technology cooperation involving foreign companies should be decided by all parties involved in the negotiation, and that departments and government officials may not use administrative means. None of the forced technology exchanges.
As of the end of November, a total of 950,000 foreign-invested companies had registered in China under current law. These companies have invested a total of more than 2 million US dollars, a major driver for China's economic and social development. (China's CCTV) Excessive drinking and smoking increases the risk of coronary heart disease and death!
(Phnom Penh): Cardiologist Jin Anh Choeung, a cardiologist from Vietnam, told reporters that drinking alcohol, smoking and stress (thinking too much) can cause atherosclerosis in patients. Coronary artery disease can be fatal and can lead to heart attack and stroke in patients 20 years of age and older.
The statement from the doctor from Vietnam was made during the free examination and treatment of "cardiovascular disease" for 50 patients with spinal disease at Cho Ray Hospital in Phnom Penh this morning. December 27, 2018 In collaboration with the pharmaceutical company DHG Pharma, the collaboration between the two institutions will take place for up to 1,000 patients.
Cardiovascular disease is divided into two types:
At the same time, the cardiologist explained that vascular disease is a disease caused by blockage of blood vessels by any factor that makes the blood supply to the heart is not enough. Insufficient blood supply to the heart can cause chest pain or congestion, suffocation, or other heart rhythm problems. The other is caused by blockage or spasm and contraction of the coronary arteries, which cause insufficient blood supply to the heart.
Following the previous free monthly screening and treatment program for this course, Choray Phnom Penh Hospital, in collaboration with DHG Pharma, organized a free "cardiovascular screening" program for the first 50 new patients in One day, this collaboration will be held for up to 1,000 patients by highly experienced Vietnamese specialists from Cho Rai Hospital in Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam.
Please be informed that the free examination and treatment program for the people "Cardiovascular Disease" is a meaningful humanitarian program of Choray Hospital Phnom Penh and DHG Pharma to contribute to the well-being of the people. Cambodians have the opportunity to receive quality health care from highly experienced Vietnamese specialists along with modern medical equipment at Choray Hospital in Phnom Penh.
