By: Chao Chak Smok, Phnom Penh, December 27, 2018 The University of Economics and Finance handed out graduation certificates on "Professional Real Estate Agent" to more than 200 first-generation trainees
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of December 27, 2018, the University of Economics and Finance handed out graduation certificates on "Professional Real Estate Agent" to 200 first-generation trainees who successfully graduated.
The Graduation Ceremony was attended by Mr. Ros Phirun, Deputy Director General of the Department of Financial Industry, Dr. Chuon Rattanak, Rector of the University of Economics and Finance, and Mr. Oknha Cheng Kheng, Chairman of the Board of Assessors. And Dr. Kim Heang, President of CVEA Association of the 5th Mandate and Mr. Chrek Soknim, President of the new CVEA Association and many trainees.
Please be informed that the training program of "Professional Real Estate Agent" and "Professional Appraisal" of this university was approved by the General Department of Financial Industry of the Ministry of Economy in early July 2018. The graduation certificate is also recognized by the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
Dr. Chuon Rattanak said that the "Real Estate Agent Professional" training course that the University has been running has a total training period of 78 hours, with 6 subjects to be studied. In addition, participants must visit the study site: Construction of flats, Boreys, condos, apartments, etc., co-organized by the University and CVEA.
On the other hand, this training program requires that before graduating, participants must participate in the final exam organized by the university and have the participation of the examiner by the representative of the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
Mr. Ros Phirun, Chairman of the ceremony, said that in order to ensure the sustainable development of a society, it is inevitable to build a strong foundation through the creation of human resources with real knowledge and skills. Hard and soft skills, in general and in particular, the Cambodian real estate sector is the fourth largest sector after the textile, trade and tourism sectors that contribute to the development of the Cambodian economy.
He added that in order to build a solid foundation to promote the development of this sector to build and develop human resource capacity requires relevant actors, including regulators, operators and educational institutions to work together and play a role. Important to attract both domestic and foreign investment, especially in competition with neighboring countries and countries in the region.
He added that in the middle of 2018, the Ministry of Economy and Finance allowed the University of Economics and Finance to cooperate with the Association of Appraisers and Real Estate Agents of Cambodia to open training courses on "Professional Real Estate Agents" and "Professional Valuation". The first generation training on "Professional Real Estate Agent" started in August 2018 recently.
In that, the delegation expressed its satisfaction and support from the Ministry of Economy and Finance for the above training program by seeing the support from practitioners related to real estate and the general public who are interested and enrolled. On this skill in the first and second generation and subsequent generations.
He also praised and appreciated all the successful trainees who passed the exam and got good results and received a certificate of education recognized by the Ministry of Economy and Finance on that occasion.
Mr. Oknha Cheng Kheng, Dr. Kim Heang and Mr. Chrek Soknim also announced their support for the delegation's statement on the value of training and human resource development in the real estate sector towards further sustainable development. The three leaders also announced the support of the Cambodian Association of Appraisers and Realtors on the University of Economics and Finance training program.
