Credit Bureau of Cambodia to launch company credit reporting system in 2019
(Phnom Penh): The Credit Bureau of Cambodia (CBC) has initiated a luncheon with Cambodian journalists held at the Rosewood Hotel Phnom Penh on December 27, 2018 to share information on operations and system contributions. Credit report in the financial sector in Cambodia.
The event was welcomed and presided over by Mr. Oeur Sothearoth, Executive Director of the Credit Bureau, staff, companies and journalists from various institutions in Cambodia.
In this important meal, Ms. Sisowath Raksmey, Director of Business Development, shared the history and legal framework of the establishment of the Credit Bureau of Cambodia, the contribution of the Credit Bureau of Cambodia in the financial and economic sector of Cambodia.
She also introduced CBC Business Solutions, which helps member institutions manage risk and expand their business. In particular, from 2019 onwards, the Credit Bureau of Cambodia will launch a corporate credit reporting system that allows member institutions to check the credit statements of companies applying for business loans.
"As a result, we are proud to launch the Corporate Credit Reporting System (Jurisdiction) from January 2019, which allows member institutions to check the credit statements of companies applying for loans," he said. "
In addition to the services provided to CBC member institutions, the general public is also allowed to check their personal credit report, which currently requires the public to visit the CBC office in person. With high efforts and commitment to provide reliable and transparent services to member institutions and the general public.
