(Banteay Meanchey): A house measuring 8 meters by 14 meters, 8 meters high, with a zinc roof above the wood and brick floor was completely burned on the night of December 25, 2018 in Ponley Thmey village, Treas commune, Svay Chek district, province. Banteay Meanchey.
Colonel Chea Sloh, police inspector of Svay Chek district, said that the owner of the house, Sok Sophal, 64, and his wife, Dat Ream, 59, were in charge of a family of six, three women, living in Ponnei Thmei village, Treas commune, Svay Chek district, Banteay Meanchey province.
The inspector confirmed that after receiving the information, the police force and the people in the village and the fire truck of the district police inspectorate intervened to help put out the fire, but could not help because the fire was so big, the road was too far for the fire truck. The fire reached 4 cars. But even though the intervention was not timely, we prevented the fire from spreading to the neighbors' homes.
At the same time, the police also found some jewelry materials during the night, including 3 gold rings, 1 pair of gold earrings, 1 gold bracelet, 1 gold necklace, 3 necklaces, 1 nut, all returned to the owner. The district police inspector, Colonel Chea Sloh, urged all residents to be careful about the fire, because this is a dry summer, very prone to fire.
