Samdech Tea Banh and Samdech Kong Sam Ol Inspect the Exercise for the Inauguration Ceremony of the Victory Monument and Celebrate the 20th Anniversary of Samdech Cho Hun Sen's Win-Win Political Day
The inspection took place at the Victory Monument in Sangkat Bak Kheng, Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh, with the participation of the leaders of relevant ministries and institutions, together with the working group for the construction of the Victory Monument, the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the Royal Cambodian Gendarmerie. Lots of crowds, too.
This inspection is Samdech Pichey Sena, who is the chairman, always leads the inspection team constantly to make sure that this monument, which is a symbol of peace and national unity of Cambodia, is built in all directions and on time of the celebration. Ceremony as scheduled by the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The construction of this win-win monument started in February 2016 on an area of 8 hectares in Chroy Changva district, Phnom Penh. The construction of this win-win monument is a symbol of the peace that Cambodia has achieved after the end of decades of civil war.
In addition, this monument will be a legacy for future generations. This is an additional confirmation from General Nem Sovath, who has worked hard to lead the team to build this historic monument under the guidance and guidance of Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh.
To Celebrate the Historic Construction and Celebrate the 20th Anniversary of the End of the Cambodian Civil War in a Win-Win Politics with First Territorial Unity From December 29 to 31, 2018, open to the general public for free.
Battambang Agricultural Exporters Strongly Support and Thank Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth for Allowing Agricultural Trucks to Run Straight Without Passing Tax Terminals
Please be informed that in July 2018, Minister Aun Porn Moniroth issued a decision recommending some implementation:
1. For trucks that have a permit from the institution or authority to transport goods from the port to the warehouse or to the construction site is not barricaded or forced to park and pay parking fees.
2. For the transportation of all kinds of agricultural goods for export, it is allowed to transport directly and complete the formalities at the border without having to go through the dry port or parking tax.
3. For the means of transporting goods across borders (other than agricultural exports), they must be transported by legal route to the Customs and Excise Office or the dry port to complete the formalities for the release of goods from customs in accordance with the regulations in force. At the border checkpoints, limit or order the owner of the means of transportation to park in the parking tax business.
4: In case the car owner needs to use the parking lot or dry port, he / she must pay the service fee for that parking lot or dry port.
The Federation of Cambodian Investors Association is committed to working as a development partner in all fields with the Royal Government.
(Phnom Penh): In its fourth meeting, the Association of Investors Federation of Cambodia expressed its commitment to create a new structure to play an important role in the development partnership in all areas with the Royal Government of Cambodia, especially in areas related to the national economy. .
The 4th meeting of the Federation of Cambodian Investors Association was chaired by Mr. Suon Rindy, Chairman of the Board of the Federation of Cambodian Investors Association on the afternoon of December 25, 2018 at the High Sky Hotel in Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh.
Mr. Ley Sopheap, President of the Cambodian Federation of Investors Association, said that the Cambodian Federation of Investors Association is an important part of the development of the country with the private sector, because this association is a large association to be a national development partner with the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership. Of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
He added that the association organized this meeting to approve the structure of work in each sector to be a national development partner in line with the policy of the Royal Government. Addressing the concerns of the people and preventing the use of counterfeit drugs and products under the guidance of the Royal Government, as well as the Ministry of Health of Cambodia and the Committee for the Control of Counterfeit Products of the Ministry of Interior.
Regarding fruits, fish and meat that contain toxic chemicals, viruses and bacteria, Mr. Ley Sopheap also confirmed that the Association of Investors Federation of Cambodia will cooperate with the authorities and law enforcement forces by providing inspection equipment by distributing to the people. Citizens as a solution to get rid of germs in vegetables, fruits and meat in stages.
He added that the association also plans to promote land development, real estate, handicrafts, tourism, industry and services so that these sectors can continue to grow, all sectors related to national development must act as development partners. Ministry of Health issued instructions to people to protect their health to avoid disease as the cold weather is approaching!
