For more details, please read the full instructions of the Ministry of Health: The Minister of Social Affairs and UNICEF in Cambodia pledges to strengthen the work on the program "Social Charity for Pregnant Women and Children from Zero to Two Years in Poor Families"
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, and Ms. Nata Chapech Dison, Acting President of UNICEF Cambodia, pledged to strengthen the “Social Charity Program for Pregnant Women and Children from Zero to Two Years in Poor Families”. More to help women and children affected in Cambodia.
The remarks came as Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, received Ms. Nata Chap Dixon, Acting Director of UNICEF Cambodia, for a courtesy call and discussion at the Ministry of Social Affairs on December 26, 2018.
During the meeting, the two sides discussed the social welfare program for pregnant women and children from zero to two years old in poor families, which is important to support women and children and to establish standard mechanisms and procedures. Legal and specific to make the implementation of this program to be successful and effective in accordance with the policy of the Royal Government.
Mr. Vong Soth said that this work requires the cooperation of all ministries, institutions and relevant units. In addition, Ms. Nata Chapech Dison, UNICEF, supported the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation to advocate for the implementation of the program, as well as to strengthen the training capacity of the officers who implement the program to make it possible. In June 2019.
In the same day meeting, the two sides also promised to maintain good relations in all work and activities in order to help women, children and vulnerable victims in Cambodia.
At the same time, Ms. Natacha Pichdison expressed her position that she will continue to support the Royal Government of Cambodia, which has the Ministry of Social Affairs as the most important partner, which can make the work run smoothly.
It should be noted that the social welfare program for pregnant women and children from zero to two years old in poor families was established with the aim of improving the health and nutritional status of pregnant women and children living in poor families and to increase the absorption capacity. Take the knowledge of young children to grow to the highest potential level.
