Mr. Tuy Sopheak, Governor of Borey Chulsar District and Mr. Nut Sina, Director of Takeo Provincial Health Department reported that the maternity building and health center of Borey Chulsar Commune was built in 2018 as a gift from Mr. Meas Sophea and Ms. Chhor Borey, along with philanthropists and officers. Many other members of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) provided food to the people in Borey Chulsar commune, which at that time did not have a maternity ward for treatment and delivery.
Seeing the difficulties of the people living in Anlong Tien village, Borey Chulsar commune to find health and maternity care services and to travel to health centers as far away as Vietnam, Senior Minister Meas Sophea and Ms. Chhor Borey Meas Sophea Initiated a fundraiser to build a maternity ward in this health center in response to the necessary requests of the people in the area.
Through the search for philanthropists, Senior Minister Meas Sophea, along with philanthropists who are natives and have lived in the district, also initiated the construction of this health center to give a bond to the people in this commune so that people Get health care and maternity leave without having to walk far from home for treatment.
Through the initiative of Senior Minister Meas Sophea and Ms. Chhor Borey Meas Sophea, together with government officials, the Armed Forces and the local authority of Borey Chulsar District, Takeo Province, with the financial support of philanthropists, the construction committee also began construction of the building. The birth took place on July 25, 2018 and was completed on October 25, 2018.
The senior minister reminded that when he was young, this district did not have a health center because the area was very difficult. People live in the water for six months and six months on land, because this is a remote rural area of the lake plain on the Cambodian-Vietnamese border, it is very difficult to get health care.
But nowadays, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, in communes and villages across the country, there are health centers for almost all of our people, it is not difficult to travel far to receive health care services as before. Many private health care sectors have been set up in each province.
Senior Minister Meas Sophea also called on all people in Takeo province to remember and be grateful to those who have worked hard to build and restore the country to peace, prosperity and prosperity in all fields. Like today, do not just go and believe the opposition, go around and provoke them, they can not even help themselves.
