Currently, the vehicles have been sent to the Land Traffic Office of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police for further instruction on the procedures. Key remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of the last meeting with workers for 2018
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on Wednesday morning, December 26, 2018, met with approximately 15,606 workers. From 22 factories from Kampong Speu and Kandal provinces.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that with only a few days left, workers will receive a minimum wage of about $ 182. Samdech Techo Prime Minister said that this is the wish of Samdech.
* Samdech Techo stated that the minimum wage of $ 182 in 2019 has not yet been able to fulfill the wishes of workers, but for the situation in Cambodia, which was once devastated and torn apart by the fires of war in the past, reaching the stage This is a good thing.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that through a series of meetings with workers, many problems have been solved.
* Samdech Techo stated that those who persuaded Samdech Roeung to ask workers to get pregnant 15 minutes early are to underestimate the management of work,
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia has never adhered to the dictatorship as claimed by the opposition.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that after the maternity support policy for workers, the birth rate has increased.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government's policy to provide subsidies for workers during childbirth and women in poor families is an effort to make Cambodia a country with clear social protection services.
As Prime Minister and President of the Cambodian People's Party, Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the workers as well as the people across the country who voted for the CPP. Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that going to the polls is a participation in the democratic process and a decision to maintain peace and development through voting for the Cambodian People's Party.
* Samdech Techo stated that with only three days left, the "Win-Win" political monument will be inaugurated. Samdech Techo underlined that the inauguration of this monument to commemorate the end of the war brought national unity and national unity for the first time in the last 500 years.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that "Hun Sen" alone could not unite and liberate the nation, with the active participation of the Cambodian people throughout the country. Therefore, voting for the Cambodian People's Party is also voting for the achievements of the Cambodian people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen called on all workers to work together to protect this peace.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen explained that the size of Cambodia, Cambodia exports less than imports is not the loss of trade balance, but the large number of imports are imported raw materials from other countries to produce products for export. .
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues to call on factory owners and factory workers to work together to build a safe factory community, not to have younger and older brothers and sisters in the factory, not to consume and distribute drugs, and not to let the factory become It is also a transmission of HIV.
* Regarding the internal conflict of the former leaders of the former CNRP, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that it is impossible for two people to become one.
* Samdech Techo stated that the amendment of the law on political parties that passed the Senate and that does not require any political party, but for all political parties in Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that this law will also not allow politicians to be convicted or politicians banned from doing politics to escape the ban. That is, they have to write a letter to the Minister of Interior or the Prime Minister to regain political rights.
* The Prime Minister asked former members of the former National Rescue Party to consider whether to apply for the right to do politics again or not, because if they do not ask, they will not have the right to do politics and participate in the 2022 commune elections.
* The Prime Minister stated that commune councilors from the former CNRP will continue to hold office until 2022, and those with good jobs will continue to the next term.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that there will be seats for the Capital, Provincial, District, Municipal, Sangkat and Khan Councils.
* Samdech Techo warned former activists of the former National Rescue Party not to dream of returning to be commune chiefs, commune chiefs or commune councilors.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen also announced that do not hope for a re-election of the National Assembly. The parliamentary election is only in 2023.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed outrage over the prisoner Sam Rainsy who dared to use the freedom of his political partner Kem Sokha as a gamble with Samdech. Samdech Techo said that this bet was immoral, but Samdech had to bet at the request of prisoner Sam Rainsy.
