Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth urges the Ministry of Commerce to continue its efforts to further reform trade facilitation and maintain a good investment climate in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, on December 25 urged the Ministry of Commerce to make reforms in many areas to facilitate trade and maintain an investment climate. Good in Cambodia.
This statement was made by the Deputy Prime Minister on the occasion of being the representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, at the closing ceremony of the 2018 Business Review Meeting and the 2019 Business Practice Direction.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth stressed, "I would like to encourage and fully support His Excellency Pan Sosak and the leadership of the Ministry of Commerce to continue their reform efforts in many other areas to facilitate "Trade and maintain a good investment climate in Cambodia in the turning point of global economic and international trade."
The Deputy Prime Minister stated that Cambodia has achieved a milestone, passing the status of a low-income country to a low-middle-income country officially in 2015, and Cambodia is considered As the "new economic tiger in Asia" in 2016 by the Asian Development Bank. With this optimistic economic growth, Cambodia has achieved a proud change in both economic and social structure.
He said that in 2018, according to the initial estimate of the government, Cambodia's economic growth rate will reach around 7.3%, which is due to the strong growth of the construction sector, continued growth of the garment sector and The average growth of exports came from agriculture, the strong growth of tourism and the growth of the wholesale-retail sector, as well as other secondary sectors.
Please be informed that the Ministry of Commerce has released a report on Cambodia's exports and imports, stating that in 2018, Cambodia's trade volume with foreign countries totaled 24.985 million US dollars. Cambodia's exports to other countries amounted to 11,215 million US dollars, while Cambodia's imports were also large, amounting to 13,771 million US dollars.
