The director of the Department of Private Security Management instructs the security agents stationed at the bank to be able to observe the behavior of individuals entering and leaving the bank in case of malicious intent.
(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharaksmey, Director of the Private Security Management Department of the National Police, instructed all private security agencies stationed at banks or financial institutions to be aware of the personalities of those who enter and leave the bank. Good.
At the Closing Ceremony of the 10th Private Security Agency Training Course on the evening of December 25, 2018, Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey emphasized that when there is a suspicious incident in its target, it must be reported. Provide local authorities immediately to have timely intervention measures.
During the refresher course, which was attended by nearly 200 private security trainees, Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey stated that private security agencies are a support force for the National Police Force and protect the security and safety on the spot with the people. If the private security agent is professional, it will improve the security involvement.
With today's training, Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharaksmey advised all participants to apply this knowledge to fulfill their role in a highly effective way to protect the private interests of the public and society as a whole. Police arrest 5 suspects and release 2 Thai victims in kidnapping case in Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province
(Preah Vihear): Five suspects were arrested by the Preah Vihear Provincial Police in connection with the detention of two Thai women for kidnapping. The arrest of the five suspects took place this morning, December 25, 2018, in Sra Em Cheung village, Sra Em commune, Choam Ksan district.
Major General Yin Chamnan, Preah Vihear Provincial Police Commissioner, confirmed that the arrest of the five kidnapping suspects was under the guidance of General Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner, and General Chhay Sinarith, Deputy National Police Commissioner. Get a security plan.
The commissioner described the story that on December 23, 2018, the two Thai women were flying from Bangkok to Siem Reap Airport. After the woman got off the plane, a tuk-tuk took her out of the airport with a car waiting to pick her up at the scene in Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province.
The five suspects then forced the two Thai women to call their families in Thailand for money transfer and release. After the two Thai women told their families and sent pictures to their families to see, the families of the victims complained to the Thai Embassy in Cambodia, and the Thai Embassy continued to file a complaint with the National Police Commissioner General.
Lt. Gen. Yin Chamnan added that after receiving instructions from the National Police General Commission, about 40 Preah Vihear provincial police forces, in cooperation with the police force of the Department of Internal Security, went to the above location and besieged one of the above locations. From dawn to dusk, the crackdown was successful, detaining five suspects, confiscating some equipment and freeing the Thai woman safely.
Currently, the five suspects and exhibits have been sent to Phnom Penh for legal action. Separately, the Thai victim was sent to Phnom Penh.
