Kratie Coalition Forces Crack Down on Timber Traded in Forest Reserve at Otron Point, Sambo District
(Kratie): In the afternoon of December 25, 2018, the joint authorities of Kratie province cracked down on the first type of wood that traders hid in the forest reserve for car resale, but the police force worked. Cracked down and confiscated at Otron point, Sre Treng village, Kbal Damrey commune, Sambo district, Kratie province.
Pal Sok Keo, chief of the Sandan Forestry Administration Sangkat, said that the joint forces involved in the crackdown, including Sandan Sangkat Forestry Administration officers, the 708th Military Security Force and the Sambo District Police, raided the forest where the traders were hiding. Sales continue, but the authorities crack down on time. These trees are the first type of wood (sokrum) more than 20 pieces, but not yet measured.
The commune chief continued that until now, the identity of the owner of the tree is still unknown because the wood is in the forest and was brought by the police to be stored at the Sandan Forestry Administration Sangkat.
The Constitutional Council will hold a meeting to review and decide on the request to review the constitutionality of the law on amendments to the law on political parties.
(Phnom Penh): The Constitutional Council will hold a plenary session on the morning of December 28, 2018 to review and decide on the request of Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, to review the Constitution of the Law on the Amendment of Article 45 (Duplicate) of the Law on Political parties that can open the right for imprisoned politicians to have the right to do politics again.
According to a press release received by Fresh News on the afternoon of December 25, 2018, the above plenary meeting was chaired by Mr. Im Chhun Lim, President of the Constitutional Council.
Please be informed that the proposed law on the amendment of the law on political parties, which could pave the way for politicians whose courts have banned the right to do politics to have full rights to resume politics, was fully supported by the Senate in the morning session of the 25th This December 2018.
This session was chaired by Samdech Say Chhum, President of the Senate, with the participation of 56 senators. All senators have voted to pave the way for the law to come into force soon.
The proposed law was fully approved by the National Assembly on December 13, 2018, after being reviewed by an expert committee.
An important function of this 24-hour customs control system is to operate using artificial intelligence (AI) technology instead of being monitored by human customs officers at ports.
"Using an X-ray machine, our officers take 20 to 30 minutes to scan a document," said Thean Song, head of the vehicle inspection unit at Hang Phu Customs. "But now, using AI technology, a single scan takes only 5.2 seconds, and on average it takes about five seconds."
This smart system allows companies to fill out their own documents at the port without the need for customs officials. This greatly reduces the time as well as the cost of the customs inspection process.
According to Thean Technology AI, the system is also designed to make customs operations more efficient.
In the past, it took customs officials at least three hours to deliver a container from a ship to a checkpoint. But with this smart system, they spend the least amount of time. This is Mr. Thean Song's additional confirmation.
