A total of 43 people have been claimed dead since the attack on a government building in Kabul, with at least two people injured and taken to hospital, the report said. More than 10 others are receiving emergency treatment.
Witnesses at the scene said that after the bombing of a car parked at the site of the Afghan government building, two gunmen stormed the building and opened fire on people inside the building. Arrived and about 357 people were evacuated from the scene immediately.
The death toll and injuries are expected to rise further as security forces are still inspecting buildings damaged by the bombings and shootings as of Tuesday morning, according to Afghan officials. In Kabul). No group has claimed responsibility for the attack, but suspicions have been raised about the Taliban.
