Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara orders officials to clearly assess land types to facilitate tax collection
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction and Chairman of the National Land Dispute Resolution Authority, ordered all Cadastral Officers in all capitals and provinces to set up clear demarcation zones in the affected areas. Registered so that the General Department of Taxation can collect more taxes into the state.
The Minister's order was made at the closing ceremony of the meeting to summarize the results of 2018 and set the direction for 2019 on the afternoon of December 24, 2018 at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh.
"If we do not disclose this land assessment, the state will lose a lot of tax revenue on land issues and there will be a lot of cases related to this land issue," he said. Or cut the layout and so on.
"From now on, all land chiefs across the country must set up clear delineation zones in registered areas to avoid losing state revenue," he said.
According to the Minister, in the past, land geography has changed the type of land from agricultural land to industrial land, residential land and market land, but now agricultural land has become almost industrial land and Borey land, while the legal practice Still registered as agricultural land.
According to the report of the Ministry, which was presented at the meeting, in 2018, the revenue from cadastral services, construction services, from the lease of factory premises and from the property transfer tax collected at the tax unit amounted to 390, 476,442,711 riels, equivalent to nearly 98 million US dollars.
At the same time, the revenue from providing services at the OWSO totaled 78,517,671,247 Riels, equivalent to nearly 20 million US dollars.
Next month, the Cambodian diplomat will attend an important meeting in Europe and explain some issues in order to continue to receive the EBA.
