Ket Sophan said that during a meeting in Belgium, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon will meet with the European Trade Commissioner in charge of trade. Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon will also address human rights issues and the adherence to democracy in Cambodia in order for the European Union to continue to provide preferential tariffs on Cambodian goods except arms (EBA).
According to Mr. Ket Sophan, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon will continue to work to facilitate as well as raise realities in Cambodian society to ensure that the European Union continues to provide preferential tariffs on Cambodian goods.
