On that occasion, Mr. Nong Veasna raised some points of the Federation to ask the Ministry of Commerce and relevant ministries and institutions to participate and continue to cooperate with the Federation to solve problems and promote the Cambodian rice sector can continue to achieve more success. More in the coming days include:
1: Given the current situation of changes in the international trade market, especially in the case that the European Union plans to impose measures on Cambodian rice imports, the Cambodian Rice Federation requests the Ministry to continue to help promote and strengthen the market through G2G quotas, especially strengthening Exports to the Chinese market, our existing quotas and market diversification to more countries.
