China's transportation system has grown significantly since China began implementing its reform program in 1978. In that, the delivery service has grown better and smoother. And China's transportation sector today has become the backbone of the national economy.
In 2017, 1,270 cases of goods were shipped in China per second. In the early days of China's reforms, China's transportation services had to start from scratch. But in less than 40 years, China can ship more than 40,000 million cases a year.
The development of integrated transportation systems that combine water, land and air transport is an important cornerstone of China's transportation sector. And by 2017, the total length of waterways and railways available in China will be 127,000 kilometers.
China's railway sector has grown tremendously, from trains with a speed of less than 40 km / h to a train with a speed of 350 km / h. Per hour. The road infrastructure has also improved a lot, with China now having 136,400 kilometers of roads.
In terms of civil aviation, in 1978, China had only 70 passenger planes, with an average of 2.3 flights per airport. But now China has more than three times as many airports as before, and each airport can provide flights to nearly 20 destinations on average.
Since 2012, the Chinese government has focused on the quality and efficiency of transport infrastructure construction. And in the past five years, China has built two-thirds of all existing high-speed rail lines in China, accounting for more than half of the total destinations used regularly and accounting for nearly 30% of the total. Total highways in China.
Meanwhile, the interconnection between all means of transportation is also smoother. In fact, in 2017, the turnover rate of passengers increased by 26%, while the turnover rate of goods transported back increased by 25% compared to the rate in 2012.
As part of the One Belt One Road project, China has also become more involved in global affairs, with China doing a number of overseas projects, including the Mombasa-Nairobi railway project and Jakarta-Bandung Expressway under construction. China is doing this so that the entire global infrastructure can be connected. (China's CCTV)
