Love the environment! NagaWorld stops using plastic straws
(Phnom Penh): NagaWorld will remove the use of plastic straws from its operations from January 1, 2019, as part of the company's environmental protection project. This is according to NagaWorld's press release obtained by Fresh News on December 24, 2018.
The "Stop the use of plastic straws" campaign will be implemented across NagaWorld and Naga II, after a survey of about 10,000 employees and a successful pilot project initiated by NagaWorld's social team, or NagaWorld. Kind Heart ”since June this year.
The campaign aims to eliminate the use of about 4 million plastic straws a year, while environmentally friendly straws will be provided upon request. NagaWorld employees have already stopped using plastic straws in restaurants as the company encourages all employees to help spread the good news to family and friends.
"According to the United Nations Environment Program, about 8 million tons of plastic is dumped into our oceans every year," he said. Plastic straws are the simplest thing to throw away and float on the sea, endangering marine life, fish and tourism, and causing at least $ 8 billion in damage to ecosystems.
He added that the commitment and environmental protection project of NagaWorld Social Hearts is in line with the sustainable development goals, energy efficiency improvement and environmental impact reduction projects, as well as the 3R Waste Management Project. Reduction, reuse and recycling) of the United Nations.
NagaWorld Managing Director added that, being recognized as the best green hotel in the ASEAN region at the ASEAN Tourism Forum 2016, which has implemented a sustainable environmental protection approach, NagaWorld will continue to study and understand the concept and project. Maintain more new environment to operate its daily business for sustainable growth.
