The Ministry of Economy held a training course on the integration of awareness on the use of public financial management information systems for civil servants from the National Audit Authority
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance this morning, December 24, 2018, organized a training course on "Integration of Public Financial Management Information System (FMIS) for 60 Civil Servants. From the National Audit Authority. This training was jointly organized by the Institute of Economy and Finance and the relevant General Departments of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and the National Audit Authority.
The purpose of this training is to strengthen the capacity and understanding of the rules and procedures for the implementation of the Public Financial Management Information System for the target trainees who are civil servants of the National Audit Authority for the preparation of the audit work using the information technology system. To achieve high efficiency and to promote participation in the implementation of public financial management reform to achieve the planned goals.
The opening ceremony was presided over by Dr. Hean Sahip, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, with the participation of the leaders of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and the National Audit Authority. .
He also said that the implementation of the Public Financial Management Reform Program is currently in the third phase, aiming to increase the "linkage of budget to policy", which is scheduled to be completed by 2020 and is progressing. Better to succeed and build a foundation to continue to implement the fourth phase to increase "accountability for achievements", which is planned to be implemented from 2021 to 2025.
The Secretary of State stressed that in order to contribute to the better progress of the Public Financial Management Reform Program, the Public Financial Management Information System (FMIS) has been implemented. FMIS is an important tool for public financial management reform programs, especially budget reforms in line with international practice to achieve the goals of the reform program.
