General Neth Savoeun Inspects National Stadium to Prepare Security Plan for 40th Anniversary of January 7 Victory Day
(Phnom Penh): The General Commissioner of the National Police, General Santibandit Neth Savoeun, this morning, December 24, 2018, inspected the location of the National Olympic Stadium, which is preparing to celebrate the 40th anniversary of the liberation of Cambodia on January 7. Free from the former regime of massacre of the Khmer Rouge.
The visit to the National Stadium site was followed by a meeting on security and order planning, the 40th anniversary of the January 7 Victory Day and the inauguration of the Victory Political Memorial, which was held last weekend at the National Police.
Accompanying General Neth Savoeun, senior officials of the National Police, Deputy Commissioners-General, Heads of Departments and leaders of relevant units were present.
It should be noted that the upcoming January 7, 2019 anniversary at the Olympic Stadium will be attended by more than 30,000 Cambodians.
General Neth Savoeun instructed all competent forces to pay attention to all points in maintaining security and order and to ease traffic congestion in the area near the National Stadium. Requested the Capital Administration to inform the people to understand the roadblocks on the day of the celebration as well.
On the same day, leaders of ministries and departments responsible for participating in the January 7 festival were also seen inspecting each plan, including the installation of a billboard at the National Stadium.
In 2018, nearly 150,000 new companies applied for business registration, while 142 companies were removed!
(Phnom Penh): In the 11 months from January to November 2018, 14,552 new companies applied for business registration with the Ministry of Commerce, an increase of 138 percent. This is according to the report summarizing the business results in 2018 and the business direction in 2019 of the Ministry of Commerce, which was received by Fresh News on December 24, 2018.
Compared to the same period in 2017, only 6,108 companies applied for business registration with the Ministry of Commerce, according to the report.
