Legal Awareness: Private Company Liability Limited
(Phnom Penh): A company is a legal entity established under the scope of the law on commercial enterprises or any special law. Separately, companies established under the framework of the Law on Commercial Enterprises are divided into two forms as follows: Co-ownership companies with general co-ownership companies and limited co-ownership companies 2. Capital companies with limited liability sole proprietorships and limited liability public companies.
Also this week, Fresh News' Legal Awareness Program, in collaboration with the Cambodian Bar Association for International Cooperation, will cover the topic of corporate liability, a limited liability company in the form of a capital company. To explain to the people, government officials, students as follows:
The limited liability of this stock is relevant, especially when the company is liquidated and when the profits from the company's assets are not enough to pay off the company's debts.
Please also note that a limited liability sole proprietorship is also considered a limited liability private company, so the shareholder liability for liabilities and other obligations is limited to its shareholding and Only the assets of the company, that is, the liabilities of the company are not related to the assets of the shareholders.
