(Phnom Penh): Ms. Chea Serey, Technical Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia, presented various tips to take advantage of sectors that promote economic growth in Cambodia, which will help increase economic growth. .
Ms. Chea Serey made this statement at the 5th Annual Macroeconomic Conference on "Expansion of Sources of Economic Growth in Cambodia" held on December 21, 2018.
Ms. Chea Serey said, "The key to Cambodia's economic growth is to take advantage of the larger sectors that support the economy more, such as tourism." More tourism.
Ms. Chea Serey explained in detail about the benefits of tourism that if tourists come to Cambodia and still use imported goods, the profits are still small, so Cambodia should have a solution and find other ways that can help increase economic growth. For example, Cambodia can integrate tourism with agriculture to boost domestic production to supply other places such as hotels.
There are a number of areas that could contribute to economic growth, said Ly Sodeth, a senior global economist who specializes in macroeconomics, trade and investment at the World Bank. As you can see, the agricultural sector, such as cassava processing plants, mangoes, bananas, these can be exported without having to rely on neighboring countries, and this is to help economic growth.
He added that in addition to the electronics industry, there are recently companies from other countries to assemble electronics in Cambodia, and the actual tourism sector, Cambodia receives more tourists is in Sihanoukville, while before. Only Angkor Wat.
Please note that the Macroeconomic Conference is organized in order to contribute to the development of research capacity and provide a forum for discussion on important topics of the Cambodian economy. Chbar Ampov District Launches Public Awareness Campaign at OWSO
(Phnom Penh): Chbar Ampov district administration this morning, December 21, launched a campaign to disseminate to local people to understand the price list and the provision of public services in the OWSO of the district.
The campaign was conducted simultaneously between the eight communes, with the working group in each commune distributing the price list of services in each section of the OWSO.
Chbar Ampov OWSO provides services in 12 areas, including: Legalization, Civil Registration, Cadastral Affairs, Culture and Fine Arts, Education, Youth and Sports, Tourism, Construction, Industry Mining and energy, trade, health, public works and transport, and agriculture.
Ms. Ek Yani, Deputy Governor of Chbar Ampov District, said that the campaign was aimed at making people more aware of the cost of providing public services at the OWSO and avoiding the reliance on their traffickers. Take prices beyond this. In this leaflet, there is also the telephone number of the OWSO of the district so that people can contact directly if they do not understand or want to know something.
Ms. Ek Yani stated that the Chbar Ampov District Administration will strive to implement the public administration reform of the Royal Government of Cambodia to make the public administration more responsive, effective and trustworthy, and to promote public culture, will, ownership, loyalty, professional conscience of civil servants. To turn public administration into an effective public service provider and serve the people better.
