Visa launches QR code scanning for Visa Card payments in Cambodia
Once the mobile app (App) launches, you can use your mobile phone to scan the QR code to make a payment with Visa by transferring money from your account to the seller's account directly.
Payment via QR code scanning allows Visa cardholders to use their mobile phones to make purchases and pay bills without having to carry cash on hand. For merchants to accept payment methods by scanning QR codes, it means that they can access low-cost electronic payment service options using QR codes with their mobile phones.
All Visa card QR transactions will be processed globally through VisaNet, following Visa's high security and reliability standards for QR code payments. QR cash payments are currently being implemented in Indonesia, Vietnam, Thailand and India, and will soon be available in a number of markets in Southeast Asia. This was further confirmed by Ms. Monica.
"We are confident that Visa Card Payment Scanning will accelerate the transition from cash to electronic payments and improve the state of the financial system across the country," she added. "Up."
