(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) on the evening of December 20, 2018, thanked members of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) for exchanging good ideas in the committee meeting. The Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party for the past three days to seek benefits for the nation and the people.
Samdech Techo also wished his compatriots happiness and a happy reunion with their families.
It should be noted that the 41st Central Committee Meeting of the 5th Mandate of the Cambodian People's Party, which was held for 3 days at the Koh Pich Exhibition and Convention Center, closed at more than 6:00 pm on December 20, 2018.
The three-day conference at the Koh Pich Exhibition and Convention Center was chaired by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party, and was attended by more than 3,000 leaders of the Central Committee and non-Central Committee members.
At the end of the conference, the CPP presented 11 key outcomes to guide its implementation in the future. In this convention, the CPP, which has been in power for the last five terms, also added seven new permanent members, bringing the total to 376 permanent members and 865 members of the Central Committee.
