(China): Senior government officials from the Mekong-Lanchang Cooperation countries, including China, Laos, Cambodia, Myanmar, Thailand and Vietnam, met in Luang Prabang, Laos last week to discuss Agree on various ways to develop this subregion in a sustainable and cooperative manner.
The fourth meeting of the Foreign Ministers of the countries participating in the Mekong-Lanchang Cooperation reached an agreement on a number of areas that benefit all parties. These benefits include cooperation on high-quality production capacity and the construction of the Mekong-Lanchang Economic Cooperation Ring.
