(Pailin): Mrs. So Moniroth, Deputy Governor of Pailin Province, died on December 20, 2018 due to a traffic accident, while her son and Mrs. Pok Nady, Deputy Governor of Banteay Meanchey were also seriously injured in this horrific traffic accident.
According to Fresh News Agency, the accident happened in Chheu Neak village, Svay Chrum commune, Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province, after the three victims returned from Phnom Penh back to Pailin province.
Prior to the incident, the car of the Deputy Governor of Pailin Province, Mark Luxis, was traveling in the opposite direction from Phnom Penh to Pailin Province until it collided with two other vehicles, causing the death of the Deputy Governor. After being sent to Kampong Chhnang Provincial Hospital for treatment, all three vehicles were damaged on both sides.
It should be noted that the victims were Som Moniroth, 56, Deputy Governor of Pailin Province, Mrs. Mok Nady, 49 years old, Deputy Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, was seriously injured and the son of Deputy Governor of Pailin Province was also seriously injured.
