Third Outstanding Chinese-Khmer Mobile Film Tour Successfully Completed in Mondulkiri
(Mondulkiri): The third outstanding Chinese-Khmer mobile film tour, which arrived in Sen Monorom, Mondulkiri province and was screened in the courtyard near the Kouprey roundabout on the night of December 19, 2018. Great success due to the full participation and support of provincial leaders as well as municipal authorities, relevant departments and the participation of a large number of people, as well as about 1,300 students.
It should be noted that in 2018, as the Cambodian-Chinese leaders celebrate the 60th anniversary of diplomatic relations between the two countries, the "Best Chinese-Khmer Mobile Film Festival" has resumed its mission. In addition, in collaboration with the Chinese Embassy in the Kingdom of Cambodia, the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, the Ministry of Information, the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia and hosted by Cambodia-China Friendship Radio.
The 3rd China-Khmer Mobile Film Festival started its mission on December 5, 2018 with great success in some provinces such as Battambang, Siem Reap, Kampong Thom, Stung Treng, Ratanakkiri and Chong. The latter is Mondulkiri province and has traveled a total distance of more than 2,500 kilometers and a total of about 15,000 visitors.
On that occasion, Ms. Vin Sithou, Deputy Governor of Mondulkiri Province, who presided over the event, said that the "Outstanding Chinese-Khmer Mobile Film Tour" event has pushed for a change in the film culture of Cambodia-China and also made the people of the two countries know each other better and get to know each other more in depth.
At the same time, Mr. Feng Huy, Director General of Cambodia-China Friendship Radio, said that the 3rd China-Cambodia Mobile Screening Event 2018 is organized to exchange culture and strengthen cooperation between the two countries. Two to be stronger and more progressive.
Mr. Feng Huy also thanked the provincial administration, the authorities and the people in Mondulkiri for their support, cooperation and participation in such a large crowd, and the participation of the Cambodian people in the provinces as well as in Mondulkiri. This has really pushed the relationship between Cambodia and China closer and stronger day by day.
Ms. Trav Chhve, a 10th grade student of Hun Sen High School, Mondulkiri, who also came to see this Chinese-Khmer film, considered that the screening was very good. She said that both the image and the education and see the various aspects of China, including the culture and lifestyle of the Chinese and Cambodian people.
Lim Samnang, a 17-year-old who is watching with great enthusiasm, also said that the screening of this Chinese-Khmer film is very special because it provides value, education and entertainment to the people. As well as the people of Mondulkiri, this is also the first time that the people of Mondulkiri have seen such a large-scale film.
Ms. Chreu Chanry, an Indigenous People in Mondulkiri Province, expressed her excitement at the Cambodia-China Friendship Radio, which brought a beautiful Chinese-Khmer film to the people of Mondulkiri Province. Visited for free. She thanked for this significant event and requested that such a film be screened in the future.
