Police crack down on a massage parlor in Chamkarmon
(Phnom Penh): The police force of the Office of Anti-Human Trafficking and Protection of Minors cooperated with the local police in Chamkar Mon district to crack down on 99 massage parlors with embedded sex services for minors, arresting 6 people, including one female owner. Four victims and a cook.
In this operation, with the indication of Lt. Gen. Thet, Deputy Commissioner and Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner, and with the coordination of Mr. Kuch Kimlong, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court and under the direct command of Brigadier General Chan Kittikhom Deputy Commissioner for Anti-Trafficking in Persons and Juvenile Protection Plan of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police.
According to the Anti-Human Trafficking and Juvenile Protection Bureau, the 99 brand massage parlor is open from 9:00 am until late at night, with four young and old women waiting for guests to come for a massage. And kidney massage (masturbation with hands and mouth) for $ 15 to $ 20 per session.
After the operation, the police arrested 6 people, including 4 female victims (a minor). A female's owner was taken to the Anti-Trafficking and Juvenile Protection Office for further questioning. This is according to additional information from the authorities.
It should also be noted that the four women were handed over by the police to a social organization for education and a cook was sent back to her home by the police because they were not involved.
