At the General Assembly to celebrate the 40th anniversary of the implementation of China's reform and opening-up policy, held on December 18, Xi Jinping, Secretary-General of the CPC Central Committee, President of the People's Republic of China and Chairman of the Committee China's central military has delivered a keynote address.
He summed up the history, achievements, meanings and experiences that China has gained over the past 40 years after embarking on comprehensive reform and opening-up through 10 practical areas: theory, concept, building, economy, politics, democracy. Cultural development, improvement of people's lives, protection of the environment, defense and modernization of the army, peaceful national reunification, peaceful diplomacy and party building.
There is no doubt that these nine valuable experiences should be the "secret code of success" of China's reform and opening-up, which is of great interest to the international community. Developing countries can learn from China's experience in resolving the relationship between development reform and stability.
After 40 years, China's reform and opening-up is now at a historic new beginning, as the 19th Congress of the Communist Party of China (CPC) has set higher goals for China's socio-economic development. One way. On the other hand, protectionism and unilateralism have increased on a global scale, undermining the process of economic globalization.
The Chinese people are well aware that the impetus for reform and development depends on trust and perseverance. In 40 years or more in the future, China will take practical steps to prove that China's innovative, open, environmental and trustworthy China will surely bring greater greatness to the world. .
