Cambodia's first biomedical laboratory receives international standard certification
(Phnom Penh): Since 2012, the Biomedical Laboratory of the Institut Pasteur in Cambodia has been involved in the continuous improvement of quality in line with the requirements of the international standard NF EN ISO 15189: 2012 required for biomedical laboratories in France. .
The biomedical laboratory implements a quality assurance principle in the context of diagnostic assessment and treatment assistance missions with the following objectives:
* Ensure the quality of the requested analytical tests, can provide the most reliable and accurate results possible * Provide timely results, especially in emergencies * Provide frequent advice on Needs and all the time
Following an audit in May 2018, the French Accreditation Committee concluded that the biomedical laboratory met all the requirements of the standard and decided to provide accreditation to a specific scope of the clinic. Biology, such as biochemistry, hematology, serum, bacterial pathology, and TB diagnosis with GenXpert.
In addition, the quality certification in accordance with the international standard ISO 15189 demonstrates the technical capabilities of the laboratory and the proper operation in this laboratory under an appropriate management system.
The Biomedical Laboratory of the Institut Pasteur du Cambodge is the first laboratory in Cambodia to be ISO 15189 certified and is a clear proof of our quality assurance policy to maximize the benefits to our clients and prescribers.
The biomedical laboratory is established with the commitment of finding the best way to provide quality services, providing reliable and timely results to its patients (Cambodians, foreigners and tourists) for use in Diagnose effectively, secretly and with the right advice. Information Minister Supports Ministry of Cult to Introduce Livestock to Slaughterhouses
