(Phnom Penh): The fourth phase of the Flood Prevention and Drainage Improvement Project, a Japanese-funded project through the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA), amounted to approximately US $ 30 million. Groundwater storage and construction of pumping station and installation of automatic mechanical bar to collect garbage in front of the drainage road of the pumping station etc. have started.
This was revealed during the first meeting of the flood prevention and improvement project in Phnom Penh in the morning of December 19, 2018 at the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh.
Mr. Sam Piseth, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh, said that the fourth phase of the project to prevent flood and improve the drainage system in Phnom Penh, a total of about 30 million US dollars, a grant from the Government of Japan through Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA).
This project will implement the following works: 1- Install the sewerage network in Toul Kork district with a length of 8.2 km, 2- Install the sewerage network in Daun Penh district with a length of 4.4 km, 3-Build a reservoir Underground and construction of pumping station in the park in front of the Council for the Development of Cambodia; 2 mobile water units.
Regarding the above project, Mr. Met Meas Pheakdey, Spokesman of Phnom Penh Capital Administration, also said that the fourth phase of the project to prevent flood and improve the drainage system focused on important work. Some such as water liberation work.
The water distribution work is divided into two parts, the main purpose or the main benefit is to get in the north of Wat Phnom in the area along the road and road 147, from Wat Phnom to the roundabout Kouch Kanong area of about 70 The hectare will be designed and considered as a pumping station, which is the fifth pumping station along the riverfront, located in front of the Council for Economic Development (CDC).
The pumping station will provide an underground reservoir with a capacity of 6,000 cubic meters before pumping rainwater from the reservoir into the river.
In addition to the pumping station, an automatic garbage collection machine will be installed, which is part of the fourth phase of the project, and will be installed at all four riverside stations: the pumping station. Old Market, Preah Klong Station, Central Market Station and Chaktomuk Station, which have been under construction since the second phase of the project.
Automatically add garbage collection equipment in all 4 stations on this 4th phase project. Benefits of Facilitation of Water in the Toul Kork Area Located in Sangkat Boeung Kak I, Sangkat Boeung Kak II.
The project will include the installation of a sewerage system in the range of 2 meters to 2.50 meters, a distance of about 7 kilometers and the installation of 1.5 kilometers of box drainage.
(Phnom Penh): After the overthrow of the Khmer Rouge regime in 1979, Khmer Rouge leaders, along with Khmer Rouge soldiers, fled into hiding and settled along the Thai-Cambodian border and in areas such as Pailin, Banteay Meanchey, and Battambang. And churches. Especially on the ridge of Dangrek mountain in Anlong Veng district, Oddar Meanchey province, was the last stronghold of the Khmer Rouge.
After struggling to re-occupy Cambodian territory for nearly 20 years, they gradually surrendered to the Royal Government of Cambodia. The last Khmer Rouge leaders and troops in Anlong Veng district surrendered in 1998, when Cambodia completely closed the pages of the war after nearly 40 years.
Why did the Khmer Rouge leaders and soldiers in Anlong Veng and other areas surrender to the Royal Government?
(Phnom Penh): There was a horrific traffic accident between a tuk tuk truck with one wheel broken and the steering wheel collided with a Samsung truck carrying workers traveling in different directions, resulting in one death and one death. Another was seriously injured. The seriously injured were taken to hospital.
This horrific traffic accident happened at 9:30 AM on December 20, 2018, in front of Wat Kampeng along the concrete road in Sangkat Prey Sar, Khan Dangkor, Phnom Penh.
The perpetrator was named Hun Nget Mean, male, 35 years old, driving a truck carrying workers, his hometown is Preah Sdach District, Prey Veng Province. The dead and seriously injured have not been identified.
Sources from the scene said that before the incident, they saw a tuk-tuk transporting steel into a city. At that moment, I saw a tuk-tuk carrying steel coming out of the city, traveling in a south-to-north direction, riding in the opposite direction with a Samsung truck carrying workers.
Suddenly, the tuk-tuk broke the left wheel and the steering wheel collided with a fully loaded Samsung car, then the car hit the steering wheel and hit another motorcycle. After the incident, the owner of the car tried to escape, but was arrested by nearby residents and handed over to local authorities. This is according to a source from the scene.
The Gaia 17bpi satellite is undergoing a phase of change and growth at a rapid rate, which is rare for scientists to be able to observe. The star is estimated to be only a few million years old, the youngest age for a star in a galaxy, but it is also rapidly increasing in mass.
When stars go through such intense evolutionary stages, they are usually difficult to spot because they are often surrounded by clouds and large space dust. Therefore, the opportunity to observe the stars at a time when they are evolving is a special thing for scientists because only a small number of such events are recorded.
