Royal Government Appoints New Member of National Land Dispute Resolution Authority
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia on December 13 recently decided to appoint a new composition of the National Authority for Land Dispute Resolution, chaired by Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction.
The new composition of the Land Dispute Resolution Authority consists of Senior Minister Khun Haing as Permanent Deputy Chairman and 20 other members, namely the Minister, Secretary of State, Secretary-General from 18 relevant ministries and institutions. The capital-provincial governor is also a member of the authority to resolve land disputes.
In addition to the above leadership, the Royal Government has also appointed 25 other members as Secretary-General, Deputy Secretary-General and members of the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Land Dispute Resolution.
Please be informed that the National Land Dispute Resolution Authority is an authority established by Royal Decree No. NS / RKOT / 0206/097 dated 26 February 2006. The National Land Dispute Resolution Authority was established to minimize and completely eliminate land disputes.
