Kratie Provincial Department of Land Management Holds a Training Course on Land Use Planning Procedures in 2 Communes
(Kratie): Kratie Provincial Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs conducted a 5-day training course on land use planning procedures at two commune / sangkat levels: O'Kreang Commune, Sambo District and Chroy Banteay Commune, Prek Prosop District, Kratie Province. Under the auspices of the Belgian government through the Global Fund for the Conservation of Natural Resources in Cambodia (WWF-Cambodia).
The opening ceremony of the training course on the morning of December 19, 2018 was presided over by Dr. Kao Madeleine, Director of the Provincial Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs, with the participation of the Governor, Deputy District Governor, District Land Office, Department Involved as well as commune chiefs, village chiefs, elders of O'Kreang commune and Chroy Banteay commune.
Dr. Kao Madeleine said that in achieving the goals of economic development, poverty reduction and good governance, the Royal Government will focus its efforts on land work in three areas, including: first, strengthening the security of land tenure; : Organize land and manage natural resources equitably and sustainably; Third, implement equitable distribution.
Dr. continued that the Royal Government of the second mandate established the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction and the Land Policy Council in order to ensure that the three directions of this land work are coordinated by all institutions and People involved in land use.
Afterwards, Mr. Chan Kong, Deputy Director of the Provincial Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs in charge of the Office of Land Management and Urban Planning, taught the participants in this training and 14 lessons to make all participants understand the procedure. Develop land use and management plans and tactical rules for implementing activities.
Dr. Kao Madeleine added that land use planning is a planning process that starts from the village, with villagers and other stakeholders involved in demarcating the village boundaries and using, protecting and subdividing all areas. All the water surface in its village.
He added that the process will determine the current status of real estate (land) and make decisions on future land tenure and use, and in the process of participating in land use planning, villagers and other stakeholders will be assisted. By coordinating neutrality at the provincial-district level and commune-sangkat representatives. Director of Phnom Penh Health Department: Drinking sweet drinks causes us many diseases
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Ngy Mean Heng, Director of the Phnom Penh Municipal Health Department, said that drinking sweet drinks causes us many diseases. He said that in Cambodia, as well as in the whole world, there are many cases of non-communicable diseases, which is a concern of public health experts.
This statement was made by the doctor during the seminar on "Maintaining knowledge on reducing sweet drinks" in Phnom Penh on December 19, 2018, which was attended by participants from Sangkat councils, schools, public and private health centers. Located in Toul Kork and Daun Penh districts, a total of 116 people.
At the same time, Ms. Sak Chendary, Deputy Director of Phnom Penh Capital Administration, stated that the Phnom Penh Municipal Welfare Committee pays high attention to the implementation of Phnom Penh Capital Welfare by integrating awareness on reducing the consumption of sweet drinks through the exhibition. Display on billboards on the boulevard, educational video broadcasts on television and some social media.
"This is a collaboration between the Phnom Penh Capital Administration, the National Center for Health Promotion and the Ministry of Health, and this is one of the activities of the partnership for urban well-being, which is a global network of cities working to reduce diseases," she said. Non-infectious and non-infectious. "Especially under the wise and skillful leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, we have made rapid growth and achievement in all areas."
The Deputy Director of Administration also stated that the health sector on health issues is the main work that is given high attention to reduce the risk of various non-communicable diseases and injuries, with the school has a place for students. Wash your hands thoroughly to avoid infections, and consuming too many sugary drinks can cause health problems.
