Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone Camcontrol Branch Found Defective Goods for Sale at Marts in Sen Sok District, Confiscated and Burned
(Phnom Penh): Camcontrol Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone Branch on December 19, 2018 cooperated with the Department of Commerce to continue to promote the quality of food safety by inspecting the pre-packaged goods at some markets in Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh. .
According to the Camcontrol Officer of Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone, some of the goods were found to be defective beyond the expiration date and were confiscated by the branch and requested to be demolished at a later date.
According to CamControl officials, the goods included 10.37 kilograms of peanut butter, Korean noodles, Korean noodles, canned noodles, Korean noodles, and canned beer.
During the inspection of the above marts, CamControl officers also instructed the owners of the marts on how to properly display the products in accordance with each type of goods to avoid bacterial contamination and to All mart owners help to check the goods themselves for the expiration date of the goods and also prohibit the display of goods that have expired.
