In the Chinese language competition "Jiangsu Award", 18 Cambodian students reached the finals on the same day.
Since 2011, the Chinese proficiency competition "Jiangsu Award" has been held more than 10 times in Japan, USA, UK, Australia and so on. 2017 is the first year in collaboration with the Confucius Institute of the Royal Academy of Cambodia to organize on the territory of Cambodia.
At this point, Mr. Yong Pov emphasized that good relations between Cambodia and China appear at all times in terms of history, politics, economy, society and nature.
Mr. Yong Pov stated that the Chinese language competition "Jiangsu Award" is suitable for the needs of the exchange between Cambodia and China, and has provided more opportunities to learn Chinese in the Kingdom of Cambodia as well as the world. Round. He said that the students are successors who are energetic, new jobs and knowledge will be the new driving force to connect the hearts of the people, promote the progress of relations between the two countries.
In that, Mr. Yong Pov hopes that all candidates should adhere to the principle of "Friendship 1, Match 2" to show their true ability, learn from each other to strengthen their abilities.
Meanwhile, Ms. Vuth Sopheakna, Director of the Cambodian side of the Confucius Institute at the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that the first "Jiangsu Award" Chinese language competition was held in Cambodia in 2017 in collaboration with the Confucius Institute. Royal Academy of Cambodia.
