Koh Kong Provincial Department of Social Affairs Celebrates 36th Anniversary of International Day of Persons with Disabilities and 20th Anniversary of Cambodian Day of Persons with Disabilities
(Koh Kong): The Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation of Koh Kong Province on December 19, 2018 organized the 36th Anniversary of International Day of Persons with Disabilities and the 20th Anniversary of Cambodia Day of Persons with Disabilities on December 3, 2018 under the chairmanship. "Promoting the Rights of Persons with Disabilities, Ensuring Environment and Equality."
Kong Roeung, Director of the Provincial Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, said that the celebration of the 20th Cambodia Day of Persons with Disabilities and the 36th Anniversary of the International Day of Persons with Disabilities on December 3, 2018 is one of the most important factors in Promoting the rights of people with disabilities to gather support and contribute to the integration of people with disabilities in social development.
In that, the Royal Government has paid high attention to the issue of disability and rehabilitation of workers in terms of programs, policies and strategies to meet the needs of people with disabilities, because in the past, Cambodia has achieved some work in the field of disability. This is according to Mr. Kong Roeung.
Mr. Phay Thun Plam Keson, Acting Governor of Koh Kong Province, read the full text of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia to people with disabilities, which has a deep meaning.
He added that the provincial Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation has provided services to people with disabilities in the community and has co-founded a number of self-help groups. The current government has taken great care of the disabled.
Chinese investors open 2018 land construction forum in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): To show the potential for development in the field of land construction in Cambodia, Chinese investors have opened the 2018 International Concierge Business Summit on Building Construction with the participation of more than 50 representatives of Chinese companies and stakeholders. More on December 18, 2018.
Speaking at the forum, Mr. Zhong Xingming, Secretary-General of the Concerned Business Development Forum on Land Construction 2018, said that there are currently about 100,000 Chinese in Cambodia and are working in Cambodia. .
Mr. Zhong Xingming added that the large number of Chinese people coming to Cambodia can prove that the relations between China and Cambodia are close and Cambodia is a friendly country.
He said that the Cambodian economy has grown by about 7% every year in a row, which puts Cambodia in the sixth place, which is assessed by the World Bank as a new economic development, and with ASEAN countries. Develop fast.
He said that the amount of investment from foreign companies is up to 22 billion dollars, of which companies have invested in Cambodia up to 44% of all investments. According to this figure, it is seen that the investment of Chinese investors has many investment opportunities in Cambodia as well as high potential.
He said that this investment, Chinese investors have developed in the construction sector, the federation has mobilized enterprises working in the construction sector to invest in Cambodia in construction and other businesses in accordance with the policy of "one road. One ”as well.
At the same time, Mr. HER Chentha, Deputy Secretary General of the National Land Management Committee and Deputy Director General of the General Department of Housing, said that Cambodia has great potential for investment for investors. He also pointed out that if you want to start investing in Cambodia, investors must first apply to the Council for the Development of Cambodia. The ring of Saturn (Ring) is melting faster than expected, according to NASA just announced hot!
3-star General Di Vichea: Private security contributes to maintaining security, safety, order, wishing the state and investors, currently has more than 26,000 security agents
(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. Dy Vichea, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police and Director of the Central Security Department, this morning, December 19, 2018, opened a training course on the management of private security agencies and bank security and handed over a car. Shanghai Security Industry Association.
The ceremony was also attended by Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey, Director of the Private Security Management Department and a representative of the Embassy of the People's Republic of China in Cambodia, and the Executive Vice President of the Shanghai Security Industry Association, as well as several national police officers.
Lt. Gen. Di Vichea welcomed the Shanghai Security Industry Association for presenting security management and sharing experiences with National Police officers of Siem Reap, Sihanoukville Provincial Police and the leadership of the Security Management Department. Private to get more new experience on private security management.
According to General Di Vichea, due to the efforts of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia and the close solidarity between Cambodia and China, Cambodia has now expanded in all areas, especially construction development. Many high-rise buildings in the presence of Chinese investors.
Meanwhile, the private security sector has also contributed to maintaining security, safety and order for the people as well as investors and national and international tourists.
On behalf of the General Commission of the National Police as well as the Department of Private Security Management, Lt. Gen. Di Vichea thanked the Shanghai Security Industry Association for donating a vehicle to the Department of Private Security Management to assist in the management of private security in contributing to care. Maintain the security, safety and public order of Cambodia.
At the same time, Deputy Commissioner Di Vichea requested the Shanghai Security Industry Association to continue to train more trainers for the officers of the Private Security Management Department.
Please be informed that there are currently 26,565 private security agents nationwide (2,381 females), of which a total of 239 private security providers and enterprises recruiting private security agents (non-private security services) are: 1,867 institutions.
