BEIJING: Chinese President Xi Jinping has warned that no one can come to command China's economic development trajectory as the Communist Party of China (CPC) celebrates the 40th anniversary of its reform and opening-up policy. Its history in the face of tense pressure with the United States. This is according to a quote from the Bangkok Post on Tuesday evening, December 18, 2018.
Speaking at the Great Hall of the People in front of several Chinese Communist Party officials, Xi vowed to continue to move forward with China's economic reform principles, but made it clear that Beijing will not give up. A system ruled by a single party or under absolute command from another country.
Without referring specifically to the United States, Xi Jinping said China does not pose a threat to any country, but he clearly warned that China would not remain silent. No. Xi Jinping's remarks refer to the actions of the United States and some US allies that have been working together to shake up China's economy through various methods, as has happened in the past.
