Samdech Techo Hun Sen issues sub-decree to increase the salary of contracted officials from 600,000 Riels to 650,000 Riels
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on December 18, 2018, issued Sub-Decree No. 172 on raising the salaries of contracted officials in 2019.
This new sub-decree decided to increase the monthly salary of contracted officials from 600,000 Riels to 650,000 Riels, which will be implemented from January 1, 2019 onwards. The Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia issues a sub-decree to increase the unit of basic salary index for civil servants from January 1, 2019 onwards
(Phnom Penh): The Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on December 18, issued Sub-Decree No. 173 on the revision of the unit price of the basic salary index of civil servants for 2019.
This sub-decree decides to change the unit of the basic salary index from 2130 Riels to 2340 Riels per index, which will be implemented from January 1, 2019 onwards.
Deputy Director General of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia: Investing in the securities market is a risk-free investment with high potential for business expansion
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chhun Sambath, Deputy Director General of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, spoke positively about investing in the securities sector, stating that investing in this sector is a risk-free investment, the risk factor is close to zero percent. Not only that, there is a high potential for business expansion as well.
Mr. Chhun Sambath made this remark at a seminar for banking and microfinance institutions under the theme "Expansion of business potential through the securities market" and was attended by many members of the public, including Mr. HA Jong Weon, Deputy General Director of Cambodia Securities Exchange.
This workshop is designed to spread awareness of the securities sector to banking and microfinance institutions in Cambodia, as well as in line with the goal of attracting financial institutions to be active in the securities sector.
Mr. Chhun Sambath explained in detail about investing in the securities sector to the public. He said that the expansion of business through the Cambodian stock market means that microfinance can come to capital in this securities market, because this market can now get capital at a low price, so they can come to capital. By issuing and selling cheap bonds.
He added that the other is not only able to raise capital, but can also invest in the stock market. Obviously, if you invest in lending, the risk factor is higher non-return, but if you invest with confidence, you will invest in the securities sector by buying bonds with a risk ratio of almost zero.
Please note that this workshop focuses on the details of the various types of business that financial institutions may have in the securities sector, with introduction to the terms and procedures of the issuance of shares and bonds.
