CamControl confiscated more than 200 kilograms of defective goods from Boeung Kantout market traders in Krakor district, Pursat province and immediately burned them.
(Pursat): Officials of Camcontrol Branch in Pursat Province, this morning, December 18, 2018, in cooperation with the officials of the Department of Commerce and the Market Commission, continued to inspect the goods displayed at Boeung Kantout Market in O'Anchanh Village, Boeung Kantuot Commune. Krakor District, Pursat Province.
Mr. Toch Chao Koy, Head of Camcontrol Branch in Pursat Province, said that during the inspection, the technical officers did a preliminary analysis to find banned chemicals on the food that the vendors put up for sale, and as a result, the professional officers did not find any banned chemicals. However, the team found defective goods beyond the expiration date, and confiscated 6 items, totaling 229 kilograms, and immediately destroyed them in front of the authorities.
On the afternoon of December 18, 2018, CamControl Pursat Branch, in cooperation with the Department of Commerce and local authorities, continued to disseminate food safety education and practice at Boeung Kantuot Primary School in O'Anchanh Village, Boeung Kantuot Commune.
