Mr. Kong Vuthy further stated that after the preliminary inspection, his team found jelly injected into the shrimp belly to increase the weight of nearly 20 kilograms that traders are selling in Doeum Kor market and 18 kilograms of banned chemicals in fertilizer. The work was decided to be demolished.
Separately, traders were called by his officials to make contracts. However, Mr. Kong Vuthy continued to advise all vendors to sell products in accordance with the technical specifications by distinguishing between appliances that contain toxic substances and food, ban the display of products, beverages, sun exposure and placement. Sell out-of-date products as well.
He also called on traders, wholesalers, wholesalers, retailers, manufacturers, importers and distributors to have a clear source before selling and stop adding chemicals to food products that harm consumers' health.
