CamControl officers continue to inspect stations, some fuel depots in Chbar Ampov district, a station was suspended after selling counterfeit
(Phnom Penh): The fuel inspection team of the General Department of CamControl of the Ministry of Commerce, through the mobile fuel laboratory vehicle led by Mr. Nguon Somlyvong, Deputy Director of the Department, on December 18, 2018, inspected the quantity and quality of fuel. At some stations and depots in Chbar Ampov district, Phnom Penh.
The operation was carried out in collaboration with Phnom Penh CamControl and Laboratory staff in order to protect the economic interests of consumers, to protect the machinery of all types of vehicles and to protect the environment arising from improper fuel consumption and to Prevent fraud.
Mr. Nguon Somlyvong stated that the quality and quantity control is based on on-site monitoring equipment, such as specific calibration tanks for measuring the amount of oil fired from the counter in different sizes, with a capacity of 5 liters, 10 liters and 20 liters. The octon and cetan indexes are used in mobile laboratory vehicles.
According to the deputy director of the department, as a result of the inspection of the quality and quantity of fuel of two depots, one depot complied with the quality and measurement, and the other depot Chhoukrath was found to be non-compliant. Officials from the General Department of CamControl decided to suspend the distribution process to deal with the procedure. As for the retail price of both depots, the locations have complied with the notification of the Ministry of Commerce.
All vehicle users must consider before choosing a gas station / depot, a company that trusts the use of new equipment, sells regular gasoline or super good quality diesel and diesel, and always check the counter number from zero before Inject.
