Vendors slaughtering pigs and cattle in the Veal Yon market protested, demanding three main points:
* First: I want the manager to stop taking the price of a pig and a cow is not less than 2,000 riel * Second: I want to change the manager of the kiln, wanting to replace the new one because the current manager uses the word Despise the traders * Third: want the veterinarian to pay only 1,000 riel, as in the past, because now it costs 1,500 riel per head.
Through this coordination, the provincial administration has decided on the following principles: one cow costs 3,500 riels and one pig costs 1,500 riels, and this pricing will be implemented from March 22, 2018 until Term ends December 31, 2019.
At the same time, the provincial administration also decided that all slaughter of animals must go to the slaughterhouse to gather at the same place, not to take place outside the slaughterhouse.
After receiving the letter of request, the provincial administration also organized a working group with relevant departments and units and invited the traders to mediate four times and issued a letter to implement, but so far the traders refused to follow the letter of the administration. No province. Please also note that through the invitation to the meeting to solve the problem 4 times ago, the traders demanded no limit.
