Free medical check-ups and medicine have become a joy for Samrong residents in Oddar Meanchey. Among them, a woman named Chea Lida, among other citizens, expressed her happiness as never before. Ms. Lida has gastritis and every day this pain in the abdomen, thanks to Mr. Hun Many's team of volunteer doctors came to treat her as well as other villagers.
Another resident, Sam Piseth, who has a nasal allergy, said: "I feel happy when they come down to check and give me free medicine, it saves me money."
Another elderly man, Pov Than, who had pneumonia, said he was overjoyed when a team of volunteer doctors arrived in his village and Treatment is free.
He said that the arrival of the doctors has saved him a lot of time and money. He also thanked Mr. Hun Many for sending a team of volunteer doctors to his village.
In addition to expressing happiness, people have asked Mr. Hun Many's team of volunteer doctors to visit people to reduce the cost and get an effective treatment.
At the same time, Mr. Leang Phaly, Chief of Volunteer Doctors, Mr. HUN Many also called on all residents in Samrong City, Oddar Meanchey Province to maintain good health because this December is the rainy season. People are more susceptible to various diseases, especially colds, which are the most easily transmitted diseases.
