Remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen Inaugurating the Lower Sesan 2 Hydropower Plant, the Highest Power Hydropower Plant in Cambodia
(Stung Treng): After 11 years of construction, the Lower Sesan 2 hydropower project, a joint venture between Chinese, Cambodian and Vietnamese companies, provides nearly 2 million kilowatt-hours of electricity per year, will be officially launched on the 17th. This December 2018.
The inauguration ceremony of the largest hydropower plant in Cambodia was presided over by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen starts his speech on the occasion of the inauguration of the Lower Sesan 2 Hydropower Plant this morning, December 17, 2018,
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he was very happy to preside over the inauguration of the Lower Sesan 2 hydropower plant, which is the largest power producer in Cambodia and the seventh hydropower plant that he inaugurated.
* Samdech Techo emphasized that Samdech is very proud of the achievements of the Lower Sesan 2 hydropower plant, which is a joint venture between China, Cambodia and Vietnam, and is the first hydropower invested by a Cambodian investor, Duke Kith Meng.
* Samdech Techo Prime Minister emphasized that the construction of Lower Sesan 2 hydropower is not a risky investment without forethought.
* Samdech Techo stated that this hydropower is an important contribution to the implementation of Samdech's policy that has been set since 1987: water, roads, electricity and people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Lower Sesan 2 hydropower is not used to supply energy in Stung Treng province, but also to other provinces.
* The Prime Minister added that the construction of hydropower here was supported by the majority of the people, but few people opposed it through foreign incitement.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen also reminded of the past of Cambodia after the liberation from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot without electricity like today, people have to use electric lights and oil lamps.
* Samdech Techo stated that the Lower Sesan 2 hydropower plant, which produces up to 400 megawatts of electricity, has solved many problems for the development of the country, not only the livelihood of the people, but also to supply to agriculture and industry, as well as The service sector as well.
* Samdech Techo stated that the construction of hydropower must continue to make more efforts to extract energy, not just the end of Sesan 2 hydropower. Samdech Techo stated that without efforts to develop hydropower, Cambodia may face a shortage of electricity in 2020.
* The Prime Minister urged the Electricity Authority to continue its efforts to connect more electricity to meet the needs of the people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that during his upcoming visit to China, there will be talks focusing on budget loans for the electricity grid in Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that for schools, hospitals, health centers, the price of electricity will go down to 610 riels in 2019 and 2020.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen commended all stakeholders for their joint efforts until the achievement of the Lower Sesan 2 hydropower project.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the past, provincial officials used various excuses, such as ferries not to cross security issues that could be caused by the Khmer Rouge, in order to avoid attending meetings. But now the roads and bridges are connected, the Khmer Rouge problem is no more, so there is no more excuse.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that during the global economic crisis, all development projects in Cambodia supported by the Chinese government were not suspended. This position shows that the Chinese government has strongly supported the development of Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo ordered the Stung Treng provincial authorities to pay attention and monitor the people who have to move from the dam site to the new place.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen also thanked the people of Stung Treng and throughout the country for voting for the CPP. Samdech Techo stated that the people went to the polls to show their support for the democratic process in Cambodia and was a political failure to win at home, and that going to the polls was a contribution to the protection of peace.
Before concluding his speech, Samdech Techo stated that tomorrow the CPP will open its three-day General Assembly. The conference will discuss issues that need to be addressed in the face of people's trust and move the country from a low-middle-income country to a high-middle-income country by 2030 and a high-income country by 2030. 2050.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reaffirmed that Samdech will be the Prime Minister for another 10 years until the opposition is destroyed.
