Demonstrations and crackdowns in Brussels over UN immigration agreement
(Brussels): Thousands of protesters clashed with Belgian police during a march against the United Nations Global Migration Agreement in Brussels on Sunday. This was quoted from the Chinese news agency Xinhua in the morning of Monday, December 17, 2018.
The demonstration was aimed at opposing the UN Convention on the Safeguarding and Safeguarding of the United Nations, which was signed in the early days of Marrakech, Morocco. Last week.
Police used tear gas and water cannons as clashes erupted near the EU headquarters. The total number of protesters was reported to be around 5,500, including more than 1,000 who marched peacefully to show support for the agreement. The Brussels Prosecutor's Office said 100 people had been arrested.
In July, 169 UN member states agreed on a global agreement on immigration, signed by 164 countries in Marrakech last week, while the United States and some European countries did not. Agree to officially sign the approval.
