(Phnom Penh): Hungarian Minister of Foreign Affairs and Trade Peter Ziaato has promised Cambodian Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation Prak Sokhon that Hungary will urge the European Union to continue providing financial assistance to Cambodia to help address development challenges.
The Hungarian Foreign Minister made the promise during a meeting between him and Prak Sokhon on the occasion of Prak Sokhon's two-day official visit from December 11 to 12, 2018 in the country. Hungary.
With regard to international cooperation, the two Foreign Ministers agreed to support each other in the UN system.
