Hungary made the remarks during a meeting between Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation Prak Sokhon and Hungarian Minister of Foreign Affairs and Trade Peter Ziarto during his official visit to Hungary on the 11th. Until December 12, 2018.
"To further strengthen the overall relationship between the two countries, Hungary will open a diplomatic representative office in Phnom Penh on January 2, 2019," according to a press release from the visit. Face. In addition, Hungary welcomed the proposal to appoint an honorary Cambodian consul in Budapest.
The two foreign ministers signed two memorandums of understanding to boost cooperation in tourism and diplomatic institutes between the two countries and agreed to work together to facilitate exchanges. A visit to the level of the Prime Minister in the near future.
At the same time, the two Foreign Ministers had fruitful discussions, during which the Hungarian Foreign Minister reaffirmed Hungary's position not to interfere in Cambodia's internal affairs and to respect the decisions of the Cambodian people regarding Cambodia's recent election.
The Deputy Prime Minister also thanked Hungary for its valuable and timely assistance and support to Cambodia in the most difficult circumstances after Cambodia was liberated from the Khmer Rouge regime, and for Hungary's contribution to the operation. Keep the peace under the auspices of the United Nations Transitional Authority in Cambodia (UNTAC). This is according to the press release.
According to the statement, this is the second meeting between the two foreign ministers in less than three months in 2019, which underscores the two ministers' mutual commitment to establish a dialogue. Regularly on bilateral and international agendas.
In addition, the two Foreign Ministers expressed satisfaction with the growing development of relations between the two countries in recent years, which was reflected in regular consultations, exchanges of high-level visits. From the executive and legislature, as well as business forums.
