Samdech Techo Hun Sen warned that politicians should not use espionage and claim that those who use espionage are stupid.
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia also emphasized the need to protect the coast, protect the forest, protect the natural environment and speed up the construction of wastewater treatment plants, first of all in Sihanoukville.
The order of Samdech Techo Hun Sen was made on the night of December 15, 2018 on the occasion of Samdech and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to open the 7th Sea Festival Round 2 under the theme "Clean Beach "People of Romney" accompanied by the slogan "Ecotourism for green growth and sustainable development" in Koh Kong province.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "This is the point where HE Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara must continue to work with HE Thong Khon to do this work with the provinces involved."
Samdech Techo Prime Minister continued, "I have received a report from HE Chea Sophara about the additional capital for drainage in Sihanoukville to try to promote the implementation of this project, but I think such a project is only temporary. "But we need to do bigger projects to ensure that all wastewater is not discharged into the sea in the future."
In addition, Samdech Techo Prime Minister also stressed the need to maintain the green sea and the reputation of the stars in the southwest and encourage the development of ecotourism like Dara Sakor without deforestation and ecotourism is not required. There should be deforestation, but it has benefited from tourism more than agriculture and forest protection.
Please be informed that four wastewater treatment plants will be built along the coast in Sihanoukville to avoid the discharge of wastewater into the sea. There are 4 wastewater treatment bases, 1: at Ekareach Beach, 2: at Ochro, Sokha Company, 3: at O Sam Ath, and 4: at Ochheuteal beach, and 919 meters long drainage system.
Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Chairman of the National Committee for Coastal Management and Development of Cambodia, confirmed that the National Committee for Coastal Management and Development of Cambodia had visited and analyzed the site directly, dealing with the impact with stakeholders and designing the station network. Drainage system and 1 meter concrete drain and detailed technical documentation to ensure proper and smooth implementation.
The final order of Samdech Techo Hun Sen was made while Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit officially opened the 7th Sea Festival in Koh Kong province on the night of December 15, 2018.
