Key remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of the official opening of the 7th Sea Festival in Koh Kong Province
The second round of the 7th Sea Festival in Koh Kong Province this year was held under the theme "Clean Beach, Citizen Resort" accompanied by the slogan "Ecotourism for green growth and sustainable development".
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech and his wife were very happy to participate in the opening of the 7th Sea Festival in Koh Kong Province.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the participation in the Sea Festival is a mechanism to monitor the progress of the province that hosts the Sea Festival and as a reminder to those responsible at all levels, especially at the local level.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that the Sea Festival is also a show and increase solidarity and attract people in all provinces to visit the Sea Festival. Obviously, in this festival, not only the people of Koh Kong province, there are people from other provinces until there is a lack of accommodation.
* The Prime Minister stated that this Sea Festival is also an opportunity to join the leaders of the most beautiful beach club together with other member countries to send a delegation to participate.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the Sea Festival Organizing Committee for its efforts to organize this festival well. Samdech Techo said that today is really happy that Koh Kong province, which is remote and isolated in the past, has attracted many companies to this province on the occasion of the Sea Festival.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen commended Mr. Thong Khon for successfully cooperating with local authorities to organize the Sea Festival.
* The Prime Minister also commended Senior Minister Sun Chanthol and the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) Engineering Corps for their efforts to repair National Road 48 in time for the Sea Festival.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen confirmed that in the future will organize the annual international professional cycling.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Koh Kong province has suffered from the flames of war and the political crisis, which is a tragedy. Samdech Techo confirmed that Samdech took the chest to protect and liberate Koh Kong province. Samdech Techo stated that he did not want the people of Koh Kong to be as sad as in the past.
* Samdech Prime Minister said that Koh Kong province has a lot of resources, in fact, many provinces are using electricity from Koh Kong province.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Ministry of Industry, Mines and Energy had proposed a $ 22 billion investment in titanium in Koh Kong province's Chi Phat district. But to get titanium, it takes about 20,000 hectares of forest as a habitat for wildlife and other impacts, especially landslides. Because of this, Samdech decided not to invest in the exploration of titanium.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen added that the promotion of investment in titanium exploration was mentioned again, but was again rejected by Samdech. Samdech Techo stated that Samdech left the younger generation to consider lest they have a way to get titanium without destroying the forest and dumping it into the sea.
* Samdech Techo Prime Minister stated that Koh Kong province is rich in ecotourism, so how to connect tourism with services and industry.
* Samdech Techo stated that agriculture last year accounted for about 25 percent of national economic income, but now the remaining rate of 23.5 percent, industry last year 30 percent, but now up to 32.4 percent, in addition to the service sector and sector. Other.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen has about 800,000 tourists visiting the 440-kilometer coastal area stretching from the Thai-Vietnamese border.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed the expectation that Koh Kong could become the most visited coastal province or the second largest after the Darasakor Development Zone was completed, including the establishment of an airport.
* The Prime Minister stated that no development without conservation and destruction is called sustainable development.
* The Prime Minister stated that no one should be tolerated who wants to destroy the peace of Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the green sea must be maintained and the reputation as a rising star in the southwest and encourage the development of ecotourism like Dara Sakor without deforestation.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that ecotourism does not require deforestation, but it benefits the tourism sector more than agriculture and forest protection.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen urges to prevent sewage into the sea
* The Prime Minister urged Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister Thong Khon and Minister Say Sam Al to work together to ensure that no sewage is discharged into the sea.
* The Prime Minister stated that in the past, there was a request to burn garbage on the islands in Cambodia to produce electricity, but he refused.
* The Prime Minister stated that now more and more garbage and dirty water flow into the sea, which must be jointly protected to ensure the beauty of the Khmer sea.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the ban on pouring soil into the sea is not all ban, some places also need to be allowed to prepare rocks to prevent waves to form a beach for recreation.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he supported the law to punish those who dumped land into the sea without permission.
* Samdech Techo urges the Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province to make efforts to restore the reputation of Preah Sihanouk Province.
* Samdech Techo pointed out that the decline in the number of tourists in Sihanoukville is justified by the more choices of people to visit. But there is also the issue of selfishness, the issue of security, social order that needs to be strengthened, especially Cambodian law must be strictly enforced by all people living on Cambodian territory.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen urged to make efforts to improve all necessary infrastructure systems, including roads, electricity and water to meet the needs of tourists.
* Samdech Techo stated that efforts must be made to prevent illegal gangs and drug use on the beach. That is, do not make the coastal area a haven for drug gangs or other criminal groups, especially terrorist groups.
* The Prime Minister urged efforts to encourage people to cultivate and raise animals to supply hotels. Samdech Techo said that tourism, agriculture and handicrafts must be taken into consideration.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that construction projects connecting Koh Kong to Pursat and Battambang will take place in the near future.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen urges more efforts to build infrastructure connecting provinces.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that efforts must be made to protect the safety of tourists traveling by water.
* Samdech Techo Prime Minister stated that all islands need to be invested because in other countries, they have already done it.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that it was too bad to spread that Cambodia was setting up foreign military bases in Darasakor and building infrastructure in the area for both civilian and military use. The Prime Minister reaffirmed that the Cambodian Constitution does not allow the presence of foreign troops on Cambodian territory, both navy and land.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen asked what Cambodia needs the presence of foreign troops?
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen has questioned what he wants from Cambodia other than killing Cambodia in the past. Samdech Techo Hun Sen asked not to continue killing and torturing Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo stated that Cambodia does not need the presence of foreign troops in Cambodia. Samdech Techo questioned why the Vice President wrote a letter to Samdech Roeung alleging that Cambodia was building a foreign military base. Samdech considers that the US Vice President received the wrong information.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he would expand the Sihanoukville International Airport for large aircraft landings and expand the airport in Koh Kong for medium-sized aircraft.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen asked the countries that have bad intentions towards Cambodia not to continue to kill the Cambodian people and let the Cambodian people live in peace. Should Cambodians continue to die?
* The Prime Minister continued that although Cambodia was able to amend the Constitution, Samdech did not change to enable the presence of foreign troops in Cambodia or the presence of Cambodian troops to other countries outside the framework of the United Nations.
Before concluding the speech due to the ceremony on the occasion of his wife's birthday, Samdech Techo Hun Sen wished and expressed his sincere love for his wife, who was born in the sad era and thanked his wife for her sincere love for Samdech. And fought together until the current situation.
