Legal Awareness: Sexual Harassment
(Phnom Penh): In general, all people have the right to communicate in activities as long as the exercise of those rights does not affect the rights and freedoms of others, not contrary to the good order of society or contrary to the law.
Sexual relations are the right of every person who reaches the age of majority to have sexual intercourse and shall be exercised by the will of the parties, but only if such sexual relations take place under the pressure of a person of higher status. The other person under the power hierarchy of the function of its role is a criminal offense.
The means of repression can be expressed in the form of gestures, words or actions that put pressure on the victim without any violence or threat with a weapon, and the act is repeated.
For example, Mr. A, a professor at a university, used his position as a professor to say to a female student who failed the exam that if she agreed to give her body to him, he would help her. Passed the exam and he always said this to her many times.
Since sexual harassment is a visual offense, it does not matter whether the perpetrator received sexual favors from the victim or not, as long as he or she was subjected to harassment. Abuse of power two or more times for the purpose of obtaining sexual favors is considered an offense.
In summary, sexual harassment is a type of sexual harassment that Cambodian criminal law criminalizes and punishes in order to protect the honor, dignity of individuals, security, order and good traditions of Cambodian society.
