Russian bomber returns home after Venezuela mission
MOSCOW (Reuters) - Two Russian bombers sent to Venezuela earlier this week have finally returned to Russian territory. This is according to a quote from the Russian newspaper Sputnik on Saturday evening, December 15, 2018.
On that occasion, the Russian Ministry of Defense also released a video clip showing the reception of the two Tu-160 fighter jets. While in Venezuela, the Russian Tu-160 flew over the Caribbean and participated in a number of military exercises in the equator, including joint flights with the Venezuelan Air Force.
The move to Venezuela was immediately criticized by the US and Colombian governments, with Moscow claiming the flight was in line with international law.
