Saturday's yellow-shirt protest was attended by thousands of protesters, with more than 1,000 in attendance in Paris. That number has seen a sharp drop from previous weeks, when there were hundreds of thousands of participants across the country. However, there were still tear gas and minor clashes between police and protesters, but they seemed calmer than in previous weeks.
The protests first erupted on November 17, initially aimed at protesting the increase in gasoline and diesel tariffs, but have since turned into anti-base protests. French government policy and violence erupted, leading to the arrest of thousands of protesters last Saturday.
Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Agriculture and Caritas Organize Workshop to Link Marketing between Stakeholders and Local Farmers
Mr. Peng Trida, Director of Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said that in order to improve the living standards of farmers as well as to establish relations between farmers, producers, traders and stakeholders, the Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries has cooperated. Caritas organized a workshop with the participation of many stakeholders.
The director of the department said that the workshop was organized in order to improve the organic products and safety of farmers to get a reasonable price and market, linking stakeholders and farmers in the province, as well as finding challenges, solutions and appropriate conditions. .
In addition, farmers' agricultural skills were trained through free courses on rice, animal husbandry, vegetable growing, hatching, egg production, chicken feed, etc., which are related to the concept of climate change adaptation, promoting Organic vegetable production in accordance with the principles (PGS), networking and partnerships to promote connectivity opportunities between production teams and business partners.
