(Phnom Penh): A horrific traffic accident caused by a public bus crashed into several cars and motorcycles, leaving one person dead at the scene and another. Injured, broken leg. The accident happened at 2:30 pm on December 15, 2018, along Street 371 in Sangkat Boeung Tumpun II, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh.
According to the police, the perpetrator was Sim Nath, a 47-year-old male bus driver living in Trapeang Chhouk village, Sophy commune, Bati district, Takeo province. The victim was named Nou Vandy, male, 36 years old, living at 17A, Street 33 Bet, Sansom Kosal 3 Village, Sangkat Boeung Tumpun, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh. One of the victims, who broke his leg, has not been identified.
(Koh Kong): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, considered the presence of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to open the 7th Sea Festival in Koh Kong Province on the evening of December 15, 2018. It demonstrates the Royal Government of Cambodia's commitment to coastal development and responsibility for the protection and conservation of natural resources.
The 2018 Sea Festival is organized under the theme "Clean Beach, Citizen Resort" accompanied by the slogan "Ecotourism for green growth and sustainable development". To celebrate this year's Sea Festival, the Inter-Ministerial Commission has organized the following key activities:
1: Achievements Exhibition, Food and Beverage Festival and Coastal Development Project, a total of 500 booths, including local product exhibition booths, including small and medium enterprise product booths and developers, 350 booths and 150 foreign exhibition booths Organized by the Ministry of Commerce, Provincial Administration, Ministries, Private Sector.
2: Marching and performing arts performances with the participation of Cambodian artists from the four provinces of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, coastal areas and friendly countries, including the Republic of India, the Republic of Indonesia, the Kingdom of Thailand and the Social Republic. Vietnamese.
4: Organizing local tour packages for young people to Koh Kong province ecotourism destination, which is a link between eco-tourism activities, city tourism and attractive sea tourism, including tour packages to Chi Phat ecotourism community. Areng, Tatai mangrove forest and there is a new beach, Pak Klang beach ....
5: "Koh Kong Saat" program, accompanied by the promotion of the campaign "Clean Restaurant: Good quality and hygienic restaurant, especially no trash under the table" and the promotion of "Code of Conduct for Clean Restaurants and Restaurants".
