Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit officially open the 7th Sea Festival in Koh Kong Province
In his message to celebrate the 7th Sea Festival, Samdech Techo Hun Sen considered this event as an opportunity to strengthen the quality of the tourism industry, promote the creation and development of new tourism products with innovation and high responsibility. With the potential of natural resources in the coastal areas of Cambodia, which has been dubbed the "Star of the Southwest".
According to a report by the Koh Kong Provincial Department of Tourism, this year's Sea Festival has attracted a lot of national and international tourists. According to the report, a total of 1,800 hotels and guesthouses in Khemarak Phoumin and Mondul Seima districts were fully booked.
In addition, to provide accommodation for tourists visiting the festival, the Ministry of Tourism as well as the Koh Kong Provincial Administration has cooperated with the Thai side to arrange up to 600 more rooms for the reception. Cambodians visiting the Sea Festival can rent a room in Trat, Thailand, which borders Koh Kong province, by simply presenting their ID cards to Thai authorities.
In addition to performing arts and spectacles to attract visitors, the Sea Festival also features an exhibition of about 500 products. This product is available from ministries and institutions, as well as from companies in the country and ASEAN member countries.
Looking back, security has also been tightened to ensure the safety of visitors to Koh Kong. Ambulances were deployed at the resort to help people with health problems. General Y Chhean calls on Cambodians to take part in maintaining a win-win monument and a win-win political operator
(Phnom Penh): Speaking to the media today, General Y Chhean, Secretary of State of the Ministry of National Defense, called on the Cambodian people who attended the celebration of the 20th anniversary of the win-win policy to light incense and pray for Sok at the Victory Monument, in particular, asked the angels to take care of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, who is a win-win political operator, to be happy as well.
The appeal of the former leader of the Khmer Rouge Army was made on December 15, 2018, on the occasion of the closing ceremony of the Victory Monument Guide Training Course in Sangkat Prek Ta Sek, Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh. Invited by a large number of participants from various units under the Ministry of National Defense.
The general added that without the presence of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, there would be no win-win policy, Cambodia would not have been able to achieve full peace to this day. Therefore, at the inauguration of the Victory Monument, I would like to ask all Cambodians to join in the celebration, and December 29, 2018 is the historic day that Cambodia has worked so hard to achieve between the Khmer-Khmer conflict.
General Yi Chhean confirmed that the construction of this win-win monument is very important as well as a monument that holds many historical documents. In particular, the story of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's struggle for national liberation, which was inscribed as a legacy for the nation, a statue of Samdech Techo or an outstanding operator who implemented a win-win policy.
Please note that to celebrate the win-win policy, the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has publicly announced that he will hold a three-night, three-day New Year celebration from December 29 to 31. The upcoming 2018 at the Victory Monument to celebrate the 20th anniversary of the end of the civil war in Cambodia through a win-win policy by gaining territorial unity for the first time.
