Cambodia willing to give up billions of dollars from titanium mining in Giphat to protect the environment, unlike France
(Koh Kong): Cambodia could earn about $ 22 billion from titanium mining at the Chi Phat resort in Chi Phat district, Koh Kong province, to protect the environment. This is in contrast to France, which is willing to abandon environmental issues and mine titanium instead.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that the income from titanium mining can make Cambodia develop the country without borrowing money from abroad, but Samdech did not allow it because it destroys the forest in that area and can affect More seawater.
"The Prime Minister's statement was clear at Giphat that our policy is clear and absolutely not to mine titanium because it must be destroyed," said Srey Thamrung, Minister accompanying the Prime Minister, to the media after the meeting. Twenty thousand hectares of forest, and when the ore is taken, the rain comes to the red soil, it flows into the sea, making the blue water turn red. "Samdech's policy is not to want that money, but to take care of the environment."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's commitment made Mr. Bruno Bodad, a Frenchman, admire and appreciate this will. Mr. Bruno Bodad said that Samdech Techo's will is contrary to his French government, which is willing to mine titanium ore without caring about the environmental impact. Watch the video of a husband shooting his wife and then shooting himself from behind a security camera in the house (Video inside)
(Kampong Thom): After a careful investigation into the murder case of a man who shot his wife and then shot himself in the aftermath of the horrific incident, on December 15, 2018, the police also showed a video of his birth. Due to the security camera in the house of the two victims. (Please watch the video below)
Please be informed that the case of a husband shooting his wife and then shooting himself in the back, causing both of them to die in a pool of blood, which occurred on the night of December 13, 2018 in Balong Keut village, Damrey Choan Khla commune, Stung Sen city, Kampong Thom province. The police of Kampong Thom province confirmed that due to the real jealousy, before the day of the incident, the couple had quarreled many times already.
He added that the murder happened at 7:30 pm on December 13, 2018 in Balang Keut village, Damrey Choan Khla commune, Stung Sen city, Kampong Thom province by the perpetrator, Heng Sovannara. A 47-year-old man shot and killed his wife, Sun Pov, 37, in the spine. After his wife died, he shot himself, killing both of them. They both sell rice and wash cars.
According to the relatives of the corpse who lived with his sister, the couple had been arguing several times because some time ago, Sun Pov's husband had strangled his wife almost once, but At that time, some relatives came to help, but now there is an explosion that killed both of them.
After the authorities examined the body, they handed over the body to the relatives for the traditional ceremony.
Cambodia plans to organize international cycling events in coastal provinces to promote tourism potential
(Koh Kong): With the support of the most beautiful beach club in the world, Cambodia plans to organize international cycling to promote the potential of coastal tourism.
The plan to establish an international cycling event was announced during a working meeting between Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Bruno Bodard, director general of the world's most beautiful beach club, on the morning of December 15. This year 2018 in Koh Kong Ty province, which celebrates the 7th Sea Festival.
Mr. Srey Thamrung, Minister accompanying the Prime Minister, told the media that during this meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Director General discussed a lot about the conservation and development of Cambodia's coastal areas. In particular, make sure that Cambodia's beautiful beaches continue to maintain their beauty with a good environment.
In this meeting, Mr. Bruno Bodad, who helped Cambodia to put the beaches in Koh Kong, Sihanoukville, Kampot and Kep into the most beautiful beach club in the world, expressed his admiration and admiration for the beauty of Khmer beaches. In particular, he praised Koh Kong province, which has both attractive mangroves and beautiful beaches as a major attraction for tourists.
In addition to discussing coastal conservation and environmental issues, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Bruno Boudad also discussed a number of projects to promote Cambodia's coastline to the world.
According to Srey Thamrong, projects planned by Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Bruno Boudad to promote Cambodia's coastal potential include the creation of an international professional cycling event and the convention of the most beautiful beach club on World in Cambodia in 2022.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen proposed to organize a general meeting of the most beautiful beach club in the tourism development area "Dara Sakor" located in Botum Sakor district, Koh Kong province. Samdech Techo expects that the organization of this General Assembly event will make it more attractive and interesting for tourism to Cambodia.
For international professional cycling events, according to Bruno Boudard, the race from the "Dara Sakor" development zone to Bokor Mountain and down from Bokor Mountain to Kep, Kampot and Sihanoukville. The event will bring together professional cyclists from countries in Asia, ASEAN and European countries.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen has fully agreed to this project, and the Prime Minister has asked the Clean Beaches Club of the World to discuss with the Ministry of Tourism to choose a suitable time, such as the sea festival or when there are guests. Come to visit Cambodia a lot.
Through this international professional cycling event, Samdech Techo Prime Minister expects to help promote Cambodia's coastal tourism potential even more to the world and also contribute to attracting tourists to Cambodia.
Please note that in the meeting with the Director General of the most beautiful beach club in the world, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also reminded of the difficult situation in Koh Kong province in the past. Such as no way to travel and confrontation with the Khmer Rouge forces.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized to the General Director of the Club that without the win-win policy to end the flames of war 20 years ago, Koh Kong could not have developed as it is today.
(Bangkok): After the successful mission of the International Conference on Islamic Solidarity on December 11-13, 2018 in Makkah, Saudi Arabia, Senior Minister for Special Mission Osman Hassan continued his mission to Thailand to lead the delegation. Of the Cambodian Halal Specialist Working Group and leaders of relevant ministries to attend the 5th Halal Conference in Thailand 2018 from 14 to 16 December 2018.
The conference will be held at the Bangkok International Trade and Exhibition Center under the theme "Halal specificity in the biochemical era" under the auspices of the Halal Science Center of Chulalongkorn University in collaboration with the Central Islamic Council of Thailand and the Thai Halal Standards Institute.
