(Kampong Speu): A company bidding from the Ministry of Rural Development to repair a road No. 127 in Phum Chrouk village, Sendey commune, Samrong Tong district, Kampong Speu province, on the morning of December 15, 2018, blocked its own Toyota car from Bang Land trucks have the right rules and have a clear contract with the authorities do not pass, claiming that the company is repairing this road and have to pay the owners of land trucks.
The use of vehicles to block the road above not only causes land trucks to not be able to move forward, but also obstructs the vehicles of passengers traveling on this road.
In the past, bidders from the Ministry of Rural Development demanded $ 4,000 from land transporters in exchange for permission to use the road, but the transport side refused. There was a conflict until the car came to block the road like this. They always use the word 'road' that the Ministry of Rural Development asked them to do, so they have all the rights on this road.
A land broker said that he had entered into a settlement with the bidder in the commune hall with the correct contract, but the bidders still blocked their way under the pretext of being the Ministry's road. Bidding rural development. Therefore, no one is allowed to use this road. According to the trader, in fact, the truck was transporting land to build a garment factory to serve thousands of people in the area.
Citizens who witnessed the incident said, "Are all the bidding projects of the Ministry of Rural Development on road issues required to close the business and demand money from travelers?" Are all the roads that the Ministry of Rural Development asked the company to repair really do not allow land trucks to develop stones until this project is completed?
They said that if so, maybe you have the money to build a house or factory to wait a little longer because the company does not have the machinery to repair quickly, hire almost all.
According to the people, the Ministry of Rural Development should have the duty to mediate the above issues, not let this handful of individuals destroy a state institution. Bidders do not come to pave the way for people to walk without money, they take full money from the state and even complicate society, which is almost everywhere.
