(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on December 15, 2018, called on local investors to invest in growing organic vegetables or safe vegetables to supply the local market, reduce imports, guarantee Quality and safe local fruits and vegetables.
Such a call was made on the occasion that Mr. Veng Sakhon accompanied his colleagues to visit Mr. Eng Sotheara's organic vegetable farm in Chamkar Luong commune, Kampong Seila district, Sihanoukville province on Saturday morning, March 8, Samreth Sak. S2562 is on December 15, 2018.
Currently, Eng Sotheara's farm has been growing a variety of vegetables and fruits produced on the farm itself, and some are co-produced with local farmers through contract farming, recruiting trained farmers. NGOs and development partners or come for training on the farm.
The farm is cultivated on more than 40 hectares and on average the farm can supply about 1-2 tons of vegetables to the market in Phnom Penh per day.
Speaking on that occasion, the Minister also expressed his great pleasure and high appreciation to the farm owners, staffs and workers at all levels who have worked hard to grow organic fruits and vegetables to contribute to the supply to the local market to ensure both quantity and quality. Gradually reduce imports in the future.
