Cambodia, Vietnam vow to continue to improve border management and control of border crossings
(Phnom Penh): General Kiet Chantharith, Director General of the General Department of Immigration, Ministry of Interior, chaired a meeting to discuss work and exchange experiences between the General Department of Immigration and the Border Guard Command of the Ministry of National Defense of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam, led by Mr. Major General Fang Sunjian, Commander of the Vietnam Border Guard on December 14, 2018.
During the meeting, the two sides will continue to work together to improve the efficiency of border management, control of entry and exit activities, export-import by coordinating administrative procedures to facilitate cross-border traffic activities.
In order to contribute to the socio-economic development of each country, cooperate in solving timely and effectively situations that occur in accordance with the spirit agreed by both sides and the laws of each country.
In addition, the two sides continue to establish cooperation to enhance the effectiveness of the fight against crime, especially drug offenses, human trafficking, and to actively prevent illegal entry and exit, maintain security and order at the border gates. International of both countries.
In addition, the Cambodian-Vietnamese side will promote propaganda to the people to abide by the treaties on the relevant border regulations of each country and encourage the people to participate in preventing illegal entry and exit against the crime of smuggling. Cross-border tariffs build solidarity and friendship between the two countries.
The two sides agreed to hold the 2019 annual meeting between the Border Guard Command of the Ministry of National Defense of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam and the General Department of Immigration of the Ministry of Interior in the Socialist Republic of Vietnam in the third quarter of 2019. The exact date and place will be agreed upon by both parties through the embassy. Facebook announces private photos of nearly 7 million users leaked due to an error
