(China): Authorities in central China's Tongting River have taken steps to restore the damaged river environment. And so far, this work has borne fruit. As a result, the river has become crystal clear and the number of wildlife enjoying the river has begun to increase in recent years.
Covering an area of 2,600 square kilometers, the Tongting River borders three cities in central China's Hunan Province. Sixty percent of the river is located along the city of Yueyang, where local authorities have taken steps to restore the quality of the ecosystems living near the river.
Illegal dredging is a major challenge for the ecosystem in the Tongting River Basin. In the past, there was a large site that sold and transported sand pumped from the east bank of the river. But the local government has closed all 39 dredging sites and replaced the old ones with grass.
More than 160 wild deer are also living here, leading to the opening of a new deer rescue center in 2016. Today, more than 200 staff and volunteers are protecting these animals. Twice a month they patrol the river and rescue trapped or injured deer.
Tongting River is rich in grass that can be processed into paper. To reduce the impact on the river ecosystem when cutting grass and to reduce pollution during paper production, local governments have closed most local paper mills. Factories that have not yet closed will be required to close by the end of this year.
Nowadays, these weeds not only provide shelter for animals but also help purify rivers.
