(Pursat): A scandal broke when a father raped his own child until she became pregnant. This incident happened from 2017 to April 2018, when her mother was suspicious and took her child to the hospital, only to find out that she was pregnant, so she was surprised and complained to the authorities to investigate and arrest the suspect. The case will be sent to court on the morning of December 14, 2018.
The victim, 16-year-old Mok Thor, living in Thlok Dangkor village, Phteah Rong commune, Phnom Kravanh district, Pursat province, told the police that before the incident, she and her father, Saing Sarun, rode a motorbike together as a construction worker. Every day. After work, Saing Sarun, the biological father, allowed Dup to return home.
When she duped him to a quiet place, he would put his arms around her waist every day, not remembering the date since 2017 and threatening her not to tell anyone. If she told the mother, the suspect father would beat both mother and child. Out of fear, she did not dare to tell the truth to her mother or neighbors.
According to Nguon Sopheap, 45, the victim's mother explained that she had previously suspected that her husband and daughter were having an affair and that locals, especially men, were joking with their daughters. On the other hand, after dinner, they often go to bed under the mosquito net with her husband and children, but her husband always chases her to another bed.
Since then, Nguon Sopheap has been puzzled and noticed that her daughter is anemic. She is pregnant. Nguon Sopheap immediately brought her son to file a complaint on December 12 so that the police could help find justice for her daughter.
Brigadier General Chap Yam, Deputy Commissioner for Anti-Trafficking in Persons and Juvenile Protection of the Pursat Provincial Police, said that after receiving the victims' complaints and with the coordination of the Pursat Provincial Prosecutor. The suspect, Saing Sarun, was summoned to the Anti-Trafficking and Juvenile Protection Office on the morning of December 13, 2018 for questioning.
Suspect Saing Sarun confessed that he had raped his daughter since April 2018 at around 12:00 pm on the bed under his house in Thlok Dangkor village, Phteah Rong commune, Phnom Kravanh district, Pursat province. She became pregnant by threatening her daughter not to tell her mother and locals about the scandal.
The deputy commissioner said that the suspect was sent to the provincial court on the morning of the 14th to seek justice for the victims. Cambodia, Korea Hold Workshop on "Developing Environmental Policy Capacity through Sharing Knowledge and Experience"
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Academy of Cambodia in collaboration with the Korean Environmental Institute (KEI) on the afternoon of December 14, 2018 organized a workshop on "Development of environmental policy capacity through the sharing of knowledge and experience." This workshop was held at the Royal Academy of Cambodia.
Please be informed that the Royal Academy of Cambodia and the Korean Environmental Institute (KEI) have agreed on cooperation in promoting joint research. From 2012 to the present, the two institutions have collaborated on joint research, capacity building workshops, international conferences, publications, and online environmental policy curricula.
At the same time, the two sides agreed to cooperate in supporting the implementation of the online environmental policy study program in Cambodia since 2016 and will continue until 2018.
