He said that the quality and quantity control is based on on-site monitoring equipment, such as calibrated tanks for measuring the amount of oil fired from the counter in different sizes, 5 liters, 10 liters and 20. L. The octane and cetan indexes are used in mobile laboratory vehicles.
According to Mr. Chamnap, as a result of quality control and quantity of fuel of 3 stations and depots at the above location, there is 1 station and depot named TELA (Russey Sros), Lot 47, Lum Road, Niroth, Chbar Ampov The amount of oil is not in accordance with the measurement standards.
The deputy director of the Consumer Protection Department of the General Department of CamControl claimed that the inspectors had asked the station and depot owners to re-contract the oil vending machine according to the prediction through the competent authority.
(Phnom Penh): After many years of banning catfish farming, the Royal Government allowed people to raise it again in 2016. Catfish re-licensing reduces Cambodia 's catfish imports from Vietnam by more than 40,000 tonnes a year.
Catfish farming is banned by the Royal Government under the explanation of the former Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Mr. Chan Sarun, that catfish farming leads to the destruction of fish that will be caught for fish food. The cat. The ban on catfish farming means that people have to buy thousands of tons of catfish imported from Vietnam every year.
In 2016, after Mr. Veng Sakhon was appointed Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, he asked the Royal Government to allow the catfish farming to resume. He explained that catfish farming does not destroy fish resources, because this fish farming is not only dependent on the young fish as food, there are other foods as well.
In addition, the opening of catfish farming also contributes to improving the livelihood of fish farmers and also reduces the import of fish from neighboring countries, where people spend a lot of money to feed Vietnamese people by buying catfish. .
During a visit to a catfish farm in Batheay commune, Batheay district, Kampong Cham province, on December 13, 2018, Mr. Veng Sakhon claimed that the reopening of catfish farm in Cambodia Reduce catfish imports from Vietnam by more than 40,000 tons. Previously, Cambodia imported about 60,000 tons of catfish per year, but now only about 13,000 tons.
According to the Minister, Cambodia currently raises about 60,000 tons of catfish per year, and it is expected that the increase will increase the number of catfish imports.
Mr. Long Sreang, a fish farmer, expressed his enthusiasm and happiness for the reopening of catfish. He explained that in the past, banning catfish farming caused a lot of losses in Cambodia, first by selling baby fish to neighboring countries and buying farmed fish to eat instead.
But after reopening, it brings benefits to the people and also makes the Cambodian people do not face diseases due to eating this fish. According to the fish farmer.
Mr. Lor Sreang claims that catfish raised in the country face a lot of diseases because they raise a lot of chemicals, unlike raising in Cambodia has a good climate, raising without chemicals and similar to natural fish does not affect the health of You eat that.
The fish farmer also claims that raising catfish is also profitable because the yield and breeding period are similar to other types of fish, but the price is higher than other types of fish.
Please be informed that Angkor Wat was declared a UNESCO World Heritage Site on December 14, 1992. As of December 14, 2018, Angkor Wat has been included in the World Heritage List for 26 years. For the past 26 years, Angkor has been saved from many dangers, especially under the protection of the Apsara Authority.
The meaning of the video posted on the Facebook page of the National Authority of Cambodia, the Royal Government of Cambodia is strongly committed to the preservation of this great heritage. Today, Angkor Wat has become the number one tourist destination in the world, attracting millions of international tourists to visit and get to know Cambodia's cultural treasures.
Every year, the Royal Government of Cambodia always celebrates this event to remind all Cambodian children to love and participate in the preservation of heritage. In particular, expressing deep gratitude to the Cambodian ancestors who sacrificed for the cause of the glorious civilization of Cambodia in the past and the continuous struggle of the country's leaders in overcoming all obstacles to protect the precious heritage of Nation and the whole world.
Angkor Wat is a temple located in Siem Reap province, located in the northern part of Siem Reap city in Siem Reap district, 7 km from the provincial town. Angkor Wat is the largest collection of Hindu temples and monuments in the world. The temples of Angkor Wat were built by King Suryavarman II, a masterpiece of great luxury and fame spread all over the world.
The Angkor Wat temple complex, including the water farm, is 1.5 km long and 1.3 km wide, with an area of 200 hectares. The central tower of the temple shows two meanings to Khmer architecture, a mountain temple with many levels and a surrounding width.
The temple of Angkor Wat was designed to represent Mount Sumeru, the abode of the gods in Brahmanical mythology. By now, Angkor Wat is almost a thousand years old.
Kampong Chhnang Provincial Administration: The football table in front of the provincial hall only allows the use of national or major sports programs, rehearsals or moderate play using other pitches
(Kampong Chhnang): The Kampong Chhnang Provincial Administration has confirmed that the missing table in front of the provincial hall allows only national or major sports programs to be used.
This confirmation was made between Mr. Sar Sokha, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports during a meeting with Mr. Chhour Chandoeun, Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province on the football table in front of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Hall this morning, December 14, 2018.
As a result, the meeting agreed on two points, including:
First, the missing table in front of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Hall allows the use of only national sports programs or large programs. Separately, practice or play moderately using another pitch.
Second: The football table in front of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Hall will be surrounded by nets to prevent the ball from going out and causing any possible accidents.
Please be informed that on December 3, 2018, Kampong Chhnang Provincial Administration issued a notification to close Kampong Chhnang Provincial Stadium. The announcement of the closure of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Stadium for two football activities, citing two reasons: First: to prevent and avoid accidents eventually, and second: to avoid disturbing the units around the stadium in the performance of daily duties. . But this decision did not get the support of the masses.
