Please be informed that the 7th Sea Festival (Round 2) 2018 will be held in Koh Kong Province from 14-15-16 December 2018 under the theme "Clean Beach, People" Officially from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen as well. National Post Institute organizes 2nd regional conference on "ASEAN Language Process in Computer System" with 5 countries participating
(Phnom Penh): The National Institute of Posts, Telecommunications, Information and Communication Technology (NIPTICT) this morning, December 13, 2018, organized the 2nd Regional Research Conference on "ASEAN Language Processes in Computer Systems" under the chairmanship of Dr. Kan Chanmeta. Secretary of State, Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications.
The conference will run for two days from December 13 to 14, 2018 and will be attended by researchers, doctors and professors from five countries, including France, Japan, Vietnam, Myanmar and Cambodia. The conference was also attended by professors, researchers and students from the National Institute of Technology (NIPTICT), Royal University of Phnom Penh, Institute of Technology of Cambodia and the Open Institute.
Dr. Kan Chanmeta said that regarding the use of Khmer language in computer systems, Cambodia needs to do more research and development to create various programs to facilitate the writing of office reports such as better communication. .
"I think this research conference is a regional forum to encourage and provide opportunities for researchers to share experiences, showcase innovations and achievements from their research related to improvement," he said. The use of Khmer as well as the languages of ASEAN countries in the computer system.
He added that the active participation of expert speakers and participants, both local and regional, showed the positive development of closer and more trustworthy cooperation between stakeholders, especially the Ministry. Educational institutions and the private sector to promote research and innovation in the ICT sector in line with the policy of developing telecommunications and information technology 2020 of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
"As we already know, research is the core work of higher education institutions to enhance the quality of education and the capacity of professors, which is an important part of training human resources with the ability to contribute to "National development."
Dr. Sam Sithy Serey, Vice President of the NIPTICT National Institute and Representative of the Conference Organizing Committee, said, "We know that language is a vehicle for communication, so we are very proud to organize it. To have a regional conference on ASEAN language processes in this computer system.
Please be informed that the main objectives of this conference include:
First, increase research on languages in the ASEAN region, which will help people access more information and improve communication as part of boosting the region's economy.
Second, increase the network of language researchers by connecting Cambodian researchers with regional and international researchers.
The conference provided some notable results, such as: Sharing experiences from 2 well-known research experts, topics on presentations on 8 research papers (from 5 different countries) related to Improving ASEAN language processing in computer systems.
