Siem Reap Provincial Police Arrested for Drug Trafficking
(Kampong Thom-Siem Reap): Kampong Thom Provincial Police, in cooperation with Siem Reap Provincial Police under the coordination of the two provincial prosecutors, arrested a suspect who was a police officer in Siem Reap in connection with drug trafficking.
On the afternoon of December 13, 2018, the prosecutor of Kampong Thom Provincial Court told Fresh News that the police officer was arrested yesterday in Siem Reap and that the suspect was a police officer from the Bureau of Serious Crimes. Siem Reap Provincial Police.
According to Mr. Ith Sothea, the arrest of the police officer came after the Kampong Thom provincial police arrested a suspect involved in drug trafficking in Kampong Svay district.
After the interrogation, the suspect confessed that he had bought drugs from a police officer wearing three uniforms (with the promotion of four uniforms) working in the Serious Crimes Division of the Siem Reap Provincial Police. After receiving such an answer, Mr. Ith Sothea ordered the authorities of Kampong Thom Provincial Police to cooperate with the Siem Reap Provincial Police under the coordination of the Siem Reap Provincial Prosecutor to arrest the suspect.
After arresting the suspects, police confiscated 26 packs of drugs and two mobile phones. The suspect is currently being questioned at the Kampong Thom Provincial Police to be sent to court tomorrow for further action.
