(Phnom Penh): Dr. Chap Sotharith, Secretary of State of the Ministry of National Assembly Senate Relations and Inspection, informed the leadership and civil servants of the Ministry of National Assembly Senate Relations and Inspection that peace has given us enough opportunities to consider our lives and personal well-being.
Mr. Chap Sotharith recalled that in Cambodia, the social security system was established since the Sangkum era in 1955. Unfortunately, during the war and during the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, this social security system was completely destroyed.
After the liberation on January 7, 1979, until 1993, the governments of the former People's Republic of Cambodia and the State of Cambodia received free medical treatment for the entire population. Later, our country gradually evolved, especially under the leadership of the Royal Government, which had Samdech Techo Hun Sen as Prime Minister. In 2002, the Social Security Law was passed. Sub-decree on the establishment of the National Social Security Fund was approved in 2007.
Dr. Chap Sotharith said that in the current situation, when the country is peaceful and is developing in all areas, the social security system is very important. Cambodians, including workers in private and public enterprises, need this social security guarantee.
He said that this activity gives people in the whole society to feel warm and balanced in life, ensuring stability and harmony in society.
According to the report of Mr. Meng Hong, representing the Director of the National Social Security Fund, the Social Security Fund has prepared 794 membership cards and handed them over to the leaders of civil servants and contracted officials of the Ministry of National Assembly Senate Relations and Inspection to receive. Has provided health care services at various health facilities that have signed cooperation agreements with the Ministry of Health.
On behalf of the Honorary Representative of Dr. Men Sam An, Mr. Chap Sotharith conveyed her deepest condolences to all the leaders and civil servants of the Ministry who attended the dissemination ceremony. The policy of implementing the social security system and distributing the members of the National Social Security Fund to civil servants and contracted officials at the Ministry now.
