(Siem Reap): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior, said this morning, December 13, 2018, that the Ministry of Interior has decided to establish anti-technology crime offices at five capital-provincial police commissioners to crack down on crime. This makes it even more effective.
The Capital-Provincial Police Commission, which established this first step, includes: Phnom Penh, Svay Rieng, Sihanoukville and Siem Reap, which are currently restructuring and training professional officers. Separately, Banteay Meanchey will also be formed after the above four provinces appear in a clear shape.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng stated, "I have set up an office in four commissioners: the Office of Technology Crimes, but in the Ministry of National Police, but in four capitals - provinces: Phnom Penh, Siem Reap, Sihanoukville and Svay Rieng and the next day will be created across the country.
Meanwhile, Lt. Gen. Chea Pov, director of the Anti-Technology Crime Department of the National Police General Commission, told Fresh News that the Ministry of Interior has been set up, but has not yet been officially released. Structuring and training of professional officers to fulfill this task.
Lt. Gen. Chea Pov confirmed that "the Ministry has already established the Office of Technology Crimes, but has not yet officially released, because now is training skills and structure. The office will be set up in Phnom Penh, Sihanoukville, Svay Rieng, Siem Reap and Banteay Meanchey.
Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Chuon Narin and Svay Rieng Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Koeng Khorn also confirmed the establishment of the new office, and the commissioner vowed to continue leading the new specialized office to crack down on crime. Up and more efficient.
However, in addition to the fight against technology crimes, Prince Sar Kheng also continued to push for drug offenses and tighten traffic law. According to Prince Sar Kheng, involved in drug work must cooperate with the owners of clubs, guesthouses and entertainment venues.
