Samdech Sar Kheng Requests a Review of the Role and Powers of the National Police Force
(Siem Reap): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, requested a review of the role and authority of the police so that the police can fulfill their role and authority in accordance with the law. Speaking of the police, Samdech Sar Kheng sees that the Cambodian police are more meek than the police of other countries.
The proposal of Samdech Krala Hom was made on the occasion of Samdech presiding over the appointment of Mr. Tea Seiha to the position of Governor of Siem Reap this morning, December 13, 2018.
The reason for the request of the Minister of Interior came after criticism that the Cambodian police tightened security on civil society organizations on December 10, 2018 as they celebrate the 70th anniversary. International human rights.
Samdech continued, "Then I have to re-study the role and authority of the police so that the police can be able to fulfill their role in accordance with the authority given by law and to protect the interests and protect the rights of the people, there should be no criticism." Come back.
Regarding civil society organizations, Samdech Sar Kheng also emphasized that the Royal Government is in need of operational partners and civil society organizations also need the Royal Government as a good cooperation partner. Therefore, the request to study the authority of the police is made so that the police can fulfill their rights and powers only in accordance with the law, that is, to build a partnership with each other.
Samdech also reminded that in order to strengthen the cooperation and partnership between the government and the sub-national administration with associations and non-governmental organizations, as well as local communities, the Ministry of Interior has also issued guidelines to non-governmental organizations. A legally registered government has the full right to operate in Cambodia.
