The new Governor of Siem Reap, Tea Seiha, has been appointed by His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, in a Royal Decree to replace Khim Bunsong. Separately, Mr. Khim Bunsong was promoted by the King by Royal Decree to the rank of General and appointed Secretary of State of the Ministry of National Defense after he retired from Siem Reap Provincial Governor.
Please be informed that Mr. Tea Seiha is the second child of Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, and was appointed by the Royal Government as the Deputy Governor of Siem Reap in August 2017.
Mr. Tea Seiha, a former officer in the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, has a high rank. After graduating from France, Mr. Tea Seiha returned to his homeland in 2001 and joined the Phnom Penh Military Police. While serving as a military officer, he took time to increase his management capacity at the Royal Academy of High Administration in 2007-2008.
In 2010-2013, while land disputes were raging, the Royal Government set up student volunteer groups to survey land across the country to provide land titles to citizens. He was also appointed Chairman of the Siem Reap Volunteer Youth Group, during which time he was appointed President of the Siem Reap Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia.
Mr. Tea Seiha, Senior Officer of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, ID No. 019864, was promoted to the rank of Brigadier General by Royal Decree dated 13 April 2011 and promoted to the rank of Major General by Royal Decree dated 4 April 2011. 2014.
Mr. Tea Seiha is a member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party. In addition to serving as a senior officer of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and social work at the grassroots level with the youth groups of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, Mr. Tea Seiha often accompanies Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh's overseas missions.
