Ministry of Economy and Finance Holds a Workshop on Dissemination of Quotes on Legal Provisions Related to Accounting and Auditing Professions
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Thursday, March 13, 2018, at the office of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, a workshop was held to disseminate the dissemination of "Legal Quotations Related to Science". Bio-Accounting and Auditing ”under the chairmanship of Dr. Hean Sahip, Secretary of State, Ministry of Economy and Finance.
The workshop was also attended by leaders, civil servants of all ministries, institutions of the Royal Government, sub-national administrations involved in the public financial management reform program, as well as all representatives of the central and local units. Ministry of Economy and Finance.
Speaking at the ceremony, he pointed out that promoting sustainable economic growth, the Royal Government has focused on two main points: (1) - Strengthen public financial management through the reform of public financial management and (2) Development of the private sector through the strengthening of investment and business, development of industry and small and medium enterprises, development of the labor market and development of the banking and financial sector.
In fact, the fourth phase of the Rectangular Strategy clearly states that "private sector development continues to be a priority of the Royal Government in the market economy development approach and plays a key role in promoting growth and socio-economic development." In this sense, the formulation of national policies to maintain macroeconomic stability and socio-economic development, as well as the nation as a whole, can not overlook the private sector.
At the same time, he added that the development of the private sector is necessary and indispensable "clear mechanisms and systems of financial management" to strengthen the efficiency, accountability and transparency of private financial management. In particular, boosting national economic growth through the development of the private sector is largely due to tax collection and the acquisition of new technologies.
He added that the Legislative Council of the Ministry of Economy and Finance has compiled and published a "Quotation of Legal Provisions Relating to the Accounting and Auditing Professions" in accordance with the implementation of the "Code" method for ensuring compliance with the registration obligations. Preparation of financial statements and independent audit.
