20 more mobile ambulances donated by Chinese friends to Ministry of Health today
(Phnom Penh): Twenty mobile clinics for the second time, a grant from a Chinese friend, was handed over to the Ministry of Health on December 12, 2018 at the Ministry of Health.
On that occasion, the Minister of Health, Prof. Mam Bun Heng, thanked the Chinese friends for donating 20 more mobile ambulances, which is the second time, the first time was held on the morning of the 10th. May 2018 ago. This grant has helped the health sector to improve the health of the Cambodian people.
"All these achievements are due to the strong commitment of the Royal Government under the wise and wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the full support of Xi Jinping, President of the People's Republic of China." .
Moreover, Minister Mam Bunheng said, "Through the cooperation in the comprehensive strategic partnership between Cambodia and China and the Belt and Road Initiative, I hope that the people and Cambodia will receive more new assistance. In particular, the project to strengthen the capacity of the Center for Combating Infectious Diseases and the project to expand the Ang Duong Hospital, which may be approved soon.
The Minister of Health also expressed his deep gratitude to the Government of the People's Republic of China, Mr. Deng Boqing, Vice President of the China Inter-People's Cooperation Agency in Cambodia, and the Embassy of the People's Republic of China in Cambodia for their full support. To the Ministry of Health of Cambodia to promote projects to appear quickly.
At the same time, Deng Boking also said, "Today is a great pleasure to attend the handover ceremony of the mobile ambulance to Cambodia, and this year marks the 60th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and Cambodia. "Under the leadership of the two heads of government, China and Cambodia, who have supported each other and worked together for development, have built a deep friendship."
In particular, in 2010, the two countries established comprehensive strategic partnership, cooperation in politics, economy, trade, culture, education, health and sanitation. More and better.
These mobile clinics will be distributed to the 25 capital-provincial health departments to provide medical services to the people, which will contribute to bringing health services closer to the people with quality, safety and efficiency.
It should be noted that in 2018, the Chinese side provided a number of grants, including 40 mobile ambulances, the construction of the Khmer-Chinese Friendship Hospital in Preah Kosomak Hospital and Tbong Khmum Hospital, and in the past, China provided vehicles. Save 200 units and 200 echo devices to save the people of Cambodia. This is an important relationship to improve the well-being of the Cambodian people.
