(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications and the Ministry of Economy and Finance, which are the staff of the Royal Government, have started using data produced by the Data Management Center for Telecommunications and Information Technology (DMC) to verify revenue figures, both tax and revenue. Non-tax collected from telecommunications and internet service providers.
In fact, on December 12, 2018, Mr. Tram Iv Tek, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications, chaired a meeting to disseminate the Joint Proclamation No. 135 of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications dated April 13, 2018 between the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications and the Ministry of Economy. And Finance on "Deployment of Telecommunication and Information Technology Services Data Center (DMC) Data Management Center".
The meeting was attended by leaders of government officials of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications, representatives from the Ministry of Economy and Finance, as well as representatives of telecommunications operators, Internet service providers, a total of about 150 people.
Minister Tram Itek stated that the joint proclamation between the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications and the Ministry of Economy and Finance established that all operators operating in the telecommunications and internet sector in Cambodia are required to be connected to the Telecommunication Services Data Management Center. And Information Technology (DMC), a data management center for telecommunications and information technology services of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications.
"The data collected by the DMC is the official data of the Royal Government to calculate the tax revenue and non-tax revenue, as well as the financial obligations of telecom operators and individuals involved in the telecommunications sector doing business in the country," he said. Cambodia as defined in various laws and regulations.
Tol Nhoc, Director General of the General Department of Posts and Telecommunications, confirmed that DMC was launched in 2016 and all telecom and internet operators are connected to DMC. Therefore, the data collected by DMC plays an important role in directly verifying the revenue figures collected.
Minister Tram Iv Tek also stated that the launch of the DMC's telecommunications and information technology services does not put pressure or increase the burden on telecom operators and individuals involved in the telecommunications sector. On the contrary, this mechanism ensures transparent management, accountability and promotes competition in the telecommunications sector.
Tbong Khmum Provincial Authority Distributes More Agricultural Materials to Farmers to Improve Livelihoods through Agricultural Production and Animal Husbandry
(Tbong Khmum): In order to improve the livelihood of farmers through the production of agricultural crops and animal husbandry, the agricultural equipment of the Food Production Promotion Project, a project that uses the entire national budget, has been handed over to 66 more farmers to implement the project. Through Tbong Khmum Provincial Department of Agriculture.
The ceremony of receiving and receiving agricultural equipment and machinery was presided over by Mr. Long Theam, Deputy Governor of Tbong Khmum Province this morning, December 12, 2018 at Suong City Hall.
He said that the project to promote food production was launched by the Royal Government of Cambodia under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, with the direct funding of the Royal Government of 20.25 million USD in order to increase rice production. Rice and vegetable varieties linked to the market to sustain the market price of agricultural products to improve the livelihood of farmers' families for 3 years from 2016 to 2019.
Mr. Long Theam said that this is the second time that the project has provided agricultural equipment and machinery to vegetable farmers to implement a project to boost food production to 66 families, up from 133 families in 2017.
The Deputy Governor requested the farmers who received the agricultural equipment from the 66 families to expand their cultivation more and pay attention to the cultivation to accept what. New planting techniques introduced by professional officers.
He stressed that farmers must be organized into production groups or farming communities and discuss planting plans clearly by studying the market needs before planting. Raising animals also needs to be considered because in addition to providing meat, it can provide manure for natural fertilizer, reduce the use of chemical fertilizers and provide safer agricultural products.
