(Kenya): Cambodia and Kenya have signed an air transport service agreement to promote closer cooperation between the two countries.
The agreement was reached during a bilateral meeting between Cambodia and Kenya on the mission of General Dr. Mao Havanal, Minister in Charge of the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation, to attend the 11th International Conference on Air Transport Services Negotiations in Nairobi, Kenya from December 10 to 14, 2018.
Please be informed that the 11th International Conference on Air Transport Service Agreement Negotiations in Nairobi, Kenya from 10 to 14 December 2018, co-organized by the Kenya Civil Aviation Authority and the International Civil Aviation Organization. . The international conference is attended by 77 member countries and a number of international organizations.
On the sidelines of the International Conference, Minister Mao Ha Vannal received bilateral meetings with senior officials of the United Kingdom, Kenya, Turkey, the United States, South Africa, the Kingdom of Jordan, Oman and Rwanda to strengthen civil aviation cooperation and promote aviation. In addition to the Kingdom of Cambodia.
Please be informed that for 2018, the Kingdom of Cambodia will receive about 10 million air passengers, with a growth rate of 25% compared to 2017, under the right leadership and a long-term vision of policy. Open the sky of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
