(Preah Vihear): On December 12, 2018, the Association of Municipal, District, Commune and Sangkat Councils of Preah Vihear Province held a one-day training course at Chep District Hall for 11 district councilors and 50 commune councilors. From the eight communes of Chep district, two lessons were learned: 1: Global principles of good governance and 2: Orientation to the newly elected council.
Mr. Yong Huot, Association of Municipal, District, Commune and Sangkat Councils of Preah Vihear Province, stated that the training on both lessons was aimed at enhancing the capacity of District Councilors and Commune Councilors on the Royal Government's policy of democratic development. The Cambodian government will reflect on sub-national practice.
Both of the above lessons were organized by national and international experts with the support of EU-UNDP in Cambodia. Lesson content includes: good society, good governance, social accountability, decentralization and deconcentration in Cambodia, roles and responsibilities of sub-national administrative councils and planning of municipal, district and khan councils and commune councils.
Separately, on December 13th and 14th, 2018, the Association of Municipal, District, Commune and Sangkat Councils of Preah Vihear Province will open the same session to Rovieng District and Choam Ksan District Councilors as well as 160 local Commune Councilors. Both.
The workshop focused on the results of the PISA-D program, which came from an international assessment of the literacy and numeracy capabilities of 15-year-old Cambodian students, and will be used as a basis for improving strategic education policy. Curriculum education as well as teaching and learning quality. Cambodia joined PISA-D in 2016 and officially announced the results today.
The benefits of participating in PISA-D 2021 can benefit Cambodia as follows:
1: Make Cambodia have a system to measure the value of students at the international level and be present in the global education framework.
2: Help highlight the key points in human resource development in accordance with the vision of 2030 and 2050 and the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4 of the Royal Government.
3. Strengthen the national student assessment system by extracting techniques and experiences from PISA 2021.
4. To fill the shortage of curriculum, teaching methods and study of students in Cambodia, especially the study of secondary school students.
5: Understand the various experiences in managing the school successfully so that students get good academic results and respond to the evolving needs of Buddhism and the regional and global market economy.
