(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on Wednesday morning, December 12, 2018, met with nearly 20,000 workers from factories. 23 enterprises in Kampong Speu province. The meeting on December 12, 2018 was held in Romduol village, Trapeang Kong commune, Samrong Tong district, Kampong Speu province.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the people who participated in the election last July. Samdech stated that participating in this election is to participate in the exercise of democracy and the exercise of their rights as determined by the Constitution.
The Prime Minister also thanked the workers and the people who voted for the CPP. Samdech Techo said that the election for the Cambodian People's Party is an election to protect peace, because only the Cambodian People's Party has the ability to maintain this peace. Peace leads to political and employment stability.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that this peace was difficult to achieve and was carefully maintained by the Cambodian People's Party. This peace has brought about the current development and also improved the lives of the people, including those who do not support the government.
Samdech Techo reminded that Samdech used to change and advocate in the National Assembly to allow people to sell their farmland along National Road 4. According to Samdech, at that time, some lawmakers opposed the idea of selling farmland along National Road 4.
Samdech Techo stated that the idea of preventing people from selling farmland along National Road 4 was a mistake. Samdech Techo said that if the land is left for the people to farm, they will get little profit, but if they sell the land at a high price and use that money to buy land elsewhere or do other business, it will be profitable. On the other hand, when factories and enterprises are set up in the fields, they provide a lot of jobs for the people.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his pride in setting out a vision for development in Kampong Speu province. Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that until now, all of Samdech's development policies are rarely wrong, if wrong, only slightly wrong.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that up to now, the income from the industrial sector has increased to 32%, injected into the national income.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that those involved in the violent incident on Veng Sreng Street must be punished according to the law. Because that incident was the cause of the overthrow of the Royal Government and the dissolution of the CNRP.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen confirmed that Mr. Ath Thorn, Mr. Pav Sina and Mr. Chea Mony were not involved in the incident on Veng Sreng Road. The Prime Minister asked Mr. Ath Thorn, Mr. Pav Sina and Mr. Chea Mony to find evidence to prove their non-involvement in the incident on Veng Sreng Road.
The Prime Minister asked the three to appeal against the Phnom Penh Municipal Court's ruling yesterday.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that currently Cambodia can produce about 7 million tons of cement instead of imports.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen called on guesthouses, hotels in Sihanoukville or Kep to try to keep prices the same during the New Year. But the Prime Minister said that when demand is higher than supply, prices will rise, and if supply is higher than demand, prices will fall.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen cited, for example, in New York City that every time there is a UN General Assembly, hotels in New York go up by 100 percent or even 200 percent.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen recalled that when Samdech went to fight in Vietnam in 1977, when he raised a spoon to eat rice, tears flowed because he missed his wife and unborn child, especially the Cambodian people who were hungry.
Samdech Techo Prime Minister continues to call for the construction of a safe community of factories, not to have younger brothers and older brothers, not to have drugs and places to transmit HIV and so on. Samdech Techo Hun Sen called on factory owners and workers to talk with understanding to solve problems.
The head of the Royal Government, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, called for a joint national movement to prevent the spread of AIDS.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that LGBT people have the highest prevalence of HIV infection. Samdech Techo called on them to protect themselves from HIV.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the amendment of the law on political parties by asking the Prime Minister to ask the King to lift the ban on political activities is for all political parties, not for any political party or group.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen has announced that after the law comes into force, Samdech is ready to accept any request from politicians asking for a waiver of the ban on politics.
