NEC urges all civil servants to strengthen their capacity to plan, budget, program and implement for transparency and accountability
(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) on December 11, 2018 issued a press release on the workshop on the procedures for monitoring and evaluating the implementation of program budgets organized by the Financial Management Reform Working Group. Public Affairs of the NEC and supported by the Public Financial Management Reform Program of the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
Mr. Som Soreida, Deputy Secretary General of the NEC, said at a workshop in Kampong Cham today that the workshop was held to strengthen the capacity of officials to prepare program budgets and implement program programs, especially on oversight procedures. Monitor and evaluate the implementation of program budget implementation to be more precise, accurate, transparent and accountable.
He claimed that in the two years that the NEC has implemented the program budget, it has gone through a number of challenges, but the NEC is still committed to continuing its efforts to follow the reform policy of the Royal Government. For example, the guidelines of the Ministry of Economy and Finance to achieve the goal of implementing the program budget, which is the principle of the third phase of the public financial management reform program.
Please be informed that this workshop will be held for two days from 11 to 12 December 2018 in Kampong Cham with trainers and trainers from the General Department of Budget of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and the Institute of Economics and Finance.
Kampong Cham Provincial Governor Leads an Expert Officer to Rescue Durian Crops in Stung Trang District
(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, on December 11, 2018, led a working group and agricultural experts to rescue durian crops that are suffering from various diseases in Kilo 10 village, Arak Tnaot commune, Stung Trang district, province. Kampong Cham.
Kim Savoeun, director of the Kampong Cham Provincial Department of Agriculture, said that the durian crop in Arak Tnaot commune, known as durian, covers 303 hectares and bears 4,600 tons of fruit per year, including durian seeds. There are two varieties, Manthong and Sony, but currently durian crops in the area are suffering from various diseases, especially fungal diseases.
Due to the recent outbreak of information on social media, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun received information on social media, so he immediately took professional measures to conduct a study on the disease of durian to find a cure for durian trees to farmers in That brown devil commune.
At the same time, the provincial governor advised farmers in Arak Tnaot commune to form a community in order to organize cooperation for the common benefit of the durian crop for the future. On the other hand, community cohesion makes it easier to provide timely information to professional officers to find ways to facilitate various tasks in the community that are experiencing difficulties.
