After more than 60 students of Thmor Koul High School fainted today, CamControl officers inspected the scene to find the real cause, the fainting was not caused by food
(Battambang): On the morning of December 11, 2018, Battambang Provincial CamControl officers inspected the location of Thmor Koul High School and met with the team at the district hall where 63 students of Thmor Koul High School fainted recently. This.
Mr. Hak Sokrin, President of Battambang Provincial Control Branch, said that the officers of Battambang Provincial CamControl attended the meeting at Thmor Koul District Hall and then went to Thmor Koul University for education and to go to Thmor Koul Referral Hospital to ask for information about the students. Fainted with the participation of many relevant institutions under the presidency of the Governor of Thmor Koul District.
The case occurred from 6 to 11 December 2018, an incident occurred with 63 students, including a boy, dizzy and fainted in the school.
According to the spirit of the meeting at Thmor Koul District Hall and the direct interrogation at Thmor Koul High School and Thmor Koul Referral Hospital, then the Governor of Thmor Koul District and Dr. Ouk Vitya, Deputy Director of Battambang Provincial Health Department in charge of Infectious Diseases and Camcontrol officers summed up. That is not caused by food.
Experts said that this case may be due to the study of both state hours and overtime should be up to 12 hours per day. Panic attacks, irregular eating habits, inadequate rest, fatigue, and poor health can cause dizziness and fainting.
