The Inter-Ministerial Commission was established to promote the expansion and strengthening of fiber optic networks throughout the Kingdom of Cambodia, which is the key to the development of the Cambodian economy towards the fourth generation industrial revolution and the digital economy.
The Commission has the following duties:
* Study the condition of the fiber-optic cable of the Kingdom of Cambodia to set technical standards and expand the underground fiber-optic cable network to be better.
* Establish legal standards to co-operate, use and list the cable network together with the infrastructure of other ministries and institutions for aesthetics and to avoid digging the infrastructure many times.
