Well-known South Korean bank expands branches in Cambodia
The official licensing and ribbon-cutting program for the inauguration of the IBK Bank branch took place on the morning of December 11, 2018 at the Raffles Royal Hotel, chaired by Mr. Rath Sovannarak, Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia.
Since its inception in 1961, IBK Bank has consistently adhered to its principles of focusing on small and medium business lending. IBK Bank is currently the largest lender to small and medium businesses in the Republic of Korea.
IBK opened its Commercial Representative Office in Phnom Penh in January 2015 and received a license in principle from the National Bank of Cambodia in April 2018, leading up to its official opening today.
Kim Do-Jin, Chairman and CEO of the Bank, said that IBK Bank is a Korean state-owned bank with a primary vision of supporting small and medium enterprises (SMEs) and the main purpose of IBK Bank. Coming to the Cambodian market now is to support the companies of the Republic of Korea that are doing business in Cambodia and local businesses, as well as to contribute to the development of Cambodia.
According to the Chairman of the Board, as the financial pioneer bank, which is reflected in the skills and experience of Korea's economic development over the last 56 years, IBK Bank will continue to strive to achieve its vision to Become the leading small and medium business lending bank in Asia as a client financial partner for a better future.
IBK Bank now operates its first branch in Phnom Penh, located in Olympia, along Monireth Street (Neang Kong Hing Roundabout), and plans to expand its branch network in the near future. The beginning of 2020.
