The presentation of this tax revenue was made at the meeting to summarize the results of tax collection in November 2018 and the direction for further implementation of the General Department of Taxation under the chairmanship of Mr. Kong Vibol, the Royal Government delegate in charge as the Director General of the General Department of Taxation. Department of Taxation.
Speaking at the meeting, Mr. Kong Vibol pointed out that in November 2018, the results of tax revenue collection of the General Department of Taxation collected 750 types of tax revenue (according to the General Income Data Management System of the General Department of Taxation) in the amount of 750 .02 billion riels, equivalent to approximately 187.50 million US dollars.
On that occasion, Mr. Kong Vibol further instructed all units to continue to work hard to enforce the labor law and to be gentle but firm based on the legal aspect in responding to taxpayers to make them happy to accept and volunteer. Every taxpayer should minimize the taxpayers' grievances and provide good cooperation in paying taxes to the people.
For 2018, in order to ensure the effective implementation of tax revenue collection and to achieve the maximum plan, the General Department of Taxation will continue to strictly and effectively implement the in-depth reform policy. Of the Royal Government and set out some measures as follows:
* Continue to implement more effectively for the last year the medium-term revenue collection strategy of the Royal Government 2014-2018.
* Cooperate with the General Department of Policy of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and relevant institutions in accordance with the instructions of the Prime Minister and the direct indication of the Deputy Prime Minister, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance to prepare a revenue collection strategy for 2019- 2023 as well as fiscal policies for the future.
* Continue to adjust the value of real estate, which is the basis for real estate tax in accordance with the recommendations of the Prime Minister.
* Improve the value-added tax refund mechanism for embassies as well as businesses, as well as take into account the request for refunds from tourists.
* Continue to reform human resources by strengthening management, evaluating performance and training.
* Continue to push for deeper implementation of key reforms to increase the efficiency of providing public services to taxpayers to have a higher quality, faster, easier to make the tax administration a more trusted state institution. From the public from all walks of life. * Continue to modernize the information technology system by continuing to develop tax management software based on information technology.
* Continue to promote and mainstream the tax culture and strengthen the implementation of the tax law among business people from all walks of life through the organization of outreach workshops on the Cambodian tax system.
* All provincial-Khan tax branches must strengthen the monitoring of taxpayers' submissions.
Cambodia, Vietnam and Laos host 21st Ho Chi Minh City Radio Cycling Festival
(Kratie): Kratie Provincial Authority on the morning of December 11, 2018, held a welcoming ceremony and awarding prizes to the 1st, 2nd and 3rd place winners and the opening ceremony of the cycling team. The Voice of Ho Chi Minh City (VOH) of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam competes in three races.
So far, it has been completed and the bike race has been released in three stages, including:
The big motorcycle team escorted the 64 bikes to three countries: Vietnam, Laos and Cambodia, with the largest number of Vietnamese riders with a distance of 144 kilometers from Vietnam. To Kratie province.
