Tomorrow, Samdech Techo Meets Nearly 20,000 Workers in Kampong Speu Province, By the End of 2018, Samdech Techo Meets Nearly 600,000 Workers
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will hold a meeting with nearly 20,000 workers on Wednesday morning, December 12, 2018. From 23 factories in Kampong Speu province. From the beginning of January 2018 until tomorrow's meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen met with a total of nearly 600,000 workers.
Tomorrow's meeting will be held in Romduol village, Trapeang Kong commune, Samrong Tong district, Kampong Speu province. Tomorrow's meeting is the fifth meeting and for Kampong Speu, there is one more meeting left to finish the first round in Kampong Speu.
According to the report of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, from August 20, 2017, which is the first day of the meeting with workers until December 12, 2018, tomorrow is The 60th meeting is over. This time, there were 859,567 workers, section chiefs, team leaders, and administrative heads.
From the beginning of 2018 until December 12, tomorrow, Samdech Techo Hun Sen met with workers 35 times, and there were 580,513 workers, group leaders, section managers, administrative directors.
