Who is Mr. Tea Seiha, who was appointed by the King to be the Governor of Siem Reap?
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Tea Seiha has been appointed by the King to be the Governor of Siem Reap Province, replacing Mr. Khim Bunsong, who has been promoted by the King to the rank of General and Secretary of State of the Ministry of National Defense.
The appointment of Mr. Tea Seiha, the new generation of youth to lead Siem Reap province, was highly praised by the people, as it is expected that this young leader will show his ability and achievements to contribute to the development of the province with the potential of tourism. There is prominence.
Who is Mr. Tea Seiha? What is your resume or education? Mr. Tea Seiha was born on August 31, 1980 in Phnom Penh, an officer of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces with a high rank. He is the second son of Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense.
After graduating, Mr. Tea Seiha returned to his homeland in 2001 and joined the Phnom Penh Military Police. While serving as a military officer, he took time to increase his management capacity at the Royal Academy of High Administration in 2007-2008.
