Family immunity is stated in Article 355 of the Penal Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia, referring to the impossibility of criminal punishment for a person who commits the crime of theft (theft of property) if he steals the property of his ancestors or relatives and property of his spouse. .
Therefore, if there is a case of theft of property in the family society committed by ancestors or heirs as well as spouses, then Article 355 of the Penal Code applies to this case, which allows the perpetrator to escape punishment for the crime of theft of property. .
Example: Mr. Sok stole a motorcycle belonging to Mr. Sao, his grandfather, to sell to gamble. In this case, the court could not convict Mr. Sok because Mr. Sok was the grandson (heir) of Mr. Sao, who was granted immunity under Article 355 of the Penal Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
In summary, theft of property within the family committed by ancestors or heirs and spouses is not punishable by law. This family immunity aims to avoid any consequences that may arise from criminal cases within the family circle. It should also be noted that this immunity is applicable only to theft offenses, not covering aggravating circumstances.
