General Sao Sokha announces the construction of standard football pitches in all provinces and capitals in 2019 and provides a salary of 2 million Riels to each coach
(Preah Vihear): General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Commander of the National Gendarmerie and President of the Football Federation of Cambodia, announced the construction of standard football fields in schools in the provinces. Then in 2019, and more importantly, the Football Federation will provide a monthly stipend to each teacher of 2 million riels per month.
General Sao Sokha made this announcement on the occasion of attending the inauguration of the football field in Chea Sim Tbeng Meanchey High School and opening the U15 Football Championship, U17 Youth Championship and Women's Football Tournament. 2018 on the afternoon of December 08, 2018.
General Sao Sokha said that the Under-15 and Under-17 Youth Championships and the 2018 Women's Football Championship are an important part of the football federation's youth football development project. Cambodia unveiled at its annual general assembly in 2017.
The general continued that that is the expansion of football infrastructure and football development plan to the 25 provinces, capitals and provinces, and through this competition, we have selected the best players to organize the national team to compete in the league. Football organized by the Southeast Asian Football Association (AFF), the Asian Football Confederation (AFC) or international football organized by FIFA.
General Sao Sokha emphasized that the current competition is important to hone the technical skills of players and opportunities for the development of football human resources such as coaches, referees, technical officers, administration, etc. The Football Federation of Cambodia so far has 100 coaches nationwide, with four coaches in each province training two teams of 25 players each.
At the same time, the Football Federation of Cambodia is responsible for supporting the salaries, training materials and technical skills training of 100 teachers on a regular basis. In accordance with the principles of the Royal Government of Cambodia and the commitment of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to serve the people in improving the lives of civil servants, the armed forces, workers, both private and public.
Please be informed that the Under-15 and Under-17 Football Championships and the 2018 Women's Football Championship Selection Competition will last for 4 months starting from December 08, 2018 in Preah Vihear Province and ending at March 31, 2019 in Banteay Meanchey province, and the athletes who have to compete now have 66 teams with a total of 1,650 athletes.
