Samdech Techo Hun Sen also highlighted the potential and excellence of investment in Cambodia in six points, including:
First, the favorable conditions of political and macroeconomic stability.
Second, Cambodia is strategically located in the ASEAN region, which has been becoming the "factory of Asia" and on the other hand, Cambodia is in the middle of the Mekong region, a region with higher economic growth and connectivity. They.
Third, a diverse and young workforce, in which the population under the age of 35 accounts for 72% of the total population, combined with an increase in the middle-income and The middle class will create opportunities for Cambodia.
Fourth, Cambodia has opened its economy to all investors without discrimination between Cambodian and foreign investors.
Fifth, Cambodian-made goods are not only supplied for the Cambodian market of more than 15 million people, but can also be supplied to the Mekong Sub-region market with about 250 million customers, the ASEAN market with customers. About 630 million people, and the regional market of the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (RCEP), which has about 3 billion customers, as well as access to other major markets in the world.
Sixth, Cambodia and Vietnam signed an agreement on avoidance of double taxation and prevention of embezzlement related to income tax on March 31, 2018 in Hanoi.
Until the morning of December 7, 2018, Samdech Techo Hun Sen began an official visit to Vietnam. During the official visit, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and a high-level delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia laid a wreath at the Vietnam People's Army Youth Memorial and also laid a wreath at the memorial to President Ho Chi Minh.
At the official welcoming ceremony held at the State Palace in Hanoi, the Socialist Republic of Vietnam, Samdech Techo Hun Sen was warmly welcomed by his Vietnamese counterpart Nguyen Suon Phuc. During the official welcoming ceremony, Samdech Techo, accompanied by his Vietnamese counterpart, paid homage to the flags and anthems of both countries.
After the official welcoming ceremony, the Heads of Government of Cambodia and Vietnam, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Nguyen Suon Phuc, held a one-on-one meeting with translators before heading to the bilateral summit for the country's leaders. Both Cambodia and Vietnam.
After more than two hours of intensive meetings and bilateral summits, the heads of government of Cambodia and Laos witnessed the signing ceremony of important documents. The six categories include:
First, Memorandum of Understanding on Cooperation in the Transport Sector for 7 years from 2018-2025.
Second, the amendment of the 2005 protocol for the implementation of the 1998 agreement on land transport.
Third: Amendments to the 2009 Inland Water Transport Agreement.
Fourth, the Cambodia-Vietnam border trade agreement.
Fifth, the Cambodia-Vietnam Bilateral Trade Facilitation Coordination for 2018-2019 on Mutual Tariff Preferential Tariffs.
Sixth: Agreement on the Prevention of Trafficking, Illegal Excavation and Return of the Heritage of the Two Countries, Cambodia and Vietnam.
The Prime Ministers of Cambodia and Vietnam have both expressed their commitment to improving relations and cooperation between the two countries. The construction of the border post between the two countries has also been confirmed by the Prime Minister of the country to be completed in 2019.
The Vietnamese Prime Minister highlighted at the conference that in 2018, Cambodia and Vietnam have achieved a lot of work, which is an important part in strengthening relations and cooperation between the two countries. The border demarcation work, which achieved about 84%, is also a good thing. As for the remaining border issues, Mr. Nguyen Suon Phuc affirmed that he will urge the relevant parties to work together to resolve them by 2019.
According to the MoU, there are two main points that the two signatories have an obligation to implement: First, both parties will abide by the laws and regulations of their respective countries regarding cross-border cash handling, and second, both parties The two must continue to discuss and resolve the remaining unresolved issues related to the border trade agreement as soon as possible.
Until the night of December 7, 2018, Samdech Techo Hun Sen attended a food washing ceremony organized by the Prime Minister of Vietnam, Mr. Nguyen Suon Phuc. The Prime Minister of Cambodia said that Cambodia and Vietnam can still maintain good relations with confidence, despite the current sharp political situation in the world and difficult to predict.
After paying a three-day, two-night official visit to Vietnam at around 12 noon on December 8, 2018, Samdech Techo Hun Sen led a high-level delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia back to Cambodia. After concluding a five-day visit to Laos and Vietnam.
