(Tbong Khmum): On December 08, 2018, Mr. Lek Vutha, Marketing Manager of Camcontrol Tbong Khmum Branch, led the CamControl officials in cooperation with the Provincial Department of Commerce to continue to inspect the date, quality, safety of goods in some marts and food. To analyze banned chemicals that cause harm to the health of consumers in and around Stung Market in Ponhea Krek District, Tbong Khmum Province.
Mr. Lek Vutha said that the implementation of this inspection campaign was carried out on a regular basis in accordance with the instructions of the General Department of CamControl, especially the recommendation of Mr. Mak Pichrith, Director General of CamControl, who instructed all CamControl officers throughout the country to Strengthen and increase activities to inspect the quality of goods, food safety in the market like the early rain to ensure the well-being of the people as consumers.
