The 79-meter-long bank of the Mekong River in Kampong Cham province collapsed 3 to 4 meters across the north end of the closed river bridge in front of three hotels: Monorom Hotel, LCN Hotel and Mekong Hotel. But the place is very broken between Monorom Hotel and LCD Hotel.
Authorities cordoned off the area to prevent people and tourists from passing through. Experts then go to the site to find out the cause of the landslide, and if it does not collapse, the provincial authorities will ask the government through the Ministry of Water Resources and Disaster Management to raise funds. Repair when the water recedes.
Experts confirmed that the landslide was not caused by dredging because there was no sand dredging in the area. However, he said that experts have found that the cause of the landslide in Kampong Cham is due to the current hit the island called Koh Dach.
Um Vibol, director of the Kampong Cham Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology, said that the new riverbank collapse occurred after the Mekong River began to recede due to the riverbank collapse built during 2013. This is located in the 11th village, Sangkat Kampong Cham, Kampong Cham city, where there are two places, causing damage to the river bank to prevent flooding and gardens, in which collapsed to the statues of elephants and lions for decoration.
According to a preliminary study by officials from the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, the landslide was caused by a change in the flow of the Mekong River during the previous rainy season.
According to the physical examination, this situation is unlikely to be repaired on the first construction unless rebuilt. And this is also a big project of the national level that needs to be rebuilt in the coming low water season.
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Cham Prasidh, Minister of Industry and Handicraft, said that the establishment of a giant industrial plant of Chip Mong is a strong contribution to the further growth of the Cambodian economy.
The Senior Minister said this on the morning of December 7, 2018, when he presided over the Chip Mong Industries, a subsidiary of Chip Mong, officially inaugurated the tile and pipe factory built More than 11 hectares is located in Kandal Village, Sangkat Rolous, Khan Dangkor, Phnom Penh.
"I believe that the establishment of such a large-scale industrial plant will make a significant contribution to the further development of the national economy, maintaining a reasonable growth rate as expected," he said. In 2019, it will be able to achieve about 7.1%.
According to the Senior Minister, in 2017, the industrial sector contributed 30% of gross domestic product (GDP) and developed and expanded the structure of the industrial economy, focusing on the expansion of production bases and production. Diversify industrial goods, with data showing that in 2018, the results will be about 21%, different from the previous stage, when the industrial structure focused on the garment industry almost 100%.
He said that this is a progress of the fruitful implementation of the Industrial Development Policy 2015-2025 of the Royal Government. Indeed, by establishing new factories here, it will contribute to providing rich employment opportunities for the people as well as improving their livelihoods.
The Senior Minister encouraged company leaders and colleagues at all levels to continue their efforts to develop their business, produce high quality products, internationally recognized to meet domestic demand and be able to compete with foreign products.
Speaking at the inauguration, Mr. Leang Khun, Chief Executive Officer of Chip Mong, hoped that large-scale industrial investment by local investors would also be a small contribution to raising the country's profile in the industry by taking steps. From an agricultural country to an industrial country, reduce the import of construction materials from abroad and help increase the national economy.
He also pointed out that the machinery of the tile factory can produce 140 tiles per minute, while the pipe factory can produce 500 tons of pipes per month. In addition to the tile and pipe factory, Chip Mong Industries also has ready-mixed concrete products to meet the needs of the domestic construction sector. President of the Cambodia-China Friendship Association: Real estate and construction are the main sectors that support economic growth
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ek Sam Ol, President of the Cambodia-China Friendship Association, said on December 8, 2018 that the real estate and construction sectors are the main sectors that support economic growth and have contributed greatly to the promotion. Social and economic development of Cambodia.
The President of the Cambodia-China Friendship Association also stated that this project is close to the Toul Kork Antenna, which can easily travel as well as geographically, culturally and economically prosperous. He added that BOYI-NEW WORLD has laid the foundation in Phnom Penh, it reflects the confidence of foreign companies, especially Chinese companies that are investing in Cambodia.
Mr. Ek Sam Ol also mentioned that Cambodia has now achieved complete peace and stability and significant progress in all areas. In recent years, Cambodia's national economy has maintained a strong annual growth rate of 7%, and people's incomes have continued to rise, and living standards have risen steadily.
"The real estate and construction sectors are the main sectors that support economic growth and have contributed significantly to the social and economic development of Cambodia," he said.
At the same time, Mr. Ek Sam Ol added that the friendship between Cambodia and China has a long history and the exchange between the two peoples has a long history. Both countries have gone through many storms and tests, but have not been shaken, and have received good prices.
"No matter how the international situation changes, our two countries are still striving to promote the development of strategic partnership and cooperation in all fields," he said. This year marks the 60th anniversary of the establishment of formal diplomatic relations between Cambodia and China.
Mr. Ek Sam Ol added that in the past, our two countries have achieved many great achievements in cooperation in the fields of economy, trade, culture, education, health and tourism. Friendly cooperation between Cambodia and China is not only at the government level, but also people-to-people friendly cooperation.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen and his delegation return to Cambodia after a four-day visit to Laos and Vietnam (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): At around 12 noon on December 08, 2018, Samdech Techo The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Hun Sen, led a high-level delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia to return to Cambodia safely after concluding a four-day visit to Laos and Vietnam.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen began an official visit to Laos on December 5 at the invitation of the Prime Minister of Laos, Mr. Thongloun Sisoulith, in order to strengthen friendship and cooperation between the two countries. In this context, the political, social, economic and trade are deepened and improved.
During his official visit to Laos, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and his delegation were warmly and warmly welcomed by the Prime Minister of Laos and other Lao leaders. During his visit to Laos, in addition to meeting with the Prime Minister of Laos, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and his delegation also paid a courtesy call on the President of Laos and the President of the National Assembly of Laos.
After a fruitful visit to Laos on the evening of December 6, Samdech Techo Hun Sen led a delegation to visit Vietnam. During his visit to Hanoi, Vietnam, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and his delegation were warmly and warmly welcomed by Vietnamese Prime Minister Nguyen Tan Dung and other Vietnamese leaders.
This visit is not different from the visit to Laos, in which the working meeting between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Prime Minister of Vietnam, as well as the President of Vietnam, Nguyen Fu Chung, focused on strengthening cooperation. Better political, social, economic and trade issues.
The two leaders pledged to boost trade to 500 million US dollars by 2020 and to speed up the construction of the remaining 16 percent of the two countries' border posts by 2019.
During his visit to Vietnam, Samdech Techo also confirmed to his Vietnamese counterpart that Cambodia is providing military bases to other countries. Samdech Techo emphasized that the Cambodian Constitution does not allow the presence of foreign troops on its territory and also does not allow its troops on foreign territory outside the framework of the United Nations.
Samdech Techo stated that the dissemination was false information, inciting information with the intention of destroying it. Samdech hopes that the rumors that caused this great investigation will not be spread anymore.
During his visit to Vietnam, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also attended the Vietnam-Cambodia Business Forum. During the forum, Samdech Techo Hun Sen called on Vietnamese businessmen to invest in Cambodia, as Cambodia has many potentials and advantages for investment with high attention and encouragement for foreign investors from the Royal Government of Cambodia.
