(Hanoi, Vietnam): On the afternoon of December 7, 2018, during his visit to Vietnam, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, met with the President of the Cambodia-Vietnam Association at the Mealea Hotel in Hanoi.
The Cambodian-Vietnamese Association is made up mostly of members who have worked in Cambodia or are descendants of former Vietnamese military cadres who have contributed to the liberation of Cambodia from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot. The association also has members who were former Vietnamese ambassadors to Cambodia.
Today's meeting is aimed at enhancing people-to-people contacts. The association has also met with Samdech Techo in the past. In this meeting, Samdech Techo opened the opportunity for members of the association to research the information of the descendants of former Vietnamese army cadres who lost their relatives in Cambodia as well as in Vietnam.
The Cambodia-Vietnam Association has played an important role in both Vietnam and Cambodia, especially contributing to the strengthening of bilateral relations and cooperation between the two countries.
Samdech Techo also informed the delegation of Cambodia-Vietnam Association about the progress of the Association and asked the Association to continue its efforts to expand its activities to continue to support bilateral cooperation between the two countries. Letter to readers: It should be written about what Cambodia has done
(Phnom Penh): In response to the release of some foreign media related to Cambodia, the political situation in Cambodia, a student studying in Phnom Penh sent a letter to readers with the following content:
First, it is said that Prime Minister Hun Sen was a member of the Khmer Rouge who had been in power since 1985. But they did not write about Prime Minister Hun Sen overthrowing the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
Second, the Royal Government is said to restrict the freedom of civil society organizations and the press in Cambodia (especially in the case of The Cambodia Daily). However, they did not write about the fact that The Cambodia Daily decided to shut down the publication itself because it evaded tax obligations in accordance with Cambodian tax law.
Third, it is said that today Cambodia is moving towards dictatorship. But they did not write about the multi-party liberal democracy reflected by the 20 political parties that contested the sixth term, and the turnout was 83.02%, an overwhelming majority.
Sixth: It is said that Hun Sen is taking the Cambodian people hostage. But it does not write about the exercise of the legal rights and freedoms of every citizen and the continuous improvement of the lives of Cambodians living under the roof of peace and stability, both politically and economically.
Cambodia still lacks a lot, but only 20 years (1998-2018) has stepped out of the flames of civil war caused by the previous generation of politicians who deceived foreign ideology into a peaceful country.
Step out of the countries that receive UN peacekeepers to countries that send Cambodian peacekeepers to countries such as Lebanon, Sudan, South Sudan, Mali and Central Africa.
Step out of a country that used to use military force to transform its leaders into a country that practices liberal, multi-party democracy, with regular elections every five years based on the principles of free, fair and just.
Step out of the poorest country to become one of the fastest growing economies in Asia with a growth rate of more than 7% per year for 20 consecutive years and move towards a higher middle income country. 2030 and high income in 2050.
Step out of the country known through the stories of the killing fields and minefields that foreigners fear, to become a country where foreigners line up to visit, want to know about tourist sites, culture and world heritage.
Step from a politically and economically isolated country to a country that successfully integrates into the regional and international arena (as a member of the United Nations, the World Trade Organization, ASEAN and more than 30 other international organizations).
Step from a food insecure country to a country that exports tens of thousands of tons of rice to more than 70 countries around the world.
What I am lifting is just a small part, there are many other points.
What happens in Cambodia does not happen in other countries. Every country has a war, but in their country, they kill indiscriminately, while Cambodia kills only those who know. Therefore, we need to recognize these successes and be mature and patient for future success. If I am wrong, teach me. Do not despise me.
