(Bangkok): Thailand's election campaign will be allowed to start after the upcoming Global New Year. This was confirmed by the Deputy Prime Minister of Thailand, Mr. Wisanuk Kramgam, quoted by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Friday night, December 7, 2018.
During a meeting between the authorities and Thai political parties on the upcoming election on February 24, 2019, Mr. Visanu announced that the Royal Decree on the National Assembly Election will be issued on the 2nd. January next year to allow all political parties to start campaigning across the country.
The Thai Election Commission will start accepting applications for parliamentary seats from January 14 to 18 and the registration of prime ministers from each political party on January 25.
