(Hanoi, Vietnam): The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, said that Cambodia and Vietnam can still maintain good relations with confidence, despite the current sharp and difficult political situation in the world. Guess that.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's presentation on maintaining the strength of Cambodia-Vietnam relations was made during a speech at a dinner hosted by Vietnamese Prime Minister Nguyen Suon Phuc on the night of December 7. This year 2018 in Hanoi, Vietnam.
History has shown that in recent decades, Cambodia and Vietnam have often had strained relations due to the ideological influence of superpowers. For example, under Pol Pot's Democratic Kampuchea regime, which was backed by China and Vietnam, which was backed by the former Soviet Union, there was a sharp conflict.
"Despite the sharp, rapid and unpredictable political situation in the world, our two countries have maintained friendly relations, mutual understanding and mutual trust," he said. "Come as a country, a village, a fence."
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia added that the Cambodian government and people will always remember the sacrifices and assistance of the Vietnamese government and people in liberating the country and the Cambodian people from the Khmer Rouge regime.
At the banquet, the Vietnamese Prime Minister expressed his appreciation to the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia for taking the most valuable time to respond to his invitation to pay an official visit to Vietnam to strengthen and expand the friendship and solidarity in Cambodia. As neighbors.
"We really appreciate the efforts of the relevant leaders of the two countries who have a high regard for the national interests and the people of both countries," he said.
Mr. Nguyen Suon Phuc said that the government as well as the people of Vietnam consider Samdech Techo's visit to Vietnam at this time as a great honor to strengthen Vietnam-Cambodia relations, which is a close friend and a village. Together.
It should be noted that the two countries, Cambodia and Vietnam, established diplomatic relations on June 24, 1967. But was disconnected in March 1970 and reconnected in January 1979. Vietnam and Cambodia are countries with villages and fences with a common border of more than 1,270 km. Check out a collection of photos from international events on December 7, 2018! (Photo inside)
