(Preah Vihear): Some defective and expired goods displayed for sale at the houses of traders in Teuk Krahorm commune, Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province were confiscated by the CamControl officers and burned on December 7. This year 2018, so as not to affect the health of the people.
Mr. Duong Mony, President of CamControl Preah Vihear Branch, said that today, CamControl officials in Preah Vihear Province, in cooperation with the Provincial Department of Commerce and local authorities, inspected pre-packaged goods that were displayed for sale at the homes of traders in Teuk Krahorm commune. Choam Ksan District, Preah Vihear Province.
The head of CamControl confirmed that the goods were damaged and expired after checking that the quality was confiscated and burned immediately.
At the same time, Mr. Duong Mony also instructed our traders before buying other goods to display for sale, to check the date of production correctly in advance to avoid buying defective goods at the bottom of the warehouse. Sold, and more importantly, to store the goods properly to avoid the sun, which is why the quality of the goods are damaged.
In particular, people also need to be careful, because the impact on our health is mostly caused by eating, so before deciding to buy goods to eat to check the date of production correctly. Also.
Cases of fishing offenses in Tonle Sap Lake and Tonle Chhma in Kampong Thom province always break before the police crack down
(Kampong Thom): Police in Kampong Thom Province have twice raided fishing offenses in the Tonle Sap Lake and Tonle Chhma area in Stong district and other areas in Kampong Thom province, but it does not seem to be as hot as it used to be due to the crackdown operation. Those offenses were broken before the police cracked down.
Recently, under the coordination of the Kampong Thom Provincial Prosecutor, Mr. Ith Sothea, the joint police force launched two operations to crack down on illegal fishing in the Tonle Sap Lake and Tonle Chhma areas, including :
* First: On November 23, 2018, the Anti-Economic Crime Police Force cooperated with the Anti-Drug Police Force, the Immigration Police Force, the Law Enforcement Police Force and the Naval Traffic Police Force, led by Col. Yim Sophorn Neay. Deputy Acting Office of the Economic Crimes Police Office cracked down on the Tonle Sap Lake area in Kampong Thom province, confiscating a number of fishing gears, such as one squid and 20 snares.
The police officer said that these materials were kept waiting for the owner to come and make a contract to stop. The fish caught in the fishing gear were released by the police into the Tonle Sap Lake.
* Second time: On the night of December 4, 2018, the above joint police force went to sleep in Tonle Chhma area for one night, but during the operation, no crime was seen. In the morning, the police asked the local people for information, and they were told that the crackdown operation had broken down since the police boat had reached the mouth of Tonle Chhma Lake.
During the visit on the morning of the 5th, the police also found some fishing gear in the protected area and cut and burned, including: 37 snipers and 2 snipers.
Authorities said that in the Tonle Chhma area, a commune deputy using the telephone number 071 90 999 67 called to negotiate with the authorities regarding the confiscation of the above fishing equipment. The deputy chief of the commune was also the one who ran the people to hide in the protected area.
Regarding this serious issue, the Governor of Kampong Thom Province, Mr. Sok Lou, also mentioned in the national meeting at Kampong Thom Provincial Hall in the past that the crime of fishing in the Tonle Sap Lake area is very famous. Yes, but every time you lead the police to crack down, you do not see those criminal activities at all, is it because the perpetrators are aware of it first?
General Chhay Sinarith: The use of private security services is necessary to participate in maintaining security and social order
(Phnom Penh): General Chhay Sinarith, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, acknowledged that the use of private security services is necessary to participate in maintaining security, public order and society as an aid to law enforcement forces.
The remarks of General Chhay Sinarith were made on the afternoon of December 7, 2018 at a meeting on strengthening the private security management of the Department of Private Security Management of the General Commission of the National Police.
"I think the use of private security services is very important," he said. "Management and staff for the General Commission of the National Police to monitor any activities that are contrary to the principles of law, contrary to the guidelines of the Royal Government of the Ministry of Interior."
General Chhay Sinarith also pointed out that private security agencies are an important support force that the police force must value, but private security agencies are not a competent force and must report all crimes that occur locally to the authorities, but not allowed. To use weapons like the authorities.
Regarding the management of this work, the Department of Private Security Management must be clearly managed, especially in the provinces, and the management work should be divided to the Provincial Police Commission, especially on applying for business licenses, while there are currently more security companies in the provinces. 1000 locations that are not yet licensed.
General Chhay Sinarith also stressed that some private security agencies do not seem to cooperate with the police force, which is an illegal act that must be corrected immediately, so the Department of Private Security Management must immediately monitor to avoid problems in the future. That sometimes a small number of security agents are the ones who give a hand to the perpetrators.
However, in order to further strengthen this management, the general said that the National Police had decided to temporarily suspend the issuance of business licenses in order to search for unlicensed companies.
During the meeting, Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey, Director of the Private Security Management Department, also said that there are currently 26,565 private security agents nationwide (2,381 females), of which 239 are private security service providers and There are 1,867 enterprises recruiting private security agents (non-private security services).
According to General Lim Sokharaksmey, a private security service provider has signed contracts with 111 national police commissioners, employing a total of 7,469 private security agents and operating on 3,194 targets.
Cambodia-Vietnam set targets for drug control cooperation in 2019 and continue to implement the spirit of the 15th and 16th bilateral meetings
The Vietnamese delegation was led by Lt. Gen. Le Kuy Voeung, Deputy Minister of Public Security of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam and chaired by the Cambodian delegation, led by Lt. Gen. Chuon Sovann, Deputy Director General of the National Authority for Combating Drugs.
The meeting was held in the spirit of solidarity, friendship, cooperation and mutual understanding, reflecting the efforts and commitment of the two countries' drug control bodies, with the vision of further strengthening cooperation activities. In accordance with the content of the agreement signed in 1998 and the action plan of cooperation signed in 2000.
* A) Appreciate the close cooperation and effective coordination of drug control work with relevant institutions of the two countries, including the sharing of information, monitoring, identification, search and arrest of perpetrators. Involved in drugs.
* B - Commit to encourage and encourage all relevant institutions and organizations to work together in both national and international frameworks in the prevention of drug offenses, as well as: Regular shifts, exchange of information related to crime. Drugs, propaganda, education, anti-drug crime at the border and the operation of the BLO.
C- Continuing the direction for drug control cooperation 2016-2017: To increase the effectiveness of drug control cooperation between the two countries, as well as cooperation between drug control institutions along the border between the two sides. Agreed to continue to urge relevant ministries, institutions and law enforcement agencies to effectively implement the following content:
* Second, continue to advise the border provinces to hold regular rotating meetings with the participation of all relevant authorities of the two countries as agreed (once every 6 months for the district and one year. Once for the provincial level) and, if necessary, both parties may convene an extraordinary meeting.
* Third: Continue to improve the quality and efficiency of the BLO Border Liaison Office to exchange information and record all new information to improve the quality of drug control cooperation, including the establishment of a new BLO office between Ratanakkiri Province of Cambodia and Yalai Province. Vietnam, Kampot province of Cambodia and Ha Tieng province of Vietnam.
* Fourth: Continue to guide and encourage border provinces and districts to disseminate the law on the program to build border villages and schools to become border villages and drug-free schools, to increase the production of propaganda materials to spread knowledge about drugs. Border residents and cooperation in cracking down on drug cases at casinos.
* Fifth, continue to strengthen the cooperation between the border provinces, the Cambodian side, train and provide technical assistance for the Cambodian law enforcement units at the border and organize technical workshops on drug crime investigation, drug analysis for law enforcement officers. And treatment and rehabilitation work.
* Sixth: Continue to encourage the exchange of delegations to study and gain experience at both the national and sub-national levels in 2019. Buy Instant Profit Up To $ 500 From Samsung In The New Year
