(China): To date, investment from China into Panama Port Colon has reached 1 billion US dollars.
Panama is famous for its waterway for ships and the Colon Free Trade Area, located on the riverfront of the waterway. The Panama Canal is bordered by the Atlantic Ocean. And the Colon Free Trade Area is the largest free trade area in the West.
The new container port is expected to be the only port capable of accommodating giant container vessels.
Wang Xiangfeng, director of the Panama Colon Container Port project, says this is a project with a relatively large investment in Panama. Both the Panamanian government and our company in China value this project very much and we have used our budget and human resources to the best of our ability. "Today, all parts of the project are going very well."
The global economic slowdown has slowed the FTA's business growth. But regional leaders are confident of their role in making Panama a world leader.
"The construction of the Panama Container Port will support the long-term plan of the Panamanian government to establish a global shipping hub," said Zhang Liang, general manager of the Panama Container Port Project. "It will also greatly enhance the strengthening of bilateral ties between Panama and China in the fields of economy and trade."
