(Koh Kong): The Koh Kong Provincial Health Department on December 7, 2018 celebrated the World AIDS Day on December 1, 2018 under the theme "We are committed to ending HIV / AIDS by 2025".
The ceremony was presided over by Dr. Tea Phalla, Deputy Director of the National AIDS Authority, Ms. Chhun Ravuth, Deputy Governor, Dr. Toa Moeng, Director of the Koh Kong Provincial Health Department, as well as government officials, students and people living with HIV. Also.
Dr. Tea Phalla said that today's ceremony is to recognize and understand the situation of HIV and AIDS, because HIV is a vicious disease that poses a serious danger to socio-economic development through the loss of resources. People who are the key to development in all areas. "Nearly 1,000 people living with HIV / AIDS across Koh Kong province will receive an end to HIV / AIDS in Cambodia by 2025."
