The bilateral meeting is based on the spirit of solidarity, friendship, cooperation and mutual understanding, reflecting the efforts and commitment of the two countries' drug control bodies, with a view to further strengthening cooperation activities. In accordance with the content of the agreement signed in 1999 and the action plan of cooperation signed in 2000.
Facing the current situation and complexity of drugs: production, cultivation, trafficking and abuse of drugs, both in the region and in our two countries, especially to join ASEAN countries in building "community security Against Illegal Drugs ”From 2016-2025, Cambodia-Laos has set the direction for the 2019 Drug Control Cooperation:
1. Strengthen information exchange cooperation to promote mutual information sharing between the authorities at the national and sub-national levels of the two countries related to cases of production, cultivation, traffic and abuse. Of drugs.
2. Strengthen the implementation of border law based on the law and regulations of the drug law, support the investigation of drug-related cases, and ensure the strengthening of drug control cooperation at both the national and sub-national levels. Meet regularly at both the district and provincial levels in shifts.
3. Strengthen the capacity of BLO border liaison officers in border provinces to increase cooperation, share experiences, as well as seek material support and training from development partners.
4. Establish drug-free villages, communes and schools along the border. Support the initiative to establish drug-free villages, communes and schools in the border areas of the two countries. Attention to implement this initiative effectively and by inspiring the participation of local people.
5: Exchange of delegates in 2019 to exchange experiences on drug control.
6. Strengthen awareness of drugs by improving the lives of the people of the two countries living along the border and promoting awareness of people on the law on drug control and the dangers posed by drugs.
7. Agree to support the Mekong River Safety Project to prevent the movement of drugs and chemicals into the production area.
