Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign, December 6: 785 illegal vehicles were found and 446 fines were imposed.
(Phnom Penh): The nationwide traffic law enforcement campaign for December 6, 2018, the traffic police force inspected 3,712 vehicles and found 785 vehicles violating the law (72% motorcycles), 339 education vehicles and 446 fines. This is according to the official report of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department of the General Commission of the National Police.
According to the report, 2,382 helmets and goggles were inspected on December 6, 147 education helmets and 312 helmets were fined.
The owner of the "9-storey waterfall" resort in Chhouk district, Kampot province, which belongs to a military officer, got into a dispute with his wife, fired several shots and set fire to many houses and bungalows.
(Kampot): A military officer named Am Phallin was reportedly shot several times and set fire to his "9-storey waterfall" resort in Anlong Kmengleang village, Techo Aphivath commune, Chhuk district, Kampot province last night. December 5, 2018, suspected of having a wife dispute.
According to military officials, Am Phallin set fire to his "9-storey waterfall" resort, setting fire to eight guest houses, one villa, one meeting hall, one kitchen, two restaurants, 25 cafes and more. A large number of materials in the resort directly above.
In addition to setting fire to his resort, Am Phallin, who works in the administration of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, also fired several shots before fleeing.
In this case, Mr. Amphallin's wife also filed a complaint to the Kampot Provincial Military Command, detailing the incident.
