JICA Collaborates with General Department of Taxation to Create Video on Tax Benefits to Educate Cambodian Students on Understanding Tax Payment
(Phnom Penh): The Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) in collaboration with the General Department of Taxation has produced a video on the benefits of paying taxes to Cambodian students. In fact, JICA and the General Department of Taxation have organized this program in many universities in Cambodia and plan to continue to disseminate in the provinces as well.
On the morning of December 6, 2018, JICA and the General Department of Taxation organized a program to share this educational video to students in the University of Human Resources, with many students participating.
This video on taxes in Cambodia is the first between JICA and the General Department of Taxation, and was created to introduce the importance and benefits of taxes to Cambodians from young to old.
"I think it is important to expand our knowledge of the tax sector, but it is also difficult to make taxpayers aware of the tax sector," said Muto Shizuki, chief adviser and official from the General Department of Taxation In the short term.
He added that this educational video program is to strengthen the education sector in the field of taxation. The program will be held at 27 universities in Cambodia and is a first step for Cambodia in raising awareness about the tax sector.
The Deputy Director General of the University of Human Resources expressed his happiness that JICA and the General Department of Taxation shared knowledge with the students of the University of Human Resources.
He added that at present, students do not yet fully understand the issue of paying taxes, which is the best way that both partners have contributed to the completion of knowledge to students at this university. After watching this video, hopefully students will have a better understanding of the tax sector.
Please be informed that according to the project, JICA and the General Department of Taxation will publish this video in 27 universities in Cambodia. Cambodia, Laos, Vietnam hold 17th trilateral ministerial meeting on drug control cooperation
