(Battambang): Mr. Hoeung Sokun, Deputy Governor of Battambang Province, led a joint working group to burn more than 3,228 kg of expired and damaged goods after the professional officers of Camcontrol branch confiscated in the markets in the province.
In fact, on the morning of December 6, 2018, the joint team inspected with the officials of the Laboratory Department, brought the mobile laboratory vehicle of the General Department of CamControl to inspect at the Central Market 5 kg and held a ceremony to burn the damaged goods. This quality took place this afternoon in Anlong Vil commune, Sangke district, Battambang province.
Mr. Hak Sokrin, President of Camcontrol Battambang Branch, said that some time ago, professional officers inspected the markets and border gates in Battambang province and found out-of-date and damaged goods. Come and keep it at the provincial branch, waiting for the decision to burn it.
Mr. Hak Sokrin stated that while storing more than 3 tons of defective goods, this morning, Battambang Provincial CamControl officials, in cooperation with the Provincial Department of Commerce, the Market Commission and the Laboratory Department, brought the General Laboratory mobile vehicle. The CamControl Department inspected the quality of goods at Battambang Central Market (Nat Market), Battambang Municipality, Battambang Province with the participation of Mr. Hoeung Sokun.
During the activity, the officers inspected food and groceries and took 67 samples, including: vegetables, fruits, trout, meatballs, fish, chicken blood, noodles, pickles, all kinds of seafood, blueberries, lentils and dumplings. To test for banned chemicals that can harm the health of consumers, experts found the presence of boracic acid in 2 kg of dumplings, 3 kg of dandruff.
During the inspection, the professional officers also confiscated 5 kg of dumplings and dried lentils and instructed the traders to understand how to choose safe products to sell as well as to eat. .
