Cambodia needs 200 blocks of blood a day! National Blood Transfusion Center Calls on People to Donate Blood, Cho Ray Hospital Phnom Penh also has a service to receive blood donors
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia needs about 200 blood transfusions a day to rescue people in hospitals across the country, which is why the National Blood Transfusion Center in collaboration with Choray Hospital Phnom Penh organizes a large humanitarian program. Under the message "Call to donate blood to save lives" to receive blood donations from citizens and volunteer government officials.
The above-mentioned voluntary blood donation program was held at Choray Hospital, Phnom Penh, located along National Road 1, Kdei Takuy Village, Sangkat Niroth, Khan Chbar Ampov, Phnom Penh from December 6. This year 2018 onwards.
At the opening of the above humanitarian program, Mr. Ou Sokleang, Education Officer for Blood Donor of the National Blood Transfusion Center, said that the blood problem is not a problem of the Ministry of Health or the National Blood Transfusion Center, it is all a problem. People, especially officials of ministries and institutions, donate blood to save lives.
"Currently, the demand for blood is high, with 200 units of blood needed per day," he said. "Even if the mobile team of the National Blood Transfusion Center collects blood, it is still not enough."
He added that now, although the National Blood Transfusion Center does not find enough blood to save, the families of patients in need of blood have contributed a lot, so the accusation of blood transfusions no longer exists. He said that each year, the National Blood Transfusion Center organizes two major campaigns, on February 14 and June 14.
On that occasion, Mr. Phan Sokha, Finance Director of Cho Ray Hospital in Phnom Penh, said that Cho Ray Hospital in Phnom Penh organizes blood donation program twice a year. This is the fifth time that Cho Ray Hospital has organized a blood donation program, the first time with 60 participants, the second time with 70 people, the third time with 80 people and the fourth time with more than 100 people. The blood donors were the staff of Choray Hospital, Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh and Sokimex.
He also called on people to volunteer to donate blood to save lives, because a block of blood can save a patient and a victim. This blood donation does not affect the body and health, but instead helps to be healthy.
