Kratie Provincial Department of Land Management Holds a Dissemination Workshop on Commune / Sangkat Land Use Planning 2018
(Kratie): The Department of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction of Kratie Province on the morning of December 6, 2018 organized a workshop on Land Use Planning in Commune / Sangkat Properly and Provide Maximum Benefit to the National Society. In accordance with the previous legal principles, the land management strategy has been focused on measures to strengthen the management system and eliminate anarchy in land tenure.
The workshop was chaired by Mr. Khan Chamnan, Deputy Governor of Kratie Province, with the support of WWF and the participation of development partners throughout the province, Mr. and Mrs. Both teachers and students in large numbers.
Dr. Kao Madilen, Director of Kratie Provincial Department of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, said that the department has conducted systematic land registration in Kratie City and Chit Borei District to reduce land disputes and ensure the security of land tenure. Out-of-court land in collaboration with the Land Dispute Resolution Team of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction.
During the opening ceremony, Mr. Khan Chamnan, Deputy Governor, said, "This workshop is an opportunity for all of us to get a long-term vision of the Royal Government in the field of environment, management and conservation of natural resources. "It is managed, maintained and protected in an environmentally and sustainable manner to help reduce conflict and poverty in Cambodia."
He added that the land use planning is based on the principle of local ownership, as well as overseeing the planning process with the participation of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, as well as the Provincial Department of Land Management, including the working group. Inter-ministerial participation in land use planning as stated in the guidelines.
Currently, the Kratie Provincial Land Management Department is preparing the process of land use planning in two communes, namely: Chroy Banteay commune in Prek Prosop district and O'Kreang commune in Sambo district, Kratie province, with the support of the Bel government. ZIC through the Global Fund for the Conservation of Natural Resources in Cambodia, also known as WWF-Cambodia.
