(Vientiane): Laos has expressed its expectation to sell 14,600 megawatts of electricity by 2030, while currently exporting 4,415 megawatts to five neighboring countries. This was quoted from the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Thursday afternoon, December 6, 2018.
Laos is also selling more than 300 megawatts of electricity to Vietnam, and the Lao government expects to increase its supply to 1,000 megawatts by 2020 and 5,000 megawatts by 2030. In addition, Laos plans to sell 100 megawatts of electricity to Malaysia via Thailand, and the Lao government expects to sell another 300 megawatts by 2020.
The Lao government will also sell 10 megawatts of electricity to Cambodia and expect to sell an additional 200 megawatts by 2020. Myanmar has bought 5 megawatts of electricity from Laos and will sell another 100 megawatts by 2022 as the two governments sign a cooperation agreement on energy sales.
The Lao government has also signed an agreement with China for cooperation on the construction of a transmission line, with both sides currently studying technical and economic feasibility, which is expected to be completed next year. 2019. Preah Vihear CamControl Officers Continue to Educate Teachers on Food Safety in Choam Ksan District
