(Phnom Penh): Cambodia-Indonesia has pushed for increased air connectivity and encouraged airline operators to operate direct flights between the two countries. This is according to the press release of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, which was received by Fresh News on December 6, 2018.
According to the press release, Mr. Prak Sokhon, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, led a delegation to attend and co-chair the first meeting of the Joint Commission for Bilateral Cooperation between Cambodia and Indonesia. 4, which took place on December 4, 2018 in Jakarta, Indonesia.
During the fourth meeting of the Joint Commission for Bilateral Cooperation, the two sides agreed that the 60th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between Cambodia and Indonesia in 2019 will be an important event. In enhancing bilateral cooperation between the two countries. Both sides welcomed a number of joint action plans to celebrate this solemn event.
Noting this positive trend, the Indonesian side agreed to continue to encourage more investors to invest in Cambodia. The meeting agreed to further facilitate trade in agricultural products and expedite discussions on a memorandum of understanding on agricultural cooperation.
The two sides also encouraged relevant institutions to review the Memorandum of Understanding on Tourism Cooperation signed in 1999 and welcomed the initiative to expand cooperation to promote a common cultural landscape between Cambodia and Cambodia. Indonesia. In addition, the meeting also encouraged the renewal of the Memorandum of Understanding on Cultural Cooperation, which will expire on February 26, 2019.
According to the press release, the two sides agreed to hold the 5th Joint Commission Meeting for Cambodia-Indonesia Bilateral Cooperation in 2020 in Cambodia. At the end of the fourth meeting of the Joint Commission for Bilateral Cooperation, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon and Ms. Reth Noel P. Mar Soudi also signed a memorandum on the outcome of the meeting.
