Deputy Prime Minister Binh Chin: More than 60,000 students with disabilities and more than 1,000 disabled education staff study and work without discrimination
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Binh Chin, Minister of the Office of the Council of Ministers, said that a total of 60,610 students with disabilities of all kinds and 1,252 educators with disabilities have been studying at all levels and working without Discrimination.
The Deputy Prime Minister said this morning, December 6, 2018, on the occasion of presiding over the celebration of the 20th Cambodian Day of Persons with Disabilities and the 36th International Day of Persons with Disabilities in 2018 under the theme "Promoting the Rights of Persons with Disabilities, Ensuring Environment and Equality" was held solemnly at the Koh Pich Theater.
Deputy Prime Minister Binh Chin said that the Royal Government recognizes the rights of persons with disabilities and their families and always considers the provision of land ownership to disabled soldiers in the 317 Taken Development Area in Taken, Koh Sla, Kampot Province. In Kulen district, Siem Reap province, and in Phnom Chhat, Banteay Meanchey province, for the construction of housing, business and family farming, as well as providing better rehabilitation services in the community.
He added that a total of 60,610 students with disabilities of all kinds were studying at all levels without discrimination, and 1,252 education staff with disabilities, 342 of whom were female. In addition, 1,433 blind and deaf students are studying in special education, integration classes, basic education classes, non-formal education classes of Krousar Thmey Deaf Development Program.
At the same time, 8,200 school buildings have provided ramps for students with disabilities in both rural and urban areas, making it easier for students with disabilities to access higher education. Young people with disabilities are also encouraged to participate in global competitions with young people with disabilities in the region and in the world, as well as bring medals that are an honor for the nation and society as a whole.
Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, said that through the efforts of the Royal Government of Cambodia, many tasks have been achieved, including:
2: Provided a policy for people with disabilities in the community. Currently, people with disabilities in 7 provinces: Kandal, Tbong Khmum, Prey Veng, Svay Rieng, Kampong Cham, Pailin and Battambang, a total of 10,353 people with disabilities received social cards. And policy support budget. 2,412 people with disabilities have received health care policies for the disabled.
3: Continue to sustain the rehabilitation services for people with disabilities. Every year, about 28,000 people with disabilities receive free rehabilitation services of all kinds. This service responds to the needs of people with disabilities in both quantity and quality.
4: Collaborated with the Cambodian Veterans Association to build houses for hundreds of disabled veterans in the community and is implementing a policy on granting social land concessions to the Armed Forces, retirees, the disabled and thousands of families. Both have increased food rations for veterans and disabled soldiers.
