The celebration of the 25th anniversary of the establishment of the International Committee for the Coordination of Protection and Development of Angkor (ICC-Angkor) was officially opened on the morning of December 4, 2018 under the presidency Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
In the ceremony, which was attended by many national and international guests, the King of Cambodia called for the participation of all national and international circles, especially the youth as a successor to the conservation and development of heritage. He considered it an endless work.
His Majesty King Bhumibol Adulyadej reminded that Angkor was inscribed on the UNESCO World Heritage List on December 14, 1992, under the auspices of His Majesty King Bhumibol Adulyadej, who appealed to UNESCO for help. Angkor.
In response to this call, an international conference was held in Tokyo on 12 and 13 October 1993 under the initiative of the Government of Japan, with the support of France and UNESCO. Action plans for the conservation and development of Angkor. To achieve this goal, the International Coordinating Committee (ICC-Angkor) was established in December 1993.
Past successes have also demonstrated the correct implementation of the Royal Government of Cambodia's national cultural policy under the skillful and wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, who has always taken great care of it. Protect, preserve and develop national cultural heritage. This is the King's speech.
In addition, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni also expressed special gratitude to France and Japan, which for the past 25 years, as co-chairs, have chaired the plenary and technical meetings in spirit. Responsible for contributing greatly to the success of ICC-Angkor.
He also expressed his hope that the ICC-Angkor will continue to function well, fulfill its duties and achieve great success in the work of conserving and developing the Angkor historical site and other relevant cultural and natural heritage for the benefit of the people. Together, the motherland and the people of Cambodia.
* To celebrate the success of the ICC Angkor mechanism, which is now a model of conservation and development for countries around the world.
* To show the national pride of the Kingdom of Cambodia, which is a cultural power and has a long history, as well as to promote the value of heritage
* To express gratitude and appreciation to the heroes, dignitaries and ancestors of all generations who have dedicated their bodies and minds to building, preserving, protecting and preserving cultural heritage.
* To cultivate the spirit of the youth and the people of Cambodia to love, participate in preserving, protecting and promoting the cultural heritage, traditions and customs of Cambodia.
* To show the achievements of the Royal Government of Cambodia in the field of heritage under the leadership of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia
* To promote the potential of culture and tourism to the international arena.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, told the media on December 6, 2018 that a study to prepare this proposal can only be done if the amendment of the law takes effect. At the same time, Samdech revealed that those who need to be examined must abide by the court's verdict.
The proposed law on the amendment of the law on political parties was prepared by 87 deputies, amending the new Article 45 (duplicate) of the Law on Political Parties. The draft law was sent to the National Assembly's Sixth Committee for study and review on December 5, 2018, before being submitted to the National Assembly's plenary session soon.
The proposed law adds a new paragraph in the new Article 45 (duplicate) so that the Prime Minister has the right to propose to the King at the request of the Minister of Interior to rehabilitate those whose court has banned him from engaging in politics. Re-engage in full-fledged politics.
Interior Ministry spokesman General Khieu Sopheak warned that once the law came into force, anyone who was barred from engaging in political activity but still violated a Supreme Court ruling would not be on the list.
He said: "Whoever follows the verdict of the Supreme Court, which prohibits the right to do politics, he will be on the list of the Royal Government to ask the King to give the right to do politics. "Separately, anyone who has violated and still violates this verdict can not be on the list."
However, neither Sar Kheng nor a spokesman for the Ministry of Interior disclosed on the review of Kem Sokha's political rights, as he is currently under investigation. The court is still different from some of the former CNRP leaders.
Mr. Kem Sokha was released on bail in the early hours of September 10, 2018 and placed under judicial supervision due to his health problems after being detained in prison. Trapeang Phlong (M3) for more than a year.
