After arriving at the airport, his items were taken from the airport to some streets in Siem Reap before heading to Kantha Bopha Hospital in Siem Reap, where his items were to be stored. On the streets, many government officials, students, and citizens were seen standing on either side of the road, mourning and paying their respects to his soul.
It should be reminded that Dr. Richner passed away on September 9, 2018 recently in his home country. After sacrificing for the cause of children and mothers in Cambodia for about 25 years, the doctor reluctantly left Cambodia in March 2017.
General Nem Sovath Holds a Press Conference on the Concept of Win-Win Monument
(Phnom Penh): With only 23 days left until the inauguration of the Victory Day on December 6, 2018, General Nem Sovath, Chairman of the Win-Win Monument Research and Research Team, organized a press conference on the concept of the construction of the monument. Win-Win is located in Sangkat Bak Kheng, Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh.
At the same time, Samdech Picheay Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, often leads a team of non-stop inspections to ensure that this monument, which is a symbol of peace, unites the Khmer nation, is fully constructed and On time of the celebration as scheduled by the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The construction of this win-win monument started in February 2016 on an area of 8 hectares in Chroy Changva district, Phnom Penh. This win-win monument is also a symbol of the peace that Cambodia has achieved after the end of decades of civil war.
Recently, the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, publicly announced that Samdech will hold a New Year celebration for 3 nights and 3 days from December 29 to 31, 2018 at the Victory Monument. Win to celebrate the 20th anniversary of the end of the Cambodian civil war through a win-win policy by gaining territorial unity for the first time.
