(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, this morning, December 6, 2018, presided over the opening ceremony of the 7th Interfaith Dialogue to Strengthen Religious Harmony in Cambodia under the theme "No Religion." Drugs and respect for road traffic laws.
The ceremony was also attended by Senior Minister Him Chhem, Minister of Cults and Religions, religious leaders, Mrs. Silvan Silvati and members of Islam, Christianity and all denominations in Cambodia. The ceremony was held at the Chaktomuk Conference Hall.
Speaking on the occasion, Senior Minister Him Chhem said that the workshop was held to discuss, exchange ideas and share good experiences to help each religious community avoid drugs and cutting. Reduce traffic accidents in Cambodian society, leading to development and progress for the whole Cambodian society.
At the same time, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng emphasized that by praising the Ministry of Cults and Religions for organizing this workshop, which is an honor and prestige of religious harmony in Cambodia, such as showing the attention of the Royal Government for the freedom of religion of the people on the national and international stage.
According to Sar Kheng, the implementation of the policy of national unification brings the disciples of each religion in Cambodia closer to each other within the gaps within the observance of each religion. And increasingly connected with respect for the policy path of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Samdech Sar Kheng also stressed that he hoped that the workshop would provide an opportunity for the members of the entire event to discuss, exchange ideas and share good experiences in order to gather useful ideas and measures. Strict and appropriate to the evolution of society to contribute to the promotion of religious harmony in Cambodia.
(Laos): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, during his official visit to Laos on the afternoon of December 5, 2018, after laying a wreath at the Lao Martyrs' Memorial. Samdech met with Mrs. Paniya Toto, President of the Lao National Assembly.
During the meeting, the President of the National Assembly welcomed Samdech Techo Hun Sen to pay an official visit to Laos. She hopes that Samdech Techo's visit will make a significant contribution to building friendship and cooperation between the two countries.
On that occasion, she also congratulated Samdech Techo Prime Minister on his election as Prime Minister of the Royal Government of Cambodia and the success of the election of the Cambodian People's Party.
The National Assembly President continued that the success of the election of the Cambodian People's Party now shows the wise leadership of Samdech Techo and she is confident that Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the CPP will continue. Develop the country to be more prosperous and successful, not only Cambodia, but also contribute to the peace and prosperity of the whole region.
The National Assembly President also congratulated the outcome of the meeting between the Prime Ministers of the two countries on the morning of December 5, 2018.
In response, the Prime Minister thanked the President of the Lao National Assembly for his kind words. Samdech informed the President of the Lao National Assembly that this election in Cambodia was held in a free and democratic manner with more than 83% of the population going to the polls, which is a higher percentage than the previous election.
Samdech Techo said that this success came because the people supported the CPP, more than 77% of the votes cast for the CPP out of 20 parties that participated in the election.
The Prime Minister also informed the National Assembly President about the outcome of the talks between the Prime Minister and the Prime Minister of Laos regarding the connection of hydropower, the bridge from Champasak to Preah Vihear, which is the connection between the people. And the people.
The Lao National Assembly President considered the success of today's meeting as important to further promote bilateral cooperation between the two countries. She wants the prime ministers of the two countries to work closely together to better resolve issues between the two countries.
