Minister Mam Bunheng: The Ministry of Health and Stakeholders Will Introduce Potential New Strategies to Prevent Antibiotic Resistance
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Health, Professor Mam Bunheng, said that the whole world, as well as Cambodia, is currently facing many new public health problems, especially the increase in immunity to viruses and antibiotics. A type of medicine that is widely used in humans and in agriculture and food.
He stressed that the Ministry of Health, through the National Institute of Public Health, in collaboration with relevant national and international partners, has regularly and actively carried out scientific evidence gathering and research findings to develop new policies for the country. Cambodia by examining various potential strategies to prevent resistance to this antibiotic.
This statement was made by Minister Mam Bunheng at the opening of the 59th International Conference on "Antibiotic Resistance" with the participation of nearly 300 national and international partners at the Cambodiana Hotel.
"Today's conference really responds to the real needs of Cambodia, especially as the Ministry of Health has been actively responding to the problem of resistance to pesticides by strengthening quality control," he said. "Imports of drugs into Cambodia, raising awareness of the use of pesticides in the health, agriculture and food sectors, and developing programs to promote the proper and effective use of pesticides."
Step by step, the Ministry of Health will begin to strengthen the record of medicines used as part of the work to improve the quality of health services. At the same time, the Ministry has been drafting a law on the management of health services, which will focus on quality assurance and control of health services, including the sale and use of medicines.
