Cambodian PM plans to distribute tens of thousands of books to readers
(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, plans to distribute tens of thousands of books at the annual National Book Fair at the National Library this weekend.
Three books with different titles, published almost 100 years ago, were re-edited: Srey Hitop Tes, Kram Ngoy, and Ou Chong. These three books will be distributed to those who like to read books from December 7-9, 2018.
Mr. Dy Vichea, Acting President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, who organized the distribution of the three books, said, "Samdech Akka Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen is a leader who likes to read, like to listen to the radio and watch TV up to 4 times. Only one. ”
Mr. Dy Vichea continued that the distribution of these books is a good intention of Samdech Techo to promote and promote the field of reading in Cambodia to revive throughout the country.
In particular, the book Srey Hitop Tes is rich in many perspectives that lead to all kinds of reflection as well as education. In one passage it is written, "When a person has little knowledge, when he loses his property, all other things perish, such as a river with little water, when summer comes, it dries up."
This year's National Book Fair is themed: "Books for Living Knowledge". Therefore, let all book lovers gain more knowledge, more energy, both physically and mentally, and more potential in all matters, including wealth.
Book lovers will go to the zodiac at the end of 2018
(Phnom Penh): Book lovers will rise to the zodiac at the end of 2018 because tens of thousands of books will be provided free of charge. Kram Ngoy, Ou Chong, and Srey Hitop Tes, all of which are educational books, both physical and mental, counseling, teaching, aids in moral education, and a collection of good ideas, will be distributed to all people who enjoy reading. Books at the National Book Fair from December 7-9.
Mr. Dy Vichea, Acting President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia (UYFC), who organized the distribution of the three books above, said, "The distribution of these books is a good intention of Samdech Akka Sena Padei Techo Hun. "Sen to promote and promote the field of reading in Cambodia to revitalize because he wants the Cambodian people to have a broader and deeper knowledge to help build and develop Cambodia to grow even stronger."
Mr. Dy Vichea expressed the expectation that the people who receive all the books when they return home will have more knowledge and hope that there will be better opportunities to do all kinds of work for the next year, because these books can As a capital to help change attitudes and thoughts that lead to progress in family life.
Hok Sothy, director of Sipar Cambodia and president of the Cambodian Library Association, said: “No leader has ever distributed a book to a reader for free. "This is the first time in the history of Cambodia that leaders have shown great will to promote reading, a treasure trove of inexhaustible knowledge."
At the end of 2017, there were 51,000 participants in the book fair, and it is hoped that in 2018, no less than 50,000 participants will be destined to receive book donations from the Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia. A lucky gift before the new year.
