Cambodian Derivatives Exchange Co., Ltd. Continues to Participate in Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia Workshop in 5 More Provinces
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Derivatives Exchange Company has continued to participate in the 2018 Provincial Workshop of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia on December 4, 2018. Kampong Cham is the second of five destinations, while the first is Sihanoukville, which was completed last week.
The workshop covered the topic of “Derivatives Business in Cambodia” and aims to promote and expand awareness of derivatives investment throughout Cambodia, build investor confidence and provide investors with the necessary skills and strategies for derivatives. Invest this one.
The provinces where the seminar will be held are Siem Reap, Banteay Meanchey and Battambang, all of which are considered to have high potential due to their population, investment history and living standards.
Mr. Sou Socheat, Director General of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, reaffirmed his commitment to promoting derivatives trading everywhere in Cambodia and to facilitate the growth of the legal market.
He also encouraged brokerage firms to publicize investor protection policies as well as hedging methods.
Mr. Yun Sovannara, Deputy Director of the Derivatives Business Management and Investment Management Business Office of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, gave an overview of the derivatives market and the progress of derivatives trading in Cambodia, the regulatory framework, challenges and plans of the Board. Securities Commission to further develop the derivatives sector.
Through the Company's participation in all events of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia and its high commitment to raising the standards of the Cambodian financial markets in line with international standards, Cambodian Derivatives Exchange provides a clear example of professionalism. Real and has driven various derivatives companies to compete positively.
Mr. Lawrence Kook, Governor of Cambodian Derivatives Exchange, was pleased to attend the 2018 Provincial Workshop with the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia. He stressed that raising awareness of trading in financial instruments is one of the main tasks of Cambodian Derivatives Exchange.
"The derivatives market in Cambodia is moving towards its full potential," Lawrence added. Brokers from countries such as Japan, China and Vietnam have joined the company and under the leadership of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, Cambodian Derivatives Exchange has brought the Cambodian derivatives market to the international stage. .
Please note that this workshop ended successfully with nearly 200 participants, each of them expressed interest in investing in derivatives, a sign of the bright future of the derivatives industry in Cambodia. .
