A student riding a motorbike at high speed hit a Samsung car in front of him, causing his sudden death in Dangkor district
(Phnom Penh): A young man broke his head and died in a pool of blood while riding a motorbike at high speed and hit the head of a Samsung car that was crossing the road at the point of concrete road, Phum Phea, Sangkat Preah Lang, Khan Dangkor, Phnom Penh on the afternoon of December 5. 2018.
According to the police, the body of Bonat Sophanit, a 15-year-old male student, was found near the scene, while the car was driven by Leng Vibol, a 23-year-old male resident of Ang village, Preah Lang commune, Dangkor district.
Currently, the local police have cooperated with the professional police to measure and drag cars and motorcycles to be stored at the Office of Land Traffic of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, waiting for a legal solution. The body was handed over to the family to be taken to the traditional ceremony.
