Phnom Penh court begins trial against Belgian cross-border drug trafficker
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of December 5, 2018, the Phnom Penh Municipal Court took up the case of a Belgian national who was a ringleader of a drug trafficking ring after he filed a lawsuit. Opposing the verdict that the court had sentenced to life imprisonment in the past.
The trial was presided over by Mr. Chhim Rithy, President of the Trial Chamber, and Mr. Top Chhun Long, Prosecutor.
However, the Prosecutor's Office will continue to uphold the charges and the hearing in this case will be decided by the President of the Trial Chamber to announce the verdict on December 19, 2018.
Please be reminded that this cross-border drug trafficker was searched and arrested by the specialized force of the General Department of Immigration in cooperation with the specialized force of the Anti-Drug Department (A1) at the exit point of Bavet International Gate. Located in Bavet Kandal Village, Sangkat-Bavet City, Svay Rieng Province on the evening of October 4, 2018.
He was sentenced in absentia to life in prison and fined 80 million riels in connection with a case of illegal cross-border drug trafficking by air from Brazil via Ethiopia-Thailand to Cambodia. The police cracked down on January 10, 2018 at the arrival of passengers.
For the last 25 years of his life, Dr. Beth Richner has sacrificed everything on Cambodian territory for the sake of Cambodian children, for the sake of Cambodian citizens. The sacrifice of the doctor or the angel of salvation, which is a nickname given by the Cambodian people, is considered a great sacrifice, rarely anyone can do like him.
When asked if there is a reason why the doctor put his life only for Cambodian children? Most doctors agree that "Cambodian love comes from the heart, sincere love for Cambodians, love without hypocrisy, love is useless" is a factor that leads doctors to sacrifice without remorse. Compassion for Cambodian children and women for the past 25 years.
Loyal love, love without tricks, love does not require a doctor's retaliation, is larger and deeper than the ocean, no meter can measure.
During his 25-year mission to save the lives of Cambodian children, the doctor sought to raise no less than $ 600 million, but he did not embezzle these funds for his life, all of which were for teachers' salaries. Doctors and staff, almost all of whom are Cambodian, and only for medical equipment for the treatment of Cambodian children.
Returning to his home country at the insistence of his sister, when he became seriously ill, the doctor returned with only a leather bag, which he had taken with him when he came to Cambodia in 1991.
While still alive, he sacrificed his physical, mental, and intellectual strength only for Cambodian children. Who can measure the depth and extent of this Swiss love for the nation, the people and the territory of Cambodia?
Although the doctor's body has left Cambodia, his good deeds, his priceless virtues continue to be immortal, still engraved in the hearts of Cambodian children. May the heart of Dr.'s husband and wife be deeply ingrained in the hearts and minds of Cambodian children, all citizens, to love the Cambodian nation together, to build good deeds, to build sharing in society, to bring Cambodian society to a harmonious society.
(Phnom Penh): Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign For December 05, 2018, the traffic police force inspected 3,801 vehicles and found 779 vehicles violating the law (68% motorcycles), 322 education vehicles and 457 fines. This is according to the official report of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department of the General Commission of the National Police.
