(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian pepper sector is expected to have a clear market stability after the Cambodian Pepper and Spices Association, together with the President of CIRD and the Ministry of Commerce, held a meeting to discuss the pepper policy in Cambodia to promote Export of Cambodian pepper.
A workshop on policy decisions in Cambodia was organized with the participation of Mr. Mao Thora, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce, Mr. Song Saran, Representative of the Cambodian Pepper and Spices Association, Mr. Prak Sereyvath, President of CIRD, organized on December 5, 2018.
Mr. Song Saran said that the consultation on pepper policy in Cambodia reflects the problems that have arisen, and this meeting provided an opportunity to discuss in formulating a strategy on the challenges of increasing pepper exports to the international market. As well as improving the quality of Cambodian pepper.
He added that as you all know that Cambodian pepper is a delicious pepper, high quality and get a lot of support from customers, but it is unfortunate that Cambodian pepper has not been exported much yet. There are only two exporting countries: Vietnam and Thailand.
"Today's meeting is for the Ministry of Commerce and the association to develop a strategy to boost official pepper exports," he said.
Mr. Mao Thora said that before entering into the policy for the first time, there must be development first and support each other to be stable in order to be integrated into the policy of the Royal Government, and this policy will be submitted as a set to be submitted to the Prime Minister. After the approval of the Prime Minister, there are many people who recognize and it is easy to find a partner.
He added that after receiving this policy, both business partners and the Ministry of Commerce will be responsible for this work.
