Guangxi is one of the largest banana growing areas in China. At a 300-hectare banana farm, only one person and one mobile app is needed to manage the entire farm. It was impossible in the past.
The team behind the software incorporates state-of-the-art technology and features motion sensors or sensors, as well as intelligent space storage or cloud storage, to make the software written more versatile.
This technology makes it possible to grow crops precisely, saving energy and other resources.
About 33,000 hectares of farms in Guangxi are using the technology. Precise planting methods reduce pollution by reducing the time that gardeners have to spend on crop inspections and by ensuring that each crop receives the nutrients and nutrients it needs properly. As a result, the crop has a better quality.
