Rinnai Kitchen Equipment Supplier Shows Support and Growth in Sales in Cambodian Market
(Phnom Penh): Currently, the business of supplying kitchen equipment seems to be growing rapidly, the increase is due to the opening of shops as well as many restaurants in Cambodia. In fact, to meet these needs, Rinnai, a leading supplier of kitchen equipment and the number one product imported from Japan, has introduced and introduced a new range of stoves and water heaters.
With the demonstration of this new series of stoves and water heaters, Rinnai also organized a party for the loyal customers. Please be informed that Rinnai Japan has cooperated with Camcona Trading Cambodia to have the right to import and distribute products from Rinnai.
Rin Nai currently sells its products in more than 80 countries and has 17 subsidiaries. In fact, in Japan, Rinnai ranks first as the largest market share in the production of gas appliances.
In foreign markets, Rinnai also has the largest market share in the United States, Australia, New Zealand and Brazil on gas water heaters.
Kim Srun Elida, CEO of Camcona Trading, said, "Camcona has been in business with Rinnai for more than six years and this year has expanded its distribution of stoves and fume hoods."
She continued, "Sales of Rinnai products from year to year have been growing steadily. The increase from Rinnai products is good, high quality and popular in Cambodia for this year. An increase of up to 25 percent.
She added that Rinnai products are popular and quickly supported by customers and consumers because of Rinnai's high quality, modern technology, innovative quality, durable, safe, economical. Power, stylish design and good service.
She stated that for this new product, there will be as much support from customers as the previous products.
China vehemently opposes idea of turning INF nuclear treaty into multilateral treaty
BEIJING (Reuters) - The Beijing government, through a Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesman, on Wednesday strongly condemned the idea of turning the INF nuclear non-proliferation treaty between the United States and Russia into a multilateral treaty. This is according to a quote from the Russian newspaper Sputnik on Wednesday evening, December 5, 2018.
The Chinese's protests came after US President Donald Trump said in October that China should be part of the INF treaty. Russia's ambassador to the United States later suggested that not only Beijing but even NATO, especially France and Britain, should be included in the treaty.
Trump has announced his intention to withdraw his country from the INF, citing allegations that Russia has violated the treaty, while Moscow has repeatedly argued that the allegations are baseless. Either way, it is concerned about Washington's compliance with the treaty.
