It should be noted that the Royal Government of Cambodia, through the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, on December 3, 2018, issued an important statement to ease the situation of opposition politicians who were banned by the court in the past, as well as to facilitate Foreign media in Cambodia, civil society organizations and unions.
A government statement said the National Assembly was studying to lift the political ban on politically-convicted politicians, paving the way for 118 former CNRP leaders to return to politics. The government has also called on the court to expedite the proceedings of individuals who have filed lawsuits or are being prosecuted in accordance with the procedures to protect their constitutional rights.
