This is according to the report of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Preah Vihear Province on the occasion that the Provincial Department of Agriculture and the Fruit and Vegetable Project (Chen) held its annual meeting in collaboration with the four provincial partners, including: Preah Vihear, Kratie, Stung Treng and Oddar Meanchey. Like many other organizations and suppliers of agricultural equipment on the afternoon of December 4, 2018.
Mr. Peng Trida, Director of Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said that the department has cooperated with the Cambodian Fruit and Vegetable Project (CHEN) by implementing in 6 target districts, 30 communes and 42 villages.
He said that in 2018, the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Preah Vihear Province has a total of 61 groups of farmers, including 6 groups of vegetable growers, 30 groups of semi-professional vegetable growers and 25 groups of vegetable growers. As of November 2018, 1,525 farmers have benefited from this project.
Mr. Peng Trida said that at the same time, 17 new groups were recruited, including training on vegetable gardening and vegetable growing techniques.
At the same time, the Department of Agriculture continues to provide technical support and market linkages, and has technical officers to support new pests and diseases, new techniques, and strengthen the capacity to train as needed and implement practical solutions to increase their productivity.
In addition, it has played an important role in helping farmers in the target group in order to promote new technologies such as the use of drip irrigation systems, netting, selection of resistant varieties to achieve high yields to meet market demand.
Please note that this annual meeting aims to share the reflective and reflective progress of partners in the 2018 project, as well as to validate the plan to respond to the project results in 2019, especially to strengthen cooperation. And the relationship between project implementation partners.
