The following is the press release of the Cambodian People's Party:
Experts continue to worry about media coverage hurting women's reputations
(Phnom Penh): Experts in Cambodia have continued to express concern over a number of advertisements in the media that could tarnish the image of women.
This concern was expressed during a meeting with the media and gender mainstreaming under the theme: Implementing the Code of Conduct for Reporting Violence Against Women on the morning of December 4, 2018 at the Phnom Penh Hotel. By the Ministry of Women's Affairs.
Pen Ravi, a representative of the United Nations Development Program (UNDP), said that the media can be a double-edged sword, but sometimes careless when writing. Or post pictures, name, identification of the victim as a woman, but seriously affect the reputation of the victim.
According to the United Nations Office on Drugs and Crime, 34% of the world's women and girls were killed at the hands of their partners, 21%. Killed by his family members and 41% by others.
She added that the media is the eyes, the ears and the message of society, and that the media plays an important role in preventing violence. In this regard, she urged journalists to participate in disseminating information to scare people, which reduces the rate of violence.
According to her, the involvement of the media that can help society has two parts: to spread information related to violence and to participate in education on violence, that is, journalists must try to spread information to the perpetrators. That this is an illegal act, an act that society hates.
For the Executive Director of the Club of Cambodian Journalists, Mr. Chhay Sophal insisted that all journalists should not use obscene words to write news, especially writing that discriminates against women.
According to Chhay Sophal, the use of inappropriate words to attract the attention of readers, such as prostitutes, prostitutes, traitors, etc., seriously affects the dignity of women and human rights.
Mr. Chhay Sophal also emphasized that the words related to professional ethics of journalism for cases of rape and violence, journalists must not appear or identify the victims. He said that doing so would make the woman more vulnerable and if the court or the authorities do not find justice for her, it will damage her reputation to some extent.
Article 7, meanwhile, states that reporting must respect the privacy, dignity and safety of victims, regardless of the source of the video or information.
Before concluding the program, the meeting addressed some case studies that led to the decision that journalists should write more clearly in order to benefit women victims of violence by:
1: Must highlight the information by entering the legal content.
2. Encourage women victims to have the courage to report violence that occurs to them.
3: Do not reveal the identity of the victim.
4: Participate in sharing information more widely.
Mr. Hun Many just got off the plane to China and immediately met with Cambodian students
(Beijing): Soon after arriving in Beijing, Mr. Hun Many and the Cambodian delegation rushed to meet with 168 Cambodian students representing Cambodian students from all over the country who are studying in the People's Republic of China under the "Khmer Spirit". Missing Khmer.
On the occasion of meeting in a happy and friendly atmosphere with Cambodian families, Mr. HUN Many, President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, instructed the youth to take care of the opportunity to seek knowledge and increase activities from education. This is to return to participate in the development of the country to grow even more in the growing priority areas, as you are already learning.
Chea Sreyly, president of the Cambodian Students Association in China, said there were 1,640 Cambodian students studying in China, including 495 women. In addition to studying, Cambodian students participate in activities to promote arts, sports and programs to promote potential achievements and products and further expand Cambodia's prestige.
Please be informed that 98 delegates from the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia paid a friendly visit to Beijing for 5 days at the invitation of the Youth Federation of China on the occasion of celebrating the 60th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between Cambodia and Cambodia. China.
Cambodia-Malaysia Association Signs Memorandum of Understanding on the Welfare and Protection of Cambodian Workers in Malaysia
The Memorandum of Understanding between Cambodia and Malaysia was presided over by Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training at the Ministry of Labor on December 5, 2018.
The purpose of this Memorandum of Understanding is to establish cooperation between the five associations in order to promote the rights, welfare and protection of Cambodian migrant workers working in Malaysia. In addition, the MoU is also a new mechanism in action to increase the benefits for Cambodian migrant workers going to work in Malaysia.
Reopening of Recruitment and Sending of Workers to Malaysia After the Royal Government of Cambodia suspended the recruitment and sending of Cambodian workers abroad, the Royal Government of Cambodia has established various mechanisms and legal standards for the protection, management and Promote the rights of all Cambodian workers living and working in Malaysia.
It should be noted that at present, there are 103 Cambodian private recruitment agencies licensed by the Ministry of Labor to recruit, train, send and manage Cambodian workers to work abroad, including 69 companies in Malaysia (as of October 2018).
Positives appear gradually after the two giants agreed to suspend the trade war, but there are still many things the world is waiting for ...
BEIJING: A 90-day moratorium on trade disputes between China and the United States is gaining international attention, with some commenting that it is not only important to help ease war tensions. Not only this trade, but also the relations between the two superpowers. This is according to a quote from the Chinese newspaper Global Times on Wednesday afternoon, December 5, 2018.
Reaching an agreement between Beijing and Washington on Saturday last week was a major development situation, apparently referring to the positive in the international stock market on Monday this week. All that remains is the thorough and honest negotiations between the two countries, but how the two sides deal with difficult obstacles depends largely on the political attitude of China and the United States itself.
The global trade war that has shaken the world has lasted for more than half a year, and for some time both China and the United States have realized the will, the core interests, as well as the strength to resist the pressure from each side. The two countries now have a common goal to start new talks in the next 90 days, a crucial period in the ceasefire agreement.
The agreement shows that both sides are well aware that they will benefit more by ending the trade war than by prolonging it. After all, it seems almost impossible to resolve major issues between the two sides in just 90 days, but 90 days of effort can build a great deal of trust and lead to A compromise that is acceptable to both parties.
In general, after more than half a year of trade war, both sides have a better understanding that neither side can achieve maximum benefits unilaterally. The two countries will have to compromise to reach a trade agreement in negotiating efforts. It is true that a trade war could escalate if China and the United States cannot reach an agreement, but the two major powers can not separate.
