(Phnom Penh): Hattha Kaksekar Microfinance Limited (HKL) has started trading its corporate bonds, known as "Cambodia's First Corporate Bond No. 1" on the Cambodia Securities Exchange.
Following the official listing on December 5, 2018, individual investors can submit a bid to buy or sell the bond through their brokerage, which is similar to the process of trading securities. This is according to the press release of the Cambodia Securities Exchange.
HKL made history by issuing the first corporate bond in Cambodia on November 14, 2018. The total size of the publication is 120 billion riels (about 30 million US dollars), with subscriptions from local and foreign institutional investors.
The launch of the bond market will provide a new source of funding for local companies and a new investment option for investors. HKL expects that the proceeds from the issuance of bonds will be used to finance the growth of the credit business, including working capital and for capital expenditures of the company.
The proceeds from the issuance of the bond will support rural micro, small and medium enterprises, including women entrepreneurs, in Cambodia.
With offices and ATM networks throughout Cambodia, HKL offers a wide range of financial products and services to a wide range of clients, including: loans, savings, local money transfers and mobile banking. As of 2017, HKL's net profit was US $ 15.36 million and total assets were US $ 691.01 million.
Sold out! The three sons of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit are mentioned in the new book published by Mr. Chhay Sophal
(Phnom Penh): The book entitled "The Three Brothers - New Blood Among the Successors" which describes the history of the three sons of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen is Released to the public on December 5, 2018, for all members of the public to learn about the social activities, the level of knowledge and ability of these three dignitaries.
Speaking to reporters at a press conference at his cafe "Book Cafe" in Sen Sok, Chhay Sophal, a professor of information and author, confirmed that he had spent five years compiling the book. He recorded the activities and words of the three brothers, Mr. Hun Manet, Mr. Hun Manit and Mr. Hun Many, as well as interviewed the three young leaders.
Mr. Chhay Sophal said that all three, as well as others, have one potential and that the public sees that all three are highly educated in the superpowers, especially the United States, which is a new blood. May have sufficient capacity to continue leadership in both the party and the government, as well as in the legislature.
The author of this book said that although this book can not describe all the history and activities of the three young political figures, at least this book can help to understand more about Their thoughts, attitudes and actions were born with the father as the supreme leader of the country.
In this regard, Mr. Sophal stated: "The reason I compiled this book is that I want to show readers to know more about the background of the three brothers as the children of the country's top leaders. The other two sisters are also briefly mentioned in this book.
In front of the media, Mr. Sophal asked many questions, including:
"If any writer or individual sees a gap, he or she can write more according to their understanding," he said. The job of a book writer is not different from that of a chef, because a pot of soup can not satisfy the mouths of dozens of people. ”
