(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will lead a high-level delegation to pay an official visit to the Socialist Republic of Vietnam from December 6 to 8, 2018. This is according to a press release issued by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation on December 4, obtained by Fresh News.
During the visit, the Prime Minister will meet separately with Vietnamese President Nguyen Phu Trong and National Assembly President Nguyen Thi Kim Ngin. Samdech Techo Hun Sen will hold bilateral talks and have a working breakfast with Mr. Nguyen Suon Phuc to strengthen friendly relations between the two countries and discuss bilateral, regional and international issues of common concern and concern. A real benefit for both nations.
