(China): Cross-sectoral marketing is becoming more and more popular for companies in China as they seek to find different ways to attract customers.
Cross-sectoral marketing refers to partnering with a company doing business in another sector and jointly developing new products.
"For our company, this collaboration helps us meet new customers," said Hussein Chalayen, a fashion designer. We can reach more people. It allows us to get involved in product development, something we have never done before. So for me it was a fun experience. ”
In addition to being able to reach a wider audience, cross-sectoral marketing methods also increase the effectiveness of a company's advertising because it can attract people's attention on social media.
