Cambodia-Vietnam: No illegal signing between Mondulkiri and Dak Nong administrations to illegally export timber to Vietnam
(Mondulkiri): The administrative team of Mondulkiri Provincial Hall of Cambodia and the Department of Foreign Affairs of Dak Nong Province, Vietnam, held an emergency meeting on the afternoon of December 3, 2018 after the fake news that the leaders of Mondulkiri Province stole the signature. With the leadership of Dak Nong province, allow illegal trade and transportation of timber from Mondulkiri to Dak Nong province along corridor 751.
Both sides added that in Resolution No. 371 / QD-UBND dated March 3, 2017 of Dak Nong Province, the Dak Nong Provincial People's Committee deems it inappropriate, so Dak Nong has terminated the above letter. Unable to confirm the number of trees on the Mondulkiri side at the request of Vietnamese traders.
Until now, the Dak Nong side has not allowed the import of timber from Mondulkiri to Dak Nong through corridor 751.
Meanwhile, the Governor of Mondulkiri Province, Mr. Svay Sam Eang, on December 4, 2018, also announced the complete rejection of any information posted on Facebook, which accused him of allowing the export of timber to Vietnam. On the contrary, the provincial governor only ordered the officers and the three armed forces to go down to prevent this crime at the border.
Speaking to Fresh News on the afternoon of December 4, 2018, the Governor of Mondulkiri claimed that he did not know the facts and did not happen that he allowed the export of timber. Hold on to Vietnam until the signing, instead take the next step to curb timber exports to neighboring countries.
"On the contrary, I have only ordered the officers and the three armed forces to go down to the border and at the border to tighten and prevent the smuggling of timber," he said. Neighboring countries and the authorities and relevant authorities have cracked down on many cases.
However, the provincial governor acknowledged that despite the prevention, the smuggling of timber, the importation of duty-free motorbikes still exist, but in this case, he has already taken measures to prevent Effective.
It should be noted that these denials were rejected after some local news and social media reported that the provincial governor had secretly signed with the Vietnamese side, the governor of Dak Nong province, to allow the import and export of timber from Mondul province. Kiri to Vietnam through port 751 without going through any relevant ministries.
