The wife of the director of the Oral District Health Center was accused of injecting tetanus with the wrong technique that caused the death of an elderly woman, the forensic team is examining the body to analyze the truth
(Kampong Speu): Oral District Midwife and wife of the director of Kampong Speu Oral District Health Center were accused of injecting the wrong medicine, causing the death of an elderly woman and her family sent the body to the Kampong Speu Provincial Referral Hospital on December 4, 2018 to analyze the truth.
According to the local police, the victim, 74-year-old Pov Yan, a widow and their two children living in Phsar Kantuot village, Sangke Satop commune, Oral district, Kampong Speu province, died after the victim suffered minor injuries and received tetanus injections. At the house of Chea Him, who runs a private hospital in the village-commune with the victim.
Before the incident, the victim went to get tetanus injection, but the director of the health center gave his wife as an alternative injector (name unknown), he did not give the injection, after a while, the victim felt unwell or could break. The wind is gone. After realizing the uncomfortable situation, Mr. Chea Him took the village chief's private car to transport the body of the victim to the provincial hospital in Nai to escape.
Mr. O Vanthen, Director of Kampong Speu Provincial Hospital, confirmed that the above case really happened and the body was kept at the Provincial Hospital, while the tetanus injector is currently a medical officer, both husband and wife.
Mr. O'Vanthen confirmed that the team is inspecting and conducting an autopsy on the body, if found to have died due to improper injection, will face legal action and will close the private medical business. Further, any kind of punishment depends on the law as a judge.
