In order to achieve the above, the Plenary Meeting of the National AIDS Authority has issued the following decisions:
* First, the National AIDS Authority, relevant ministries, institutions and development partners prepare, complete and implement the 5th National Comprehensive and Multi-sectoral Strategic Plan for HIV and AIDS Response 2019-2023 and the National Sustainability Strategy. To respond to the work of fighting HIV / AIDS in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
* Second, the National AIDS Authority incorporates the activities outlined in the Roadmap for Sustainable Response into the Fifth National Comprehensive Strategic Plan for HIV / AIDS 2019-2023. .
* Third, the National AIDS Authority must cooperate with the Ministry of Interior and the Ministry of Economy and Finance to provide funding for the implementation of the integration of HIV / AIDS into the commune development and investment plan.
* Fourth, the Ministry of Health and the Ministry of Planning must identify people living with HIV as vulnerable people with poor family identities and equity funds that ensure access to health care and social protection.
Fifth, the Ministry of Health and the Ministry of Economy and Finance shall revise and prepare rules and procedures for funding so that the OD, referral hospitals and health centers have direct funding for HIV / AIDS response.
* Sixth: The Office of the Council of Ministers, Ministry of Interior, Ministry of Economy and Finance, Ministry of Health and the National AIDS Authority must recognize the important role of civil society organizations in responding to HIV / AIDS and continue to support their continued participation. Through: Funding from the Royal Government according to the national budget.
Seventh, the Supreme National Economic Council must study the budget to ensure the implementation of the Royal Government's commitment to end the AIDS problem by 2025.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that "Cambodia will continue to work with international partners, with the support of international partners still determined to protect the heritage on its territory."
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also hopes that we will continue to work together for success for Cambodia and success in the regional and international framework.
Please be informed that Angkor Wat was inscribed on the World Heritage List on December 14, 1992, Preah Vihear was inscribed on the World Heritage List on July 7, 2008 and Sambor Prei Kuk was inscribed on the World Heritage List. On July 08, 2017. The decision was made at the 41st meeting of the World Heritage Committee in Krakow, Poland.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen cited the fact that Angkor Wat and all of Cambodia's temples were subject to international sanctions and economic sanctions because during the 1980s, the United Nations recognized the Pol Pot regime and no country. Na did not support the government at that time.
On the occasion of presiding over the celebration of the 25th anniversary of the establishment of the International Coordinating Committee for the Protection and Development of the Angkor Area (ICC-Angkor) this morning, the Prime Minister raised this issue. It can be an experience for the international community to consider before deciding to impose sanctions on any country.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "I would like to emphasize that Angkor Wat, Preah Vihear or all temples in Cambodia are subject to political sanctions and external siege. This is a point that should be tested, not just for problems. "Cambodia, but this issue should be tested for the world as well."
Samdech Techo Prime Minister continued, "We are really unfortunate, even Angkor Wat was punished because at the United Nations still recognize the Pol Pot to occupy the seat at the United Nations, so we have no foreign aid. No help. "This is either the experience of the United Nations or the experience that they should not use any of the sanctions that even sanctions on heritage or cultural property will suffer as a result of such sanctions."
However, the head of the Royal Government also reminded of one of the stories that Cambodia is lucky after the sanctions, because there is Professor Isisawa from Japan who came to study and discuss with the prince regularly and then the government India also sent technicians to rescue the stage in the 1980s.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also emphasized that the United Nations and all the international community should not allow the historical heritage of mankind in the countries to interfere with political issues, because this is a separate issue.
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia said: "I think the people of Cambodia will understand and understand more and not come to encroach on the land in the area of the temple, so that we preserve the heritage for our country that our ancestors. "Thousands of years ago, built for us, now we have a duty to protect."
Samdech Techo added, "But in Cambodia, I am unfortunate in this place that when the election is near, during the election campaign, they always use people to encroach on the land around the temple, so what should I do between the two points?" "If we respect the right of people to occupy the land, our temple will no longer be a World Heritage Site."
Samdech Techo expected that the people would understand this issue by not encroaching on the land in the temple area, which led to the loss of the heritage that our ancestors left for future generations, and especially the property. The nation's culture is no longer valuable. Peng Huot Group Wins Asia-Pacific International Real Estate Award in London
