Minister of Culture: ICC-Angkor Spirit and Mechanism will be long-lasting and proud to be a model for all international mechanisms in the protection of World Heritage
(Siem Reap): Ms. Pheung Sakona, Minister of Culture and Fine Arts, stated that the spirit and mechanism of ICC-Angkor will continue to be sustainable and will become a source of pride and role model for all international mechanisms in the protection of World Heritage. Mr.
The remarks of the Minister of Culture were made on December 4, 2018, on the occasion of her participation in the celebration of the 25th anniversary of the establishment of the International Committee for the Coordination of Protection and Development of Angkor (IT). ICC-Angkor in Siem Reap.
Ms. Phoeung Sakona stated that the celebration of the 25th anniversary of the establishment of ICC-Angkor today in order to reaffirm our commitment to the past 25 years, as well as to show the success that the Royal Government of Cambodia And the international community has overcome the challenges of the past and will continue to work together to pave the way for future goals.
Mr. Pheung Sakona said that 25 years ago, after the Angkor resort was inscribed on the World Heritage List under the most precious relics of His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, the Father of National Independence and the Royal Treasure, the ICC-Angkor mechanism was Established shortly after the first Intergovernmental Conference on Angkor in Tokyo, Japan.
The Committee is an international mechanism for mobilizing financial, technical, and human resources from the international community to restore, preserve, and enhance the value of temples, as well as the development of the large and resource-intensive Angkor World Heritage Site.
The Minister of Culture stated that culture is the greatest core force of peacekeeping that the whole world needs to preserve what is a legacy and cultural heritage left for future generations.
On this occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also announced the good news of the inclusion of theatrical performances in the list of Intangible Heritage of Humanity on November 18, 2018 recently.
