Very symphonic! A female student riding a motorbike hit the steering wheel of a tuk tuk and was crushed to death by a car in Po Sen Chey district
(Phnom Penh): It is very sad that a young girl who is a student at Hun Sen Bun Rany Arun Vatey High School drove a motorbike over a tuk-tuk and hit the steering wheel of the motorbike, causing the car to fall from behind the brakes and not break its head and die Immediately at the scene.
This horrible traffic accident happened on December 3, 2018 along the concrete road in Chung Ruk village, Sangkat Trapeang Tra Saing, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
According to local police, the victim, 15-year-old Ban Srey Pich, a ninth-grade student at Hun Sen Bun Rany Arunavattey High School and a resident of Trapeang Anchanh 6 village, Trapeang Krasaing commune, Por Sen Chey district, died on the spot. As for the car that crushed the dead body, it was a blue Hyundai car with license plate Battambang 3A.1494 driven by a man and was arrested by the police.
Police said that before the incident, the victim was riding a motorcycle with license plate Phnom Penh 1GQ7029 by a friend named Hang Srey Pich, 15 years old, a driver traveling on the concrete road in the direction from the east. To sink out of school, aiming to return home.
Police officials said that when they arrived at the scene, they were riding a motorbike, overtook a tuk-tuk, could not get out of the steering wheel, causing it to fall and was hit by a Hyundai truck coming from behind, breaking its head and dying on the spot. . After the accident, the driver was detained by the authorities. Immediately, the victim's family arrived at the scene and cried and hugged their son's body with great emotion.
Currently, cars and motorcycles, as well as drivers, have been sent by the police to the land traffic office for legal action. The body was taken to the family for a traditional ceremony.
