(Phnom Penh): The University of Specialties of Cambodia, Stung Meanchey location, on December 2, 2018, organized a workshop on "Roles and Benefits of Taxes and Tax Systems in Cambodia" under the Cooperation between Specialized Universities of Cambodia, General Department of Taxation. And JICA (Japan).
In this workshop, many distinguished speakers, including university leaders from the representatives of the General Director of Taxation of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and JICA Advisors, who have a lot of experience and knowledge, presented and shared to the workshop.
Dr. Keo Chea, Vice Chancellor, gave a presentation on the relationship between business and tax companies to the workshop that all businesses need to understand the tax system and tax law, as well as the obligation to pay taxes and annual tax returns to the state. Properly presented as presented in each annual financial statement, this report includes balance sheets, income statements, balance sheets, etc.
On the other hand, professors and students must understand and strive to learn various subjects, including the tax system, because the knowledge that is properly trained in the university profession is an important resource for working in companies / institutions and have High awareness of work and business from small to large companies.
Professors and students asked a lot of questions to the speakers and got a lot of answers and basic knowledge from the performance.
In closing, Dr. Keo, a representative of the University, summarized the content and encouraged the students to study hard and prepare well to become human resources with virtue, knowledge, skills, abilities and experiences for themselves, their families, society and the nation.
The University has started training for the past 17 years at all levels in 5 colleges. Currently, the University has 8 locations: 2 locations in Phnom Penh (Toul Kork, Stung Meanchey) and 6 locations in the provinces, including provinces. Kampong Cham, Kampong Thom, Siem Reap, Banteay Meanchey, Battambang and Kampot provinces. More than 30,000 graduates and nearly 20,000 undergraduates are increasing each year.
The University has signed memorandums of study and research with more than 500 foreign universities and public and private institutions to find places for students to train and work. The university strives to improve quality through a number of measures, such as the addition of physical materials.
Recently, the university has decided to pay twice the monthly salary for staff and professors, as well as to provide additional study aids, LCD machines at each location to support the study and research. In addition, the university always pays attention to promote research through the organization of conferences, seminars, practical workshops, today's seminar is a proof.
