Mr. Sieng Thirith, Deputy Director General of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, announced the opening of the seminar program in these five provinces. He then mentioned the mission of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia in promoting derivatives trading and encouraging participants to seek knowledge about the derivatives market as well as consider trading in derivatives.
Mr. Yun Sovannara, Deputy Chief of Business Management Office, Derivatives Investment and Derivatives Business, gave an overview of the derivatives market, the growth of derivatives trading in Cambodia, and the regulatory framework used to ensure trading and protection mechanisms. Transparent investors.
As the guest speaker, Mr. Lawrence Kook, Governor of Cambodian Derivatives Exchange Company, expressed his pleasure to participate in the 2018 Provincial Workshop with the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia and said that raising awareness and sharing Sharing extensive knowledge of trading in financial instruments is an obligation of Cambodian Derivatives Exchange.
Lawrence emphasizes the importance of self-assessment and the implementation of appropriate strategies for each investor, as well as how to derive positive returns from the investment.
Mr. Lawrence announced the commitment of Cambodian Derivatives Exchange to appear at SEC events in the coming years.
