Ministry of Education launches project to improve higher education in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports on December 3, 2018 launched the project to improve higher education in higher education institutions, which are five main goals in the capital-province.
According to the Minister, this project covers the quality of education in five target higher education institutions, including: Royal University of Phnom Penh, Royal University of Agriculture, Institute of Technology of Cambodia, Svay Rieng University and University of Battambang. The project also strengthens private higher education institutions and strengthens the public higher education system.
He added that improving STEM and agricultural research focuses on improving the quality and responsiveness of research through financing of higher education institutions identified in the project and the construction of laboratories and equipment. . Strengthening governance and project management focuses on strengthening the higher education subsystem and project management and coordination.
"This project to improve higher education is in line with the priority reform of the higher education sub-sector as stated in the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategy, Phase 4, Government for 5 years (2019-2023). "The main focus is on improving the quality of teaching, learning and research, increasing the accessibility and equity of students, strengthening the quality assurance system and strengthening governance and management in higher education."
