Notice! Volunteer doctors from France come to treat children with oral and general disabilities in Pursat for free for 15 days from December 1-15
(Pursat): With the good communication of the provincial leaders as well as the director of the Department of Health and the director of the Provincial Referral Hospital, the friendly countries, philanthropists and national and international organizations have been very interested in Pursat Provincial Referral Hospital by helping Build office buildings, provide medicine, medical equipment and distribute gifts to patients who are being treated in the hospital.
In fact, now a group of doctors from France have volunteered to examine and treat the people of Pursat free of charge for 15 days, from December 1 to 15, 2018.
He added that the other focus is on surgery for children with oral disabilities (cleft lip or palate by accident). In this treatment, the team of doctors have specific skills and experience, and this is the third visit for Pursat province.
The medical team has a mobile vehicle to go to the village-commune for treatment. If the patient has a minor condition that can be treated at the local level, it is treated, but if it is large, it must be transported to the provincial referral hospital for treatment.
Mr. Ung Kimleang, Deputy Governor, who participated in the opening ceremony of the examination and treatment of the French doctors this morning, December 3, expressed his happiness and thanks to the French doctors who volunteered. The continent considers the health of the Cambodian people. The Royal Government has identified three areas that need to be focused on: First, the health sector, second, agriculture, and third, rural development.
Mr. Ung Kimleang called on people with various diseases, especially cleft lip and palate, to be examined and treated by foreign doctors at Pursat Provincial Referral Hospital. The Deputy Governor instructed the doctors in Pursat Provincial Referral Hospital to pay attention to study and learn from the experience of foreign doctors in order to gain knowledge to treat patients in the hospital without being dependent on them. Forever.
