(Sri Lanka): Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, led a delegation to attend the 54th Summit of the ASEAN Governors 'Conference and the 38th SEACEN Governors' Meeting in Colombo, Sri Lanka. The meeting was held to bring together all the governors of the central bank to exchange experiences and ideas on how to maintain macroeconomic and financial growth and stability.
The Saxon Center has a total of 19 central bank members and monetary authorities in the Asia-Pacific region and plays a key role in providing capacity building training to central bank member members.
According to the National Bank of Vietnam, the conference provides an opportunity for central bank leaders to meet and exchange views and experiences on regional challenges and key solutions to maintain macroeconomic and financial growth.
For this year's meeting, the topics focused on monetary policy in the context of the central bank's rapid evolution of e-currency, inflation issues in emerging countries and central bank challenges in small economies. And open.
The meeting of the Council of Governors also reviewed the results of the Center's Achievements Center in 2018, with congratulations on the effective training provided by the Scheme Center.
The Shaanxi Board of Governors also approved the Sean Sen Strategic Plan for 2019 and initiatives to enhance the quality of future training and research. In addition, these forums provide opportunities for the governor of the Central Bank as a member to strengthen friendships and cooperation.
In the past, the National Bank of Cambodia has sent staff officers to participate in training courses, research and meetings of the SASEN Center to strengthen the skills and specialization of staff officers.
