Legal Awareness: Rape Offenses
(Phnom Penh): Rape is one of the most common acts of sexual harassment that occurs almost daily, and it mostly affects women and minors. In the past, rape has also occurred in the form of stepfathers raping children, grandparents raping grandchildren and uncles raping nephews, etc.
Rape has caused serious damage to the victims, their families, relatives and society as a whole, which requires measures to prevent and punish the perpetrators. What kind of acts are defined as rape? And to what extent will the perpetrators be punished?
FRESH NEWS 'Legal Awareness Program in collaboration with International Cooperation Lawyers This week, the topic of "Rape Offenses" will be shared with citizens and students:
"The crime of rape" is defined in the Penal Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia in Article 239, which stipulates that: "Whether they are of the same sex or not, by violence, coercion, intimidation or opportunistic assault is a crime."
On the other hand, the perpetrator may commit this act by using a weapon or threatening to use a weapon or using drugs or other substances to make the victim lose consciousness. Victims of rape must be surviving physical persons, whether of the same or different sex.
As for the punishment for rape, Article 239 of the Penal Code stipulates that "rape is punishable by imprisonment from 5 (five) to 10 (ten) years." This conviction only applies to ordinary rape offenses that do not have aggravating circumstances.
If there is an aggravating circumstance, the level of punishment will vary as follows:
Article 240: Rape is punishable by imprisonment from 7 (seven) to 15 (fifteen) years if the act is committed by: 1: Using a weapon or threatening to use a weapon 2: Using drugs or methods Others cause the victim to lose consciousness. 3: The person who has power over the victim. 4: The person who abuses the power given to him by his function.
Article 241: The offense of rape shall be punished by imprisonment from 7 (seven) to 15 (fifteen) years if the act is committed on: 1: A person who is weak, especially due to the age of that person. Pregnancy when the fetus is visible or when the perpetrator is aware 3: A person who is weak, especially due to illness or disability, when the condition of this person is obvious or when the perpetrator is aware.
Article 244: The offense of rape shall be punished by imprisonment from 15 (fifteen) to 30 (thirty) years if the offense causes the victim to die unintentionally. In addition to imprisonment, there are other additional penalties that can be announced to the perpetrators, and those additional penalties are provided for in Article 245 of the Penal Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
