He claimed that due to climate change at the end of the rainy season, there was not enough rain, causing about 2,700 hectares of rain-fed rice to be completely damaged, and about 1,900 hectares of rain-fed rice to be completely rescued. Another 2,900 hectares of paddy fields, which were scheduled to be salvaged, recovered due to two days of rain on November 26 and 27.
The district governor said that in the case of flooded rice in Baray district this year, the people have cultivated 6,525 hectares on the plan to grow only 3,500 hectares, which is the people. Growing more than the planned water supply up to 3,025 hectares, but due to two days of rain in the past, the water in the fields, irrigation canals and canals are sufficiently wet to supply water. Back.
As for the expectation, this year's rice will not be short of water, because only the reservoir of Samdech Hun Sen, Tonle Chum has a lot of water, which can help irrigate about 3,500 hectares and maybe Nearly another 500 hectares.
Please be informed that the people in Baray district, Kampong Thom province have irrigated 6,525 hectares of rice in 7 communes: Chhouk Khsach commune, Thnaot Chum commune, Baray commune, Treal commune, Sralao commune, Pong commune and Chong Dong commune.
