Cambodia is the latest investment destination in Southeast Asia, a key strategic destination on the Silk Road "Belt and Road" Cambodia is a member of the Indochina Peninsula, bordering Thailand to the northwest, Laos to the north. It borders Vietnam to the southeast and the Gulf of Thailand to the south.
In 1993, with the establishment of full legal authority and the achievement of national unification, Cambodia entered a new era of rapid peace and development.
In recent years, Cambodia has become a major investment destination in Asia, attracting a lot of international investment.
The economy is growing rapidly and steadily at a rate of more than 7% per year, with a return on real estate investment of between 8% and 15%, a strong inflow of foreign investment and excellent geographical location in ASEAN.
With the deepening cooperation with the Chinese economy, the "One Belt One Road" policy dividend has contributed to the continuous improvement of Cambodia's infrastructure.
Development space for the future is something that many investors are interested in. The Royal Government of Cambodia has implemented a comprehensive and open investment policy with no control over the international exchange rate, and has preferential tariffs, low investment requirements, and a population of young people with an average age of more than 30 years. .
