Samdech Techo Hun Sen returns to Cambodia after visit and meeting in Nepal (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen at 6 pm on December 1, 2018 Leading a high-level delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia, returned home safely after concluding his official visit and Asia-Pacific Summit in Nepal.
The return of Samdech Techo Hun Sen with many achievements and achievements should be a source of pride for the nation and the people of Cambodia as a whole, welcomed by many leaders and senior officials. Also at Phnom Penh International Airport.
During the working visit of the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia in Nepal, Samdech Techo Hun Sen met with the Minister of Foreign Affairs of Nepal, Mr. Pradip Kumar Gavali, and the two sides pledged to further enhance cooperation and relations. Making the country have a history of similar divisions benefits the nation and the people of both countries.
In response, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that he was very grateful to the Prime Minister of Nepal for the honor of inviting him to visit as well as to attend the Asia-Pacific Summit. Special thanks for meeting with the Prime Minister of Nepal in September 2018 in New York at the United Nations General Assembly.
In addition, the Prime Ministers of the two countries also presided over the signing of four important documents. The four signed documents include: Visa waivers for diplomatic and official passports, agreements related to air transport, a memorandum of understanding between the two Ministries of Foreign Affairs and cooperation in the field. Politics, economy and culture.
The Prime Minister expressed his high appreciation and appreciation to the Government and people of Nepal for their efforts to quickly restore historical structures after the tsunami. At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also signed the Golden Book for world leaders who visited these two heritage sites of Nepal.
Speaking on the occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that this agreement is a part that promotes the people-to-people relations of the two countries, and Samdech Techo really intends to visit Nepal for a long time. The visit to Nepal now marks the beginning of high-level diplomatic relations between the two countries.
At the same time, the President of Nepal also expressed his pleasure at the visit of Samdech Techo Hun Sen in Nepal and encouraged the two countries to have better relations.
In particular, on the occasion of attending the Asia-Pacific Summit 2018 in Nepal, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also delivered a speech in line with the theme of the Asia-Pacific Summit 2018-Nepal "Addressing the key challenges of our era: "Interdependence, mutual prosperity and universal value."
Please note that Samdech Techo Hun Sen's trip abroad in Nepal is the 13th trip abroad in 2018.
