(Phnom Penh): Two suspects rode a motorbike to seize a bag until they decided to grab a GPS-enabled mobile phone and escaped safely while the victim was driving a motorbike on a public road. Only one day later, he was handcuffed during an investigation operation by the Russey Keo district police force led by Colonel Koul Yi, district inspector.
The operation to crack down on the two bag thieves took place at Group 4, Village K1, Sangkat Chrang Chamres II, Khan Russey Keo on the afternoon of November 30, 2018.
The victim told the police that after the thieves took the bag and the phone, he did not come to file a complaint until the morning of the 30th, then decided to ask the police to intervene through the lost phone. The GPS system was connected to the investigation immediately until the suspect was arrested after fleeing for a day.
Mr. Koul Yi confirmed that the suspect who stole the bag, which was cracked down on during the GPS search operation, was all with drugs in his body. Sangkat Chrang Chamres 2 and another named Radavit, 18 years old, living in Group 5, Village K1, Sangkat Chram Chamres II.
