MOSCOW (Reuters) - Russia's Defense Ministry announced on Saturday that a new generation of ballistic missile systems has been tested and successfully tested at a test site in the territory of Afghanistan bordering southern Russia. The name of the new system has not been revealed. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Saturday afternoon, December 1, 2018.
A statement from the Russian Defense Ministry said that after several tests, the new ballistic missile destroyer could intercept missiles from all targets. The new missile defense system will be equipped to protect Moscow from air strikes through early warning systems and regular air surveillance systems.
In addition to production to protect its vast territory, Russia will also be able to allow the system to be sold to its customers in the future, while the current S-400 and S-400 missile defense systems are The product is being sold to major countries such as China, India, Turkey and some of Russia's major allies.
