The following is the announcement of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs: Arrested the Chief Bishop of Wat Tep Onnaram, Samrong Tong District, Kampong Speu Province, the myth that a thief stole pagoda money
(Kampong Speu): Preah Chao Athikar Wat Tep Onnaram in Sampov Ngor village, Penay commune, Samrong Tong district, Kampong Speu province, was arrested by the provincial Department of Cult and Religion for falsely claiming that he stole more than 16 million riels and $ 900 dollars from the pagoda. From the police force, Preah Chao Athikar stole the pagoda money himself.
Major General Sam Samoun, Provincial Police Commissioner of Kampong Speu Province, released a report on November 30, 2018, with a complaint to the police, a specialized force opened a case of theft (money) at Wat Tep Onnaram in Sampov Ngor village, Penay commune. Samrong Tong district urgently according to the complaint of the pagoda chief.
According to the research results, at 2:20 pm on November 29, 2018, 42-year-old Mon Oeun, the Chief Inspector of Wat Tep Onnaram, complained to the Samrong Tong District Police that an unknown person did not know the number of activities. Smashed the glass door of the coffin and took 16,050,000 Khmer Riel and 900 USD.
After receiving this complaint on November 30, 2018, the police force conducted a thorough investigation, finding that the above case is a clear fabrication and committed by the monk himself named Mon Oeun. Once. Authorities gathered evidence and questioned the bishop until he admitted that he lied because he had a family problem and needed money.
