According to Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesman Geng Shuang, US warships entered Chinese waters without permission, while the Chinese military sent a number of warships to monitor the situation and warn US ships to leave. Shuang stressed that Beijing urges the United States to stop such provocative actions immediately because it violates China's sovereignty and threatens security.
Apart from China, the Spratly and Paracel Islands, which are among the most disputed areas in the South China Sea, are also claimed by Taiwan, Vietnam, Malaysia, Indonesia and the Philippines. As for the movement of warships and sometimes even US bombers into the South China Sea, it is Washington's opposition to Beijing's claim to the region.
Tomorrow, more than 10,000 Cambodians and foreigners run to Angkor for charity
(Phnom Penh): The 23rd Angkor International Half Marathon 2018 will start the history page on Sunday, December 2, with more than 10,000 national and international athletes running to be a humanitarian force.
According to the Organizing Committee of the National Olympic Committee of Cambodia (NOCC), for the 2018 Angkor International Half Marathon, there are more than 10,000 registered participants, both Cambodians and foreigners.
Runners will gather in front of Angkor Wat Temple of the 23rd Angkor Wat International Half Marathon, sponsored by WURKZ on December 2, 2018 at 5:30 AM Side.
This annual multi-ethnic running event is held with the sole purpose of donating to Angkor Hospital for Children, Kantha Bopha Hospital, Cambodian Sports Federation for the Disabled, Cambodia Trust and supporting the Child Care, Youth Development and Rehabilitation Education Project. Disability in Cambodia.
For the 23rd time since Angkor Wat International Half Marathon Day, the first event has been organized since 1996, with participants from about 70 countries around the world.
So far, the number of registered runners has increased by nearly 10,000, and this number will continue to increase until the closing date of registration, which the committee expects to increase to more than 10,000 participants.
