Cambodia, Nepal push for direct flights soon
(Nepal): During the official visit of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia to Nepal, the two countries signed an agreement on direct flight cooperation in the field of civil aviation soon. This was confirmed by Mr. Kao Kim Hourn, Minister accompanying the Prime Minister on November 30, 2018.
Speaking at the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen informed the President about the signing of four agreements with Nepal. "Among them, this agreement can promote direct flights between our two countries and Cambodia Airlines or Nepal Airlines can fly directly," he said.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that this agreement is part of the promotion of people-to-people relations of the two countries, and Samdech Techo really intends to visit Nepal for a long time. Nepal is now the beginning of a high-level diplomatic relationship between the two countries.
"I have always dreamed of making it possible for Nepal to be connected by air with other countries, including Cambodia, especially those who believe in Buddhism," she said.
"Nepal is the land of the Buddha and the philosophy of the Buddha, so on behalf of Nepal, she is very happy to sign a flight connection between Cambodia and Nepal and encourage traders," she said. Nepal is also involved in this field.
