The family cycling event in front of the Elephant Terrace will start tomorrow!
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of December 1, 2018, tomorrow, there will be a cycling event with all kinds of disciplines for families, bring children as well as friends to ride for fun and good health, which will take place in In front of the Elephant Camp in the land of wonder: Siem Reap province.
The cycling event, sponsored by Wurkz Energy Drink and Cambodian Pure Water, has three events to register for: 17km, 37km and 117km.
The 37-kilometer event is open to everyone, especially families, who can bring their young and old to enjoy the ride, because it does not require much competition, but to entertain health, solidarity and attract tourists in the area of ancient temples. Great Khmer.
The 37-kilometer event is for those who have cycled and experienced, while the 117-kilometer course is for high-level professionals. This is the 13th cycling event organized in Siem Reap.
What is special is that the participation of all of you is an important contribution to the children and charity, especially for health and strength.
Where to find! Let's register and ride a bike for all children on Saturday, December 1st. Gather in front of the Terrace of the Elephants of Angkor. For registration and more information: 077 30 38 60.
Japanese Government Provides Nearly $ 400,000 in Grants for Health, Education and Infrastructure Development in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Government of Japan has provided a total grant of US $ 353,276 to support the development of health, education and infrastructure in Cambodia.
The signing ceremony for the grant took place on November 29, 2018 at the Embassy of Japan, in which the Japanese side was represented by Mr. Horino Uchihi Hidehisa, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia and the Cambodian side was represented by four institutions.
These grants will support four departments in Cambodia, including: For a small-scale project, Human Security provides $ 88,995 to the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology of Kampong Speu, the Department of Health of Takeo $ 87,304, Department Education, Youth and Sports of Kandal Province with a budget of $ 89,162 and the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Kampong Cham with a budget of $ 87,810.
Since 1991, the Government of Japan has provided more than US $ 58 million to local authorities and NGOs to implement 594 Kusanoni projects throughout Cambodia.
