On that occasion, General Meas Virith stated that the drug problem is under the control of the national and sub-national levels and instructed all stakeholders to continue to work harder on the fight against drugs for community safety:
1: Promote the activities of the Community-Based Drug Treatment Coordination Committee in all 105 communes to send addicts to receive treatment at health centers, referral hospitals and national hospitals.
2: Strive to build focal points for outreach work, provide understanding to all destinations, especially entertainment clubs, guesthouses, hotels, student rooms, absenteeism, unemployment, drivers and unregulated areas, etc. .
3: Continue to take measures to strictly implement administrative measures, apply the law so that perpetrators do not take the opportunity to commit crimes under the brand name of all kinds.
