Director General of Taxation: The presence of Korean investors to invest in Cambodia has contributed to the development of Cambodia's economic growth
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kong Vibol, the Royal Government delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Taxation, mentioned the progress made in Cambodia, especially in the field of taxation. In fact, he mentioned the presence of Korean investors who came to invest in Cambodia, this investment has contributed to the development of economic growth in Cambodia to another level.
"The presence of Korean investors has contributed to the development and economic growth of Cambodia, as well as facilitating and promoting fair competition among companies," said Kong Vibol.
He added that for the past six years, the General Department of Taxation has worked hard to reform both the tax administration and tax modernization, as well as to improve some tax laws and regulations by strictly implementing the mobilization strategy. Medium-term income for 2014-2018 as well as the participation of enterprises as taxpayers.
He continued that as a goal in implementing the medium-term revenue collection strategy for 2019-2023, the General Department of Taxation will focus on many factors such as: 1: Ensuring sustainable revenue growth, Second: Sustainable economic growth, Third: Competitive Equally and fourth: social justice.
He said that the General Department of Taxation of Cambodia and the Tax Administration of the Republic of Korea have been strengthening tax cooperation, sharing knowledge and good experience lessons in order to further strengthen and improve the Cambodian tax administration.
He said that the General Department of Taxation has encouraged and encouraged the organization of such forums to strengthen and improve the provision of services to taxpayers to listen to all the challenges and difficulties, as well as access. Solutions based on tax laws and regulations in force.
Mr. Oh Nak Young expressed his pleasure at providing opportunities for Korean investors to invest in Cambodia and thanked the Royal Government Delegation and all relevant officials for organizing this forum to make it easier to understand. Be clear about the Cambodian tax system in order to strengthen tax compliance and provide mechanisms for addressing tax challenges.
The Ambassador congratulated the Cambodian economy for maintaining steady growth of around 7% per year as the level of regional and global economic and trade competition increased.
