(Phnom Penh): Through the event "40 km to history" has made the Cambodian youth today amazed at the sacrifice of all, even the lives of the previous generation to liberate the country from the brutal regime. The brutal slaughter of the regime of 3 years, 8 months and 20 days until peace and development progress as it is today.
The event "40 km to history" organized by the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia to highlight the heroism of the previous generation to the youth of today, departed from Phnom Penh this morning, November 28, 2018 to Travel to Snuol district, Kratie province, led by Mr. HUN Many, President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia and attended by a total of about 700 young people.
Speaking in an interview with the press, Mr. Hun Many said that this event is to commemorate the spirit of December 2, but also to reflect the efforts, struggles, sacrifices that have achieved the liberation of the motherland from The genocidal regime of Pol Pot, as many Cambodian children knew and heard of this bitter history from a group of young people in the past, brought about the recovery of the entire Cambodian nation.
Not much different from Mr. Hun Many, the young people who participated in this event all claimed that they are very proud of what the dedication of the previous generation and the "40 km to history" event. Reflects part of the aspects that the younger generation must dare to go through to understand all those values.
Dara Pi, a member of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, stated that despite the "40 km to history" event for the younger generation to learn about the high sacrifices and sacrifices of the previous generation, but the event is still not possible. Compared to what they sacrificed, young people can also recognize that history is really hard and bitter.
Chan Vathanakar, one of Cambodia's most famous football players, also took part in the "40km to history" event. Mr. Vathankar expressed his pleasure to participate in this event, as this is something that the younger generation should understand about the sacrifices of the previous generation who dare to sacrifice everything, even their lives.
"I feel very happy to be part of this event and I think we should understand that he dared to sacrifice almost his life for the nation," he said. For me, I want them to see their dedication as a source of strength.
At the same time, an actor who is gaining popularity, Mr. Na Khon, as a younger generation of Cambodians, found that this event was really great so that he could clearly understand how difficult it was at that time. That is why he volunteered to walk 40 kilometers to this history.
"The younger generation should take care because the older ones, they all really sacrificed, they have sacrificed a lot, and he left a lot of legacy for the next generation of Cambodians, and we are the next generation of Cambodians." . Thus, each of us must unite to preserve our Khmer history. This is what actor Nakon mentioned.
Western University students who are getting ready to get on the bus to the venue say similarly that the event is really good for the younger generation to know more about history and understand the sacrifices. Of the previous generation is very important and the youth must keep it all together.
"For me, I think it is important because we should all learn a lot about history and should learn what the previous generation dared to sacrifice, we just walk," she said. "But he pretends to be at war, while we just walk normally, there is no more fatigue."
Not only that, this event is designed to create a friendly and fraternal atmosphere, in which all young people are encouraged to participate in team building activities (Team Building), walking together, singing together, singing together, cooking together, throwing Camps, bonfires, storytelling and the display of personal talents, as well as singing, dancing and entertainment.
To ensure the smooth running of the event, all participants will be divided into groups and will travel 40 km (for men) and 20 or 40 km for women. According to the schedule, the trip will take about 2 days, 1 night and 1 day for camping at the 2 December Memorial.
Vietnam is ready to receive the state visit of the King of Cambodia and the official visit of Samdech Techo Hun Sen next month (Video Inside) (Phnom Penh): Vietnamese Prime Minister Nguyen Tan Dung has revealed that Vietnam is ready to Receive the visit of His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the visit of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister in December.
This is according to the announcement of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation on November 29, 2018 on the results of the official visit of Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia to the Socialist Republic of Vietnam for 2 days. Fresh News Received.
The visit is to further strengthen and expand the existing friendship, solidarity and comprehensive cooperation between Cambodia and Vietnam for the harmony and well-being of the people of the two countries.
During his visit on November 26-27, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon paid a courtesy call on his Vietnamese counterpart Nguyen Suon Phuc.
Nguyen Suon Phuoc praised the long-term relations between the two countries and asked both sides to further strengthen this relationship for the benefit of both nations.
The Vietnamese Prime Minister confirmed that Vietnam is ready to receive the visit of the King of the Kingdom of Cambodia and Samdech Techo Prime Minister in December.
Lt. Gen. Hun Manet Calls on the Armed Forces to Strongly Oppose Internal Interference in Cambodia from Outsiders, Not to Allow Traitors Conspiring with Foreigners to Destroy
(Battambang): Speaking from Battambang province, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the Army, continued to call on all armed forces, both the Army, the National Police and the Royal Gendarmerie, to continue to trust and be honest. Absolutely for the nation, the King and the legitimate government, that is, to strengthen the position not to participate in any illegal activities or cause insecurity to the nation.
This commitment was made during the meeting between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Minister of Foreign Affairs of Nepal on the afternoon of November 29, 2018 in Nepal, where Samdech Techo is visiting.
Mr. Srey Thamrong, Minister accompanying the Prime Minister, confirmed after the meeting that Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked for the warm hospitality and this was the first time that the top leaders had visited the country for the first time in history. Nepal, after establishing diplomatic ties, hopes the visit will further strengthen friendly relations and cooperation between the two countries.
The Nepalese Foreign Minister also thanked Samdech Techo for accepting an invitation during a meeting in New York with the Prime Minister of Nepal to visit Nepal. He described the election process and the rebuilding of Nepal, and also praised Cambodia for rebuilding the country through many obstacles.
The Prime Minister thanked for the invitation to pay an official visit to Nepal and also thanked for congratulating the CPP on its victory, which allowed him to continue as the Prime Minister. Samdech Techo said that the history of Cambodia and Nepal is complicated, the situation is not the same, but went through almost the same difficulties.
Samdech Techo praised the success that Nepal has achieved in national unification. Samdech informed that Cambodia has gone through many experiences from a divided country to a united country from a multi-party country with a division of territory and fighting on its own territory and going through hardships. Everything. Now the nation is united into a country with a constitution, an army and is promoting the development of the country.
He added that Cambodia has achieved economic growth of about 7.7 percent per year for the past 20 years and is turning from a low-middle-income country to a high-middle-income country by 2030. The Prime Minister continued that our two countries have experience and have exchanged experiences in development despite different situations.
He added that from Cambodia to Nepal, from Nepal to Cambodia is not far away, which should expand cooperation on what the two countries have potential. Samdech Techo stated that because Nepal has an Ambassador to Vietnam and presented his credentials in Phnom Penh, Samdech intends to send the Cambodian Ambassador, who resides in New Delhi, India to Nepal as well. Open an embassy in Nepal.
The Prime Minister also praised Nepal for organizing the 2018 Asia-Pacific Summit. The Prime Minister said that he will contribute to the success of this summit.
The Nepalese Foreign Minister also took the opportunity to congratulate the Cambodian People's Party, the Cambodian people for developing the country, and Nepal will strive in various fields to promote cooperation in tourism, trade, where we have potential. As much as possible.
He added that next year Nepal will open a new airport and provide direct flights to Cambodia, and then Nepalis will be able to visit Angkor Wat and Cambodians will be able to visit the birthplace of the Buddha. .
