According to Mr. Kao Kim Hourn, Minister accompanying the Prime Minister, during the meeting, the Prime Minister of Nepal mentioned that Samdech Techo's visit was the first visit to Nepal. The Prime Minister also thanked Samdech Techo for his visit and participation in the 2018 Asia-Pacific Summit organized by Nepal.
The Prime Minister of Nepal considered Samdech Techo's visit to be historically important and considered the bilateral relations between Nepal and Cambodia to be cordial and friendly.
The Prime Minister of Nepal praised the progress and maintenance of peace in Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, and he also congratulated the Cambodian People's Party, which was elected by a large number of votes in the past.
Mr. Kao Kim Hourn stated, "At the same time, he also saw a lot of progress in Cambodia, which has transformed from a least developed country to a low-middle-income country today."
The Prime Minister also said that in this bilateral meeting, 2019 will be the 55th anniversary of diplomatic relations between the two countries.
Samdech Techo also thanked the Prime Minister of Nepal for sending a message congratulating the 65th anniversary of the recent independence of the Kingdom of Cambodia and also thanked the Prime Minister of Nepal for sending a message for the success of the party. Past elected people.
The Prime Minister said that he had wanted to visit Nepal for a long time but could not take the time. The Prime Minister also thanked Nepal for providing land for the construction of temples and pagodas in Nepal.
At the same time, Samdech Techo also congratulated Nepal for achieving peace, in which Samdech Techo also spoke about the exchange of views on how to make the two countries exchange experiences with each other. To further strengthen the cooperation between the two countries.
Regarding bilateral relations, Samdech Techo also said that Cambodia will open an embassy in Kathmandu, Nepal, and Nepal can establish an embassy in Phnom Penh.
He also stressed that what needs to be done now is to promote the development of bilateral cooperation.
