(Phnom Penh): Cambodia and Vietnam have shown their common political will by not allowing any enemy force to use their territory to oppose or interfere in the internal affairs of another country.
During the visit, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon had a fruitful bilateral meeting with Vietnamese Foreign Minister Pham Binh Minh.
A statement from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs stated that during the meeting, the two sides agreed to increase the exchange of information with each other and in a timely manner to rescue victims, prevent and prevent any problems such as natural disasters, smuggling. Illegal trafficking, transnational crime and illegal logging.
A statement from the Foreign Ministry said: "Both sides have reaffirmed their political will not to allow any enemy force to use their territory to oppose or interfere in the internal affairs of another country. "
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon's visit to Vietnam comes after some foreign media outlets attacked Cambodia for allowing China to set up military bases in Koh Kong province. However, this information was completely rejected by the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Ministry of National Defense and considered to be false news.
During the meeting, the two Foreign Ministers also praised the frequent exchanges of heads of state and government of the two countries as important in promoting bilateral ties. Bilateral parties and comprehensive cooperation between the two countries.
The two sides welcomed the positive growth of joint trade volume and agreed to expedite the conclusion of border trade agreements and trade facilitation agreements between Cambodia and Vietnam to contribute to achieving bilateral trade goals. 5 billion US dollars by 2020, as expected by the two heads of government.
For agriculture, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon thanked Vietnam for encouraging Vietnamese state and private companies to continue buying agricultural products from Cambodia and requested the Vietnamese government to continue to encourage this activity to contribute to strengthening people-to-people contacts as well as business people. And businessmen of both countries. In response, Mr. Pham Binh Minh agreed to further strengthen cooperation in this area.
The two Foreign Ministers also shared views on regional and global issues of common concern and interest and expressed mutual support in the regional and international framework.
