Minister of Commerce: Better Factories Cambodia (BFC) project brings positive results for textile industry
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Commerce, Mr. Pan Sosak, emphasized that the Better Factories Cambodia (BFC) project has brought positive results for the national textile industry, especially to improve the working conditions and living standards of more than 700,000 workers. Working in factories across the country.
The Minister emphasized this on the occasion of presiding over the quarterly meeting on the implementation of working conditions of the garment and footwear industry held at the Ministry of Commerce on Thursday morning, November 29, 2018 in the presence of representatives of the Ministry. Employment and Vocational Training The International Labor Organization (ILO) and the Garment Manufacturers Association of Cambodia (GMAC).
On that occasion, Minister Pan Sosak welcomed the results of the ILO-BFC 2018 Report, which showed the improvement of the working environment, the reduction of violence and non-compliance with legal standards in 464 factories under the study and Evaluated by the Project Advisory Committee (PAC), which is comprised of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, the Ministry of Commerce, the Garment Manufacturers Association of Cambodia, and labor unions.
