Chinese traders are looking for new trade trends as steel prices fell in November, with steel stocks becoming an important tool for the steel industry. To withstand risks.
Since the beginning of November, steel prices have fallen to $ 108 a tonne, with sharp declines in eastern and northern China.
The general manager of a private steel plant in northern Hebei province said demand for steel products had declined since the winter.
Central government efforts to reduce overcapacity in recent years have created many opportunities for the steel industry. Earlier this year, steel mills made $ 173 a tonne, the highest level in history, but fell to $ 115.
Due to high profit growth, the steel industry has expanded output, and individuals in the industry believe that the imbalance between supply and demand has contributed to the decline in the steel market.
"Steel prices rose until the fourth quarter of last year, but this year is different from last year," Zhang said. "As prices fell, so did our profits."
Iron ore, coal and coal prices have remained high since November. High raw material prices and falling steel prices have affected profits for steel companies.
In recent years, the Chinese stock market has issued a series of derivatives focusing on major commodities. Steel, iron ore, coal and coal, and its role in the steel industry have become important means for steel enterprises and traders to hedge market risks.
