(Phnom Penh): On November 29, 2018, the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie's Office of Drug Crime Investigation sent 9 male and female suspects to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court in connection with drug cases and white crystals. 36 packs (ice cubes).
And 9th: Chhun Ratana, 21 years old, was arrested by the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie in cooperation with the specialized force of the Phnom Penh Military Police Drug Investigation Office at 05:40 on 27 November. 2018 Point on concrete road and house No. 30, Lum road, Kob Kong village, Sangkat Choam Chao 2, Khan Por Sen Chey.
After interrogation, the nine men confessed to the military police that they were involved in a drug case, so the military police collected evidence and prepared a case to be sent to court for legal action.
Vietnam is seriously considering food safety and calls for more investment in food safety
(Ho Chi Minh City): The growing demand for safe food and clear sources is seen as giving a lot of opportunities to food producers in Vietnam. This is according to a quote from Vietnam News on Thursday afternoon, November 29, 2018.
The comments were made at a two-day international forum organized by the International Finance Corporation (IFC) on food security in Ho Chi Minh City, during which there was a discussion on investment opportunities. Provide safe food and promote a safe food culture that can help companies gain business opportunities, create new jobs and contribute to economic growth.
At present, as the Vietnamese economy is booming, consumers are increasingly demanding, with the wealthy paying more attention to the quality and source of the food they eat. Therefore, it is a golden opportunity for food producers to supply safe food and clear sources to meet the needs of consumers in Vietnam.
Supreme Advisory Council seeks justice for 10 families in Siem Reap until authorities agree to hand over land titles
(Siem Reap): Ten families living in Anchanh village, Nokor Thom commune, Siem Reap city / province, where the authorities have refused to issue land titles for many years, now the authorities have agreed to issue them land titles. After requesting and finding solutions from officials of the Supreme Advisory Council.
In 2016, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, decided to grant land ownership to about 31 families who cut down, used and cultivated land in Anchanh village, Nokor Thom commune, Siem Reap city. However, at that time, the authorities decided to hand over the titles to only 21 families, while 10 other families did not issue titles, claiming that the land occupied by the 10 families was too large.
The 10 families have been protesting for their land titles from the authorities, but to no avail. Recently, Mr. Nuon Sokhavy, President of the New Light Party and a member of the Supreme Advisory Council, went to study and find a solution for these 10 families.
After understanding the problem, on November 28, there was a joint meeting with the participation of the delegation of the Supreme Advisory Council, led by Mr. Nuon Sokhavy and his colleagues and the Deputy Governor of Siem Reap in charge of administration. Provinces and associates as well as advisors and lawyers of APSARA Authority.
Mr. Nuon Sokhavy told Fresh News on November 29, 2018 that after the joint meeting, there was a good solution: the provincial authorities and the Apsara Authority agreed to hand over the land to the 10 families. However, the people have not yet received the title deed, waiting for the Siem Reap Provincial Cadastral Office to continue the actual procedure and issue the title to them.
Mr. Nuon Sokhavy hopes that officials from the Siem Reap Provincial Cadastral Office will expedite the issuance of title deeds to these 10 families. For Mr. Sokha Vy, helping to claim land titles for these 10 families is his first success in solving problems for the people as a member of the Supreme Advisory Council.
The member of the Supreme Advisory Council expressed his happiness for the solution to the 10 families, as well as to solve social problems for the Royal Government.
"The task of this Supreme Advisory Council is very useful in eradicating corruption in this society effectively." Mr. Nuon Sokhavy confirmed.
However, the member of the Supreme Advisory Council also expressed dissatisfaction with some authorities who still do not value the duties and responsibilities of the Supreme Advisory Council and always ask for letters of mission. When they go to find solutions to inactive problems in the provinces.
It should be noted that after the 2018 National Election, in order to gather intellectual and intellectual resources to help solve social problems, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, decided to establish the Supreme Advisory Council with members from political parties. 16 The delegates from these 16 political parties have been given the same status as senior ministers to facilitate their work.
The members of the Supreme Advisory Council have been given the right by Samdech Techo to report all issues directly to Samdech without infecting others.
Through this role, it is seen that the members of the Supreme Advisory Council have been actively working to help solve problems in society, as well as to help review and advise on draft laws before submitting to the Royal The government also approved.
The Ministry of Social Affairs and nearly 50 other partners open a forum to discuss social welfare development action plans
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation and nearly 50 other partners on November 29, 2018, opened a forum to discuss the action plan for social welfare development. Dissemination meeting on "Social Welfare Development Action Plan and Summary of Work Report for the first nine months of 2018" was held to discuss the positive and negative points as well as some challenges in the field of social welfare.
The ceremony was attended by Mr. Touch Channy, Director General of the General Department of Technical Affairs, Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, Ministry of Social Affairs, Department of Social Affairs and other partners in the provinces.
Mr. Touch Channy said that the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation has three major priority areas: the social sector, the veterans sector and the youth rehabilitation sector. As a result, the Ministry of Social Affairs has contributed to the welfare of victims and vulnerable people of all kinds in society, both materially and spiritually, as well as providing social services with remarkable results.
