Nearly 1,000 hectares of dry paddy fields in Kratie city's Roka Kandal commune were inundated by rain for two days in a row
(Kratie): As of the evening of November 28, 2018, nearly 1,000 hectares of farmers' dry paddy fields in Sangkat Roka Kandal, Kratie City, Kratie Province are being flooded and will be completely damaged if the flooding situation continues. Continued for a long time without timely rescue.
The unfortunate large-scale flooding of the above farmers was after the whole of Kratie province was affected by USAGI, causing two days of rain, causing floods in some places. Some submerges up to two meters deep are also available.
Citizens who grow dry season rice have urged municipal authorities to dismantle various fishing gears that block waterways in lakes, creeks and streams to release rainwater quickly. The municipal authorities said that after the flood caused by the typhoon for two nights and one day, it caused severe flooding almost everywhere in Kratie city.
Heng Rath Molida, Director of Kratie Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology, said on the evening of November 28 that he had sent his officials to cooperate with the authorities and the people to remove fishing offenses such as fishing nets and barriers. Mosquito nets in the canals, which cause water to clog the river.
