(Siem Reap): The Ministry of Tourism of Cambodia has organized a special meeting of the ASEAN Tourism Professionals Monitoring and Supervision Committee (ATPMC) from 28-30 November 2018 in Siem Reap to continue to standardize the ASEAN Spa Skills Training Program. Participation from representatives of ASEAN Ministries of Tourism, Spa Association of ASEAN countries and relevant ministries and institutions.
Mr. Pak Sokhom, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism and Deputy Minister of Tourism, Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, said at the opening ceremony that the Ministry of Tourism of Cambodia has made progress in human resource development in accordance with ASEAN mechanisms and standards. Request Cambodia to lead the development of ASEAN spa skills training standards for implementation in all ASEAN countries.
This standard will be incorporated as an appendix to the ASEAN Tourism Professionals Agreement (ASEAN MRA TP), which aims to facilitate the competence of tourism professionals in accordance with 32 ASEAN standards in hotel services and Travel services can relocate jobs in the region in accordance with common ASEAN laws and mechanisms.
In an effort to develop tourism skills for young people, the Ministry of Tourism of Cambodia has organized and implemented this ASEAN training program in tourism vocational training schools with high results and shared successful experiences to some ASEAN member countries.
Recently, the Ministry of Tourism has also developed and implemented its Cambodian Spa Capacity and Wellness Standards at Tourism Vocational Training Schools to enhance the value of this spa profession. At the same time, thousands of massage therapists are being trained.
Please be reminded that with the strong growth of national and international tourism in recent years, the tourism sector has created more than 620,000 direct jobs to date, equivalent to 13% of the total work, and in 2020 will create About 1 million direct jobs, about 1.2 million in 2025 and 2 million in 2030, not to mention tens of thousands more indirect jobs.
The Embassy of Japan in Cambodia Celebrates the 84th Birthday of the Emperor of Japan and the Last Year of His Ascension
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Horinouchi Hidehisa, Ambassador of Japan to the Kingdom of Cambodia, celebrates the Royal Birthday of His Majesty the Emperor of Japan Akihito 84 on his 85th birthday, the 30th anniversary of his accession to the throne. And as an opportunity to fulfill the role of the Emperor of Japan as well.
The celebration of the Royal Birthday of the Emperor of Japan was held on the evening of November 28, 2018 at the Embassy of Japan with the participation of Deputy Prime Minister Binh Chin, Minister in Charge of the Office of the Council of Ministers, HE Ambassadors, ambassadors of friendly countries and leaders of the Royal Government of Cambodia in large numbers.
On this occasion, Mr. Horinouchi Hidehisa stated that His Majesty Emperor Akihito will abdicate on April 30 next year, and his successor, Prince Naruhito, will ascend the throne on May 1 next year. Well.
The Japanese ambassador to Cambodia said that the 30 years since Emperor Akihito's accession to the throne were from the process of seeking peace to the development of Cambodia today, as well as a time of strengthening and expanding ties. Remarkable friendship between Japan and Cambodia.
Deputy Prime Minister Binh Minh said that since 1990, Japan has played an important role in Cambodia's peace process and further peacebuilding. At the same time, Japan contributed greatly to the post-war rehabilitation of Cambodia and contributed to the socio-economic development of Cambodia.
