The new Ambassador of Laos congratulates the National Assembly on entrusting Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin to lead the National Assembly of Cambodia.
Samdech Heng Samrin praised and appreciated the efforts of the Lao Embassy in Cambodia, which has acted as a representative of a successful diplomatic mission in strengthening bilateral relations and cooperation between the two nations.
On behalf of the National Assembly, Samdech emphasized that the National Assembly of Cambodia fully supports the Ambassador's mission and pledges to cooperate fully to ensure the success of Lok Phak's diplomatic mission in Cambodia, and Samdech Heng Samrin highly appreciated the progress of relations. Traditional friendship, solidarity and cooperation in all fields between the Party, State, Government, as well as the National Assembly of Cambodia and Laos have been constantly evolving.
Regarding the cooperation between the two parliaments, Samdech Heng Samrin stated that the National Assembly of Cambodia of the 6th legislature will continue to strengthen parliamentary diplomatic relations through bilateral and multilateral cooperation, especially to continue close cooperation with the Lao National Assembly and Support each other on inter-parliamentary forums to serve the common interests of the people of the two countries.
At the same time, Mr. Amphay Khin Davong congratulated the results of the 6th National Assembly election and congratulated the National Assembly of Cambodia for giving confidence to Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin to continue to lead the National Assembly in the new term.
The Ambassador emphasized that in order to further strengthen the relationship and cooperation between the Party, State and the people of Cambodia and Laos, in December, Cambodian dignitaries including Samdech Heng Samrin and Samdech Hun Sen and others will be visiting Laos.
Mr. Amphai Khin Davong said that during Samdech Techo Hun Sen's official and friendly visit to Laos, the two governments will sign a memorandum of understanding on education, culture and electricity. The two countries will also discuss trade issues, especially double tax exemption and extradition.
