Ministry of Interior Establishes Working Group to Organize Meeting to Accelerate Trial Proceedings After Prison Overcrowding
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior, has issued a decision to establish a working group to prepare the contents of the meeting to promote the acceleration of trial proceedings and issue a final verdict or verdict after the overcrowding in the prison. Up by birth of the inmate. This is according to the decision received by Fresh News on November 29, 2018.
The working group is composed of 11 people, led by Mr. Sak Setha, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior, with Mr. Pao Hamphan, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior, and Mr. Keut Rith, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Justice as the Deputy Chairman.
It should be noted that the decision to establish this working group was made after Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, agreed to the request of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, for all relevant ministries and institutions to hold a meeting to resolve Overcrowding in prisons comes after the number of inmates across the country increased.
According to the request of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng on November 08, 2018, said that so far the prison situation is overcrowded in almost all prisons across the country, as of September 30, 2018, the number of detainees A total of 31,008 people, of which 22,295 detainees are in court proceedings, accounting for 71.9%, and in addition, some detainees have not yet had a final verdict or verdict, although the court has tried It's over.
The request of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng to report to Samdech Techo Hun Sen that these issues have made it very difficult to control the implementation of the sentence, as well as the implementation of the procedure to commute and pardon prisoners in accordance with the law.
The following is the decision of the Ministry of Interior: Minister of Health: In 2018, no Cambodian people died of malaria
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Health, Prof. Mam Bunheng, stated that the Ministry of Health and related partners are jointly committed to eradicate all types of malaria in Cambodia by 2025 and maintain a zero mortality rate. In the first 11 months of 2018, there were no deaths due to malaria.
This statement was made by the Minister at the Advisory Meeting on the Progress of the Provincial Working Group on Malaria Eradication (IPMF) and Malaria Eradication Strategy on 28 November 2018 This is at the office of the Ministry of Health, with the participation of health officials from all 25 provinces and cities, with the invitation of the Technical Director General of the Ministry of Health, Dr. O Vandin and relevant national and international partners.
The Minister of Health said, "In 2018, we used 3 million insecticide-treated mosquito nets to distribute to people living in malaria-prone areas. In particular, people migrating to the mountains. "Without knowing the exact basis, we have already set up a ministry agency to distribute educational mosquito nets and test them, and if they see any malaria symptoms, give them medicine immediately."
At the same time, Minister Mam Bunheng also called on people with fever and sweating to come to the hospital or health center and have village volunteers to test them for malaria and get medicine. Immediately to recover. In addition, people living in vulnerable areas must use colored mosquito nets to ensure safety.
According to the director of the National Center for Malaria Control, Parasitology and Bacteriology, Dr. Huy Rekul confirmed that from January to the end of November, there were 30,000 cases of malaria, of which 10,000 were serious cases. And no deaths. India launches more than 30 satellites into space
