(Phnom Penh): On the morning of November 29, 2018, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, led a high-level delegation to pay an official visit and attend the Asia-Pacific Summit in Nepal. November 30 to December 3, 2018. To find out what the Asia-Pacific Summit means, read the following document:
The Asia-Pacific Summit 2018 - Nepal will be held in Kathmandu, Nepal from November 30 to December 3, 2018. The theme of the summit is "Addressing the Most Important Challenges of Our Time: Mutual Reliability, Mutual Prosperity and Global Values."
The Global Peace Federation, in partnership with the government, civil society and the private sector, has launched a free international summit to find solutions to key challenges in this era:
* "The First African Summit for Peace and Human Development" in Gaddafi, Senegal in January 2018, with more than 1,200 participants from 60 countries.
Nepal is scheduled to invite a high-level delegation from the Asia-Pacific region and other parts of the world to attend the summit, including the current and former heads of state, parliamentary speakers, parliamentarians, religious leaders and leaders. Gender and media representation, academia, business, the arts, and civil society.
Note: UPF Cambodia representative confirmed that UPF has made a separate invitation for National Assembly members and senators to attend the summit. The two legislatures have not yet responded, receiving information about the leadership of the Cambodian delegation invited by the Prime Minister to attend the Asia-Pacific Summit. Therefore, it is not necessary for both institutions to send a delegation to participate in this separate invitation.
