The Minister of Agriculture advises officials to take good care of state property!
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Mr. Veng Sakhon, this morning, November 29, 2018, closed the training course on state property management.
The 3-day training was co-organized by the Inspector General of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, the Inspector General of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, together with the relevant departments, for the following purposes:
1: Provide opportunities for professional officers to learn from each other's experiences, analyze strengths, weaknesses, challenges in the implementation of the reform program, control system and state property management system as an input to strengthen the implementation and Improve inspection procedures for the agricultural sector.
2. Contribute to the implementation of the Royal Government's policy, strategic plan and effective human resource development in strengthening good governance and combating corruption, inactivity and respect for the rule of law within the framework of the Royal Government's in-depth reforms.
The Minister informed the ceremony that the topic of state property management is important in that each unit must be responsible for the loss of state property and must take care to maintain state property. Good.
The Minister instructed the heads of all units to pay attention to high responsibility and implement the following key points:
Second, to audit the management of inventory of state assets effectively, transparently and accountably.
Third, prepare an inventory of the base year, recording in detail all the state assets as movable and immovable property under the management of the unit, which should be done every 5 years, called the base year.
Fourth, the unit must complete the real estate registration form and apply for the certificate of identification of the owner of the immovable property or the title of possession of all immovable and immovable property to the Ministry in order to submit to the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction Economic land, social land concessions and other state property concessions.
Fifth, each time each project is completed, please, Mr. and Mrs. Chairman of all project management units, cooperate with the state unit to prepare the form for handing-over of those assets and record them in the inventory of state assets and provide all relevant documents. Ministry Inventory Committee to monitor, evaluate and manage.
Sixth, continue to implement the Notification No. 9339 KSAK dated October 26, 2017 on the management of the presence of civil servants and contracted officials to be more effective.
