This Morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Visits and Participates in the Asia-Pacific Summit in Nepal
(Phnom Penh): At the invitation of the Prime Minister of Nepal, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, this morning, November 29, 2018, led a high-level delegation to pay an official visit and attend the Asia-Pacific Summit in Phnom Penh. Nepal.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's visit is the first historic visit by the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia to Nepal since the two countries re-established diplomatic ties on September 7, 1999.
According to a statement from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, Samdech Techo and his delegation will spend about three days from November 30 to December 2, 2018 to visit and attend the Asia Summit. - Pacific in Nepal.
During the official visit, Samdech Techo Hun Sen will pay a courtesy call on the President of the Democratic Republic of Nepal, Ms. Bhatya Devi Bandavi, and also hold bilateral talks with the Prime Minister of the Republic of Khatga Prasad Samaoli. Federal Democratic Republic of Nepal. The two leaders will then preside over the signing ceremony of a number of bilateral cooperation documents.
In particular, on the occasion of attending the Asia-Pacific Summit 2018 in Nepal, Samdech Techo Hun Sen will deliver a speech in line with the theme of the Asia-Pacific Summit 2018-Nepal "Addressing the key challenges of our era: Dependence "Mutual prosperity and universal values."
During his stay in Nepal, the Prime Minister will visit the ancient town of Patan Duba, a UNESCO World Heritage Site.
The Cambodian dignitaries who will accompany Samdech Techo Prime Minister include: Mr. Prak Sokhon, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, other members of the Royal Government of Cambodia and representatives from the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce.
Please note that Samdech Techo Hun Sen's trip abroad today is the 13th trip abroad in 2018.
The following is the history of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's mission abroad in 2018:
8th: Samdech Techo led a delegation to attend the 73rd General Assembly of the United Nations General Assembly and other relevant meetings for 4 days from September 27, 2018 to September 30 Miss in New York, USA.
The 9th: Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, leads a high-level Cambodian delegation to attend the 10th Mekong-Japan Summit in Tokyo, Japan from October 6 to 10, 2018. Then continue to Bali, Indonesia to attend the ASEAN Leaders Meeting from October 10-12, 2018.
The 12th: Samdech Techo Hun Sen leads a delegation to attend the 33rd ASEAN Summit and related summits in Singapore for 3 days from November 13-15.
