Minister of Tourism urges stakeholders to participate in the 3rd Model Tourism Resort Competition and the 2nd Model Tourism Community
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, Ministry of Tourism, urges all stakeholders, including the public, private, people-tourists and development partners, to participate in the 3rd Model Resort Competition and the 2nd Model Tourism Community Competition. 2019, which has just been announced to be implemented from November 28, 2018 onwards.
The launch of the two movements was held at the Phnom Penh Hotel, following a review workshop on the "Second Model Tourism Resort Competition" and the "Second Model Community Tourism and Ecotourism Competition". 1 ".
To promote the effective implementation of these two movements, the Minister made the following recommendations:
First. Investment: Continue to promote the development and investment of all types of tourist resorts and tourism communities that consider the environment, cleanliness and society. In this regard, the specialized department of the Ministry of Tourism must prepare guidelines and criteria for tourism and community development projects that need to take into account the environment, culture and social protection as a basis for evaluation of those projects.
Second. Management: Capital-Provincial Departments of Tourism must strive to encourage all tourism resorts and tourism communities to have clear managers and have a clear management structure and must encourage all resorts and tourism communities to have a clear development plan. . Must continue to make efforts to manage and develop tourist resorts and tourism communities in their locality well.
At the same time, the Ministry of Tourism, the Capital and Provincial Departments of Tourism must cooperate to promote public awareness to staff and tourists who visit the resorts and tourism communities about proper garbage disposal and to prepare a code of conduct. About do's and don'ts to promote to tourist resorts across the country.
Fifth. Dissemination: The Capital-Provincial Department of Tourism must continue to encourage all resorts and tourism communities to participate in various races, especially these two model races.
Sixth. Private Sector: The private sector, especially travel agencies, must organize tours and bring more tourists to all resorts and communities across the country, especially resorts and community winners in these two model racing movements. At the same time, prepare a lot of local tour packages for people, students, private employees, workers, civil servants with reasonable prices to all tourist destinations across the country.
