He added that the import of salt is really on time, while the salt in stock in Cambodia ran out. The price of imported salt is $ 90 per ton, but the selling price in Cambodia is not yet known because the association has not yet paid.
He stated that 5,000 tons of salt supply to the Cambodian market is not enough to import 30,000 tons. Salt will continue to be imported from other countries until the salt production season, but if the season is over and Cambodia can no longer produce salt, it is necessary to continue importing.
The decision to import salt from China is due to the fact that Cambodia is facing a shortage of salt supply due to unsustainable salt production due to the rainy weather. The risk of salt shortage this year is due to the Salt Producers Association not being able to produce due to the changeable weather this year, ie the sky is constantly raining.
Please note that this is the second time that Cambodia faces a shortage of salt, that is, in 2008 Cambodia experienced this problem. In particular, in 2016, Cambodia produced about 140,000 tons of salt, which is more than the demand. In general, the supply is only 100,000 tons, but for 2017-2018, salt production will decline due to climatic factors and will have to import salt from other countries.
