Discover Nepal where Samdech Techo Hun Sen will Visit and Participate in the Asia-Pacific Summit
(Nepal): Nepal, a South Asian country, will host the Asia-Pacific Summit on November 29, 2018, in the presence of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. This meeting, too.
The following is the general situation in Nepal:
* Official name: Federal Democratic Republic of Nepal
Government: Federal Republic, with both President and Prime Minister
Density: 180 people per square kilometer
* Driving directions: Left
1: Land and climate
Nepal has a maximum length of 800 km and a maximum width of 200 km. It is divided into three regions: mountains, plateaus and plains. The country covers an area of 147,181 square kilometers and has a population of about 28 million. Nepal is the 93rd largest country in the world and the 41st most populous country in the world.
81.3% of Nepalis are Hindus, which is the highest percentage of Hindus in the world. Buddhism has been a religion since ancient times, but now only 9 percent practice, 4.4 percent of Muslims, 3.1 percent of Kiratism, 1.4 percent of Christianity. Other spirits make up 0.4 percent.
Nepal is still a low-income developing country, ranking 145th out of 187 countries, according to 2014 figures. Nevertheless, Nepal continues to fight hunger and poverty. The government has vowed to secede from the world's least developed countries by 2022.
5: Tradition
In the lowlands, most people build bamboo houses that want to be tightly connected, while the walls are made of mud mixed with cow dung because it can keep cool for the summer, instead it is warm for the winter. In the highlands, bricks are used for walls and thatch or roof tiles. But for high-rise buildings, cement is used to make walls and planks for roofing.
