According to the announcement of the National Examination Committee, which was received by Fresh News on the evening of November 28, 2018, Ms. Thorn Ratana passed the entrance exam for the basic school year for the bachelor's degree at Health Training Institute, 2018-2019 academic year.
Studying at a medical university is the desire of this motodup driver's daughter. But initially, Ratana was very desperate to achieve this goal, even though she passed the A-level exam with the highest score.
Despair because she thinks that going to medical school, even if she gets a scholarship, she may not be able to afford the cost of school supplies and other expenses.
After hearing the young woman's concerns through Fresh News, the President of the Cambodian Red Cross, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, came out to end her worries and encouraged her to apply for the college exam. The announcement covers all the expenses for her study needs as well.
With this excellent result, Miss Ratana was very happy. She also thanked Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen for encouraging her and helping to achieve great goals in this life.
Ratana is committed to study hard to achieve its goals and contribute to the well-being of the Cambodian people. Especially in return for the great gratitude of Samdech Kittipritthbandit. Nationwide anti-drug campaign for November 28 Result: 10 cases cracked, 17 arrested
