* The results of the crackdown include: 10 cases, 17 arrests
Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign on November 28: 677 illegal vehicles were found and 325 fines were imposed.
(Phnom Penh): The nationwide traffic law enforcement campaign for November 28, 2018, the traffic police force inspected 3,368 vehicles and found 352 vehicles violating the law (59% motorcycles), 352 education vehicles and 325 fines. This is according to the official report of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department of the General Commission of the National Police.
According to the report, 1,705 helmets and goggles were inspected on November 28, 208 education helmets and 262 helmets were fined.
For the results of the 28-day inspection from November 1 to 28, the police inspected 123,458 vehicles and found 24,326 offending vehicles (79% motorcycles), including 6 education, 735 units and fined 17,591 units. Cambodia will create a special tourist site to extend the stay of guests, today inter-ministerial discussion on the draft sub-decree to create this special tourist site
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism, together with other professional institutions, this morning, November 28, 2018, met to review and discuss the draft sub-decree on the establishment of special tourism areas, while officials claim that special tourism areas are new tourism products. In promoting tourist attraction from all over the world.
Mr. Tith Chantha, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Tourism, stated that the goal of establishing special tourism areas is to diversify new tourism products to promote national and international tourism attraction and also to provide job opportunities, create employment opportunities, income and improve product quality. And tourism services Delaying the stay of tourists attracts investment, especially investment in tourism.
Mr. Tith Chantha affirmed that the establishment of this special tourist area is focused on promoting environmental development in the socio-economic framework as a whole and also to turn potential tourism areas into tourist sites or tourist sites. Especially as a collection of fitness products, tourism services and other tourism support services.
The Secretary of State said that although tourism is growing at more than 10% per year, which is a source of pride for Cambodia, tourism will decline if Cambodia does not develop more new tourism products.
He said that Cambodia currently relies heavily on cultural potential, but in order to attract more tourists, Cambodia should create more and more new tourism products. That is why Cambodia pays attention to organize this special tourist site.
He recalled that from the perspective of the Royal Government, which plans to attract about 30 million tourists, both national and international, by 2030, of course, we can not rely entirely on cultural and natural tourism as today, but we Efforts must be made to develop new tourism skills, such as processed tourism, to complement the potential of cultural and nature tourism.
However, Mr. Tith Chantha expects that the special tourist area that will be formed in the future through this sub-decree, it will be a new tourism product to attract active tourists as this special tourist area is concentrated by tourist area. Which has the most attractive potential.
Please be informed that in the first 10 months of 2018, Cambodia received more than 4.9 million international tourists, an increase of about 11% compared to the same period last year. At the same time, it is expected that throughout 2018, Cambodia will receive about 6 million international tourists and about 10 million national tourists, an increase of more than 10% compared to last year.
The Royal Government of Canada continues to provide assistance to Cambodia on border defense skills training (Video Inside) (Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Canada has decided to resume border security skills training to Cambodian officials after a hiatus and expects that relations between Cambodia and the country Canada is growing further as Cambodia claims to be doing something democratic and holding regular elections.
In a meeting with Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, on the afternoon of November 27, 2018, Canadian Ambassador to Cambodia Donica Pottie stated that Canada is pleased to provide border security training to Cambodia is back after the funds that helped in this area were temporarily suspended.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng told the Ambassador that a large number of Cambodians went to the polls in July 2018, which clearly shows that the majority of people have exercised their rights in accordance with the law. That real democracy.
As for civil society organizations, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng told Ms. Donica Pottie that the Royal Government of Cambodia has enhanced cooperation between the Royal Government and associations and non-governmental organizations, especially the establishment of a working group to consult and not require notification. Authorities before taking action. General Ith Sarath inspects the preparation of the 2019 Golden Dragon Training Ground in Chum Kiri District, Kampot Province
(Kampot): General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander and Joint Chief of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Chairman of the Steering Committee for the Golden Dragon Exercise 2019, this morning, November 28, 2018, inspected the field preparation. Training "Cambodia-China Golden Dragon Exercise 2019" in Chum Kiri District, Kampot Province.
The inspection was also accompanied by military officers, artillery, tanks, engineering, radio communication, Air Force, Air Force, Gendarmerie, Security Team and 70th Brigade, 911 Parachute Special Brigade, along with other relevant institutions. Well.
The Golden Dragon Exercise 2019 is scheduled to take place in March 2019, which is larger than the Golden Dragon Exercise 2018. This was confirmed by General Ith Sarath at the field in Chum Kiri district, Kampot province.
