Mr. Sithak Visai mentioned the annual rotation meeting between the three city headquarters, Phnom Penh, Hanoi and Vientiane, agreeing on many issues and continuing the cooperation between the three cities and will solve the problem. Together in a peaceful framework, and if any problems arise, we will solve them together. Ratanakkiri Joint Police Confiscate Nearly 100 Pieces of Koki Timber Traded in Cashew Farm in Vern Sai District
(Ratanakkiri): Coalition forces including the National Armed Forces, Provincial Armed Forces, Vern Sai District Local Armed Forces and Vern Sai District Forestry Administration on November 28, 2018 confiscated 90 pieces of Koki wood hidden in traders. Cashew plantation is located in Phang village, Vern Sai commune, Vern Sai district, Rattanakiri province.
Lieutenant Colonel Khy Sokha, director of the Technical and Security Department of the Provincial Gendarmerie, told Fresh News Agency in Ratanakkiri province that the case of confiscation of the timber after receiving information from villagers reported and asked for advice from higher authorities to crack down. Lt. Col. Khy Sokha said that the team collected 90 pieces of wood from different places, one place first.
Currently, the above timber was transported to be stored at Vern Sai commune hall to find a way to transport and store at the Forestry Administration.
It should be noted that despite the efforts of the competent authorities and relevant institutions to crack down, there are still a lot of smugglers who are not afraid of the law at all.
Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone Camcontrol Branch Brings a Mobile Test Vehicle to Check the Quality of Goods at Dei Huy Market, No Chemical Products Found
