Samdech Techo Hun Sen confirmed this on the occasion that Samdech continued to meet with nearly 20,000 workers in Kandal Stung district, Kandal province this morning, November 28, 2018.
Addressing the workers, Samdech Techo Hun Sen recalled the political situation in Cambodia after the 2013 election in which the former opposition party attempted to overthrow the legitimate government that emerged from the election through protests over the election results.
Samdech Techo recalled that at that time, the protesters led by the former opposition party used the wrong language until "Hun Sen, go down!" This is evidence that they want to overthrow the legitimate government that emerged from the election.
The demonstrations of the former CNRP lasted for a year from July 2013 to July 2014. The protests caused millions of dollars in damage to public and private property, as well as severe economic losses.
However, for the July 2018 election, national and international institutions praised the maturity and smooth operation until more than 83% of the people voted, of which about 77% Voted for the CPP as well.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen considers that the participation of more than 80 percent of the people is the success of the democratic process in Cambodia. For this election, up to 20 parties participated in the election.
Samdech said that after the election, the wages of workers have increased, the people are safe, which shows that people voted to maintain peace and development of their country.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also reacted to the opposition propaganda that the workers' salaries have increased due to criticism from the opposition. Samdech questioned that now there is no former opposition party, why is the salary of workers increased to $ 182 per month.
(Prey Veng): Mr. Kem Rath Viseth, Secretary of State of the Office of the Council of Ministers and Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Civil Society Forum, presented 695 water filters donated by the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen to the people in Kamchay Mear district for 695 families to contribute to solving the problem of clean water for the people.
On the occasion of handing over the water filters on November 27, 2018, Mr. Kem Rath Viseth also thanked Huawei Cambodia for sponsoring a total of 2,941 water filters. Equivalent to 100,000 US dollars to Samdech Techo Hun Sen to distribute to people who face water shortages, with the forum of the Civil Society Alliance as a facilitator.
