Trade Minister urges UAE to invest in four key areas to accelerate Cambodia's economic growth
(Dubai): Four major sectors, including agriculture, tourism, industry and infrastructure, have been urged by the Cambodian Minister of Commerce, Mr. Pan Sosak, to invest in Cambodia to accelerate economic growth and reduce poverty in line with the fourth phase of the Rectangular Strategy. Of the Royal Government.
The Minister made the request during a bilateral meeting with REEM Al Hashimy, Minister of International Cooperation and Chair of the United Arab Emirates Dubai World Expo 2020 on Tuesday, November 27. 2018 to strengthen economic and trade relations.
On that occasion, Minister Pan Sosak informed Ms. Rim Al-Hashimi about the progress of Cambodia's economic growth, the vision of the Royal Government, the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4, investment protection policies and other incentives that the Royal Government has provided to foreign investors. Doing business in Cambodia.
The Minister also invited the United Arab Emirates to participate in the international "Cambodian Products and Export-Import of Cambodia" event, which is scheduled to be held in December 2019 to find business partners and promote the Dubai World Expo 2020 to the people. Cambodia and the people of ASEAN countries.
In response, Minister Rim al-Hashimi thanked Mr. Pan Sosak for sharing good information on investment opportunities in Cambodia and promised to encourage the private sector of the United Arab Emirates to study investment opportunities in Cambodia as well as participate. Exhibition organized by the Ministry of Commerce.
In addition, Ms. Rim al-Hashimi expressed her intention to visit Cambodia in the near future to better understand the potential of Cambodia's rich tourism and culture to strengthen diplomatic relations and cooperation between the two countries. .
Prime Minister Hun Sen calls for an end to all union cases in court by 2018 (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, calls for an end to all union cases in court By 2018, the prince also urged all union leaders who are in court to send a proposal to the Minister of Labor and Vocational Training.
Therefore, Samdech urged the union to send a request to the Minister of Labor so that the Minister of Labor, Mr. Ith Sam Heng, can continue to work with the Minister of Justice, Mr. Ang Vong Vathana, as well as the judiciary to solve the problem quickly, that is, to Completed by 2018, not delayed until 2019.
The Prime Minister made this statement on the occasion that Samdech Techo continued to meet with a total of nearly 18,000 workers from 12 factories in Kandal province. The meeting took place in Kraing Sbov village, Preah Puth commune, Kandal Steung district, Kandal province on the morning of November 28, 2018.
Samdech Techo said, "I call on all unions to file a complaint, please send the complaint to the Minister of Labor and Vocational Training for the Minister of Labor and Vocational Training to work with the Ministry of Justice and "Work with the court to quickly resolve any issues related to complaints against union leaders or relevant NGOs."
He added that the court is also speeding up the investigation to close the investigation when it closes and the court will conclude or proceed to trial. Samdech Techo emphasized that if it is taken to trial, it must be cleared immediately or it will be dropped and not handled immediately (reserved, not handled).
According to the Prime Minister, some unions while in office are also under the influence of lawsuits, which is not a good thing. The freedom of association of the unions is not yet fully achieved, so the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training should cooperate with the Ministry of Justice, and through the Ministry of Justice, work with the courts to close cases related to the activities of unions representing Workers.
The head of the Royal Government stated that these are also part of the guarantee of labor rights, political rights and labor rights of unions and workers. But let everyone respect the law, factory owners also respect the law, workers also respect the law, whoever respects the law, rights, freedoms and labor productivity will occur in the factory. Earthquake hits northern Japan and could cause sea level fluctuations
