(Anlong Veng, Oddar Meanchey): Anlong Veng district, Oddar Meanchey province, is the last sanctuary of the former Khmer Rouge leaders and also the last territory to achieve complete peace under a win-win policy issued by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the founder of Win-Win politics, once said that bringing the Khmer Rouge to take refuge under the roof of the Royal Government was a step in the right direction, but could not be completely successful without considering the construction of connected infrastructure as well. The construction of various achievements that are the needs of the people in Anlong Veng district.
This spirit has made Anlong Veng district receive the attention of the Royal Government for the development of this miserable land, as well as other areas. Education is one of the four priority areas that the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, pays close attention to.
Under the leadership of former Khmer Rouge leader Anlong Veng, there was only one school built by Ta Mok during 1993, which was three stories high. To date, school buildings in Anlong Veng district have been constructed to provide education for the children of Anlong Veng district.
At present, Anlong Veng district has 16 community kindergartens with 16 classrooms with a total of 300 students and 16 teachers, and 2 private kindergartens with 7 classrooms with a total of 214 students and 7 teachers.
Of these, 14 new buildings with 144 classrooms on seven schools were provided by Samdech Techo Hun Sen during his return visit to Anlong Veng district in 2016.
Anlong Veng High School, a school left behind by the Ta Mok era and one of the places where Samdech Techo Hun Sen traveled to bring Khmer Rouge soldiers to live under the roof of the Royal Government in 1999, is under development. Progress, too. Currently, this high school has more than 17,000 students and many of the graduates are working.
The increase in the number of students has also made the high school lack a school building. In 2016, during his visit to Anlong Veng district again, Samdech Techo Hun Sen sponsored a new school building with a height of 3 floors equal to 30 rooms to meet the study needs of students.
The principal of Anlong Veng High School, Mr. Sreng Koma, who went to work in Anlong Veng district in 2006, was very happy because he did not expect that this rural school would have such a skyscraper.
Mr. Sreng Koma stated, "We could not have imagined that in our rural area there is such a huge school building as a gift from the Prime Minister." "He donated a lot of money, including the infrastructure in the school, all the concrete roads, as well as football, basketball, volleyball, he helped make it all."
The high school principal also praised Samdech Techo Hun Sen's win-win policy to bring peace and provide opportunities for the children of Anlong Veng district to get an education.
"Previously, because this was a war zone and the latest integration, it was very difficult to study. So far, for 20 years, the implementation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's win-win policy has made the area peaceful and given the people of the area the opportunity to study and develop more human resources. In particular, students have continued their studies in college, and some have come out to work in other institutions. Mr. Sreng Komar added.
