(Phnom Penh): The assailant who stabbed to death a man in Phnom Penh's Sen Sok district who escaped for more than two weeks was searched and arrested in Stung Treng province, but he also decided to commit suicide by hanging himself. In the temporary detention room in Stung Treng Provincial Police on the night of November 27, 2018.
The suspect who hanged himself in this murder case was named Chheng Nin, 41 years old, a construction worker living at the construction site on Concrete Road, Samrong Teav Village, Sangkat Kraing Thnong, Khan Sen Sok, was released by the Deputy Prosecutor of Phnom Penh Municipal Court. Order No. 326. Dated November 16, 2018, ordered to enter.
Colonel Ho Meng Wang, Police Inspector of Sen Sok District, confirmed that on November 27, 2018 at 17:45, the Police Inspectorate of Sen Sok District cooperated with the Serious Criminal Police Force of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police and the Criminal Police Department. The Ministry of Interior and the police force of Stung Treng Provincial Police have arrested a suspect named Chheng Nin in connection with the murder (stabbing and stabbing to death).
The inspector said that this case happened on November 5, 2018 at 21:00 on the concrete road at the construction site, Samrong Teav village, Sangkat Kraing Thnong, Khan Sen Sok, caused by one suspect. With a sharp knife.
