(Kandal): In the morning of Wednesday, November 28, 2018, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, continued to meet with a total of 17,912 workers. From 12 factories in Kandal province. The meeting took place in Kraing Sbov village, Preah Puth commune, Kandal Steung district, Kandal province.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen starts a talk with nearly 20,000 workers in Kandal Steung district, Kandal province this morning, November 28, 2018
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that as a leader in a sovereign state, he has to work both abroad and in the country
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen also asked for understanding and tolerance from workers who have not been invited by Samdech to meet.
* Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, said before that Cambodia is trying to deploy schools, now it is trying to deploy factories near people's homes.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that his current visit to meet with workers is to do what he promised before the election.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech took the issue of workers as an important issue to promote the building of society by promoting this industry.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that with only one month left, workers will receive a salary of 182 US dollars per month and will be paid every two weeks.
* Samdech Techo Prime Minister said that compared to the beginning in 1997, workers received only $ 47, but now wages are higher and higher than some countries.
* Samdech Techo stated that the presentation of wages in other countries is to give workers a basis to consider, that is, not to demand higher wages, to look at job competition with other countries, if not Therefore, it can cause the loss of factories in Cambodia.
* The Prime Minister said that the decision to increase wages to $ 182, the Royal Government must reduce the price of electricity to factories.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia is as it is today, workers must not forget the efforts of the Cambodian People's Party to end the war and bring peace.
* The Prime Minister said that if there is only peace, there is no development, it is impossible, that is, peace and development must be linked without missing any part.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that exports amounted to more than 12 billion US dollars, which was a success under the leadership of Samdech and the Cambodian People's Party. Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the people for their support of the Cambodian People's Party and Samdech's leadership for more than 30 years.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the election of the workers is not only an election in support of the Cambodian People's Party, but also an election to protect and preserve the achievements of their grandparents, as well as to vote for themselves.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the turnout of more than 80 percent of the people is the success of the democratic process in Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that a Royal Government cannot be overthrown through street activities. The Prime Minister added that the activities of overthrowing the government of the opposition in 2013 will be life threatening if they act beyond the red line.
* The Prime Minister stated that the wage increase in 2019 was not demanded by the opposition. At this point, Samdech wants to show that the wage increase does not need to be shouted at by the opposition.
* Samdech Techo appealed to all factories to be ready to implement the payment of $ 182 to workers in 2019 and to be open every two weeks.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen estimates that by the end of 2018, about 60,000 children will be born this year and about 6 million dollars will be provided to support them.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that an advance budget of approximately US $ 22 million was taken to address the workers who were fired by their employers.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the past, in Kandal Stung district, there were no factories, without which these workers would have to migrate to find work or could still farm with their parents.
* Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government, emphasized that there is no stability, no peace, no investors and no tourists.
* The Prime Minister stated that in a meeting with the French company that manages Phnom Penh International Airport, the company expressed unimaginable growth in tourists in Cambodia and supported the establishment of airports in Phnom Penh and Siem Reap.
* Samdech Techo further stated that the airport in Sihanoukville must be expanded, which may receive about 3 million guests in the coming days.
* Samdech Prime Minister continued to remind factory owners, enterprises and workers to work together to keep the factory community safe, not to have younger brothers and sisters, and factory owners, enterprises and workers must know how to solve problems.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen requested all union leaders who are in court to send a resolution to the Minister of Labor and the Ministry of Justice, as well as the court to resolve the issue as soon as possible.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen urged to expedite the settlement of union cases to ensure the right to freedom of work. But Samdech asked everyone to do everything under the law.
* The Prime Minister added that after the meeting with the workers, Samdech will visit the factory directly to ensure the rights and freedoms of workers and guarantee their income.
* Samdech Techo, Head of the Royal Government, reaffirmed that from now on, every New Year and Pchum Ben must release public buses on all national roads.
* At the end of this year, Samdech Techo Hun Sen will be in charge of many other overseas tasks, including: Nepal, Laos and Vietnam.
This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued to meet with nearly 20,000 workers in Kandal province
(Kandal): In the morning of Wednesday, November 28, 2018, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, continued to meet with a total of 17,912 workers. From 12 factories in Kandal province. The meeting will take place in Kraing Sbov village, Preah Puth commune, Kandal Steung district, Kandal province.
According to Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, the 12 factories that allow workers to meet with Samdech Techo Hun Sen tomorrow will be invested by 10 investors from China and Cambodia. 2. These factories consist of 5 garment factories, 1 shoe factory, 1 shoe factory, 2 garment printing, 1 construction steel factory and 2 cigarette factories.
The minister emphasized that the products from these factories are exported to international markets and supplied to domestic markets as well. Through these factories, these enterprises have created many additional occupations and jobs locally, such as renting houses, selling food, transporting and other services.
At present, Kandal province has 464 factories, enterprises and establishments with 155,138 workers with a total wage of about $ 372 million. Of which, 170 garment and footwear factories employ 137,664 workers, earning more than $ 330 million a year.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng considered the presence of factories, enterprises and establishments in Kandal province as the success of the policy of attracting investment, the national policy on employment and employment, the policy of industrial development in Cambodia, the policy on education, training, technical and vocational and The National Social Protection Policy Framework of the Royal Government of Cambodia, headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
