"Recently, the agricultural sector seems to be declining due to the growth of other sectors," said Kea Boran. However, agriculture is still a big sector to support the economy of Cambodia, and about 60% of Cambodians are still engaged in small-scale farming to support livelihoods.
He added that agriculture is an important sector in the world and can not be lacking because no one can live without food. Cambodia is a country with good resources, fertile soil can grow better, in fact, Cambodia is also ranked No. 1 with good rice.
"For AMK, although the agricultural sector is declining and the real estate sector is growing, AMK has no intention or plan to change the direction of real estate lending, it is to continue to provide agricultural loans to rural farmers to improve their livelihoods," he said. "Improve the living standards of the people and also improve the sector further."
In particular, the conference on the declaration of membership in Shanghai Commercial and Savings Bank of AMK Microfinance Institution was held to change the face to become one of the leading microfinance institutions in Cambodia in the future, especially to promote the banking sector. In Cambodia as well.
He said the decision to invest in AMK focused on a number of key factors, as well as looking at its financial strength and social mission, confidence in AMK's staff and management.
He warmly welcomed the membership of AMK. He hopes that after joining AMK will continue to play a role in promoting incredible economic growth in Cambodia and will also change the lives of people from low to middle income.
(Phnom Penh): The nationwide traffic law enforcement campaign for November 27, 2018, the traffic police force inspected 6,436 vehicles and found 1,148 vehicles (80% motorcycles), 265 education vehicles and 883 fines, according to the official report of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department of the General Commission of the National Police.
