Key remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of presiding over the closing ceremony of the 4th National Congress of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia
The 4th National Congress of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia was held on the morning of November 26, 2018 under the chairmanship of Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate and Vice President of the Cambodian People's Party.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked all relevant actors for working together to maintain the role of this youth organization.
* Samdech Techo stated that the activities of the youth did not just happen on December 2, 1978. But youth activities have taken place in the past to oppose the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen can not cut history into pieces, and without a historical perspective can not become an assessor of the situation.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen urged the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia to adhere to the principle of collective leadership of responsible individuals.
* Samdech Techo stated that if we adhere to the principle of collective leadership of responsible individuals, there will be no division.
* Samdech Techo stated that Samdech does not care what is communist or non-communist, only knows what is really happening in Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo reminded that in the past, when he went to a free country, he was called a communist, when he went to a communist country, he was called a free man, but he did not care, it was important that he belonged to Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen called the people who called the current regime communists, when they had the right to freely choose their jobs, traitors.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that today's youth have good opportunities and strong abilities compared to the previous generation, but they have not yet matured.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the younger generation must learn from the older generation because the older generation has a lot of experience.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that being a difficult leader, but must dare to sacrifice, even if the sacrifice is large enough to sacrifice life, must also be done for the benefit of society and the people.
* The Prime Minister stated that he had also reprimanded Khieu Samphan in connection with the Paris Agreement.
* The Prime Minister reminded that until today, there are many deaths.
* Samdech Techo mentioned how many leaders in the world have dared to risk their lives to enter the enemy camp.
* Samdech Techo reminded that when he received the support of the National Assembly to become the Prime Minister on January 14, 1985, he saw that it was not possible to end the war. That is why Samdech put out politics, political reform and economic reform must go hand in hand.
* Samdech Techo stated that the three repressive forces that could kill Samdech's political life include: Disagreement within the party, 2. Fear of Vietnam blocking because Cambodian and Vietnamese politics are different, while the Vietnamese army in Cambodia about 100,000 people, 3. Fear that the Soviet Union would cut off aid because at that time only the Soviet Union and Europe were donors to Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that setting goals was important in leadership, as Samdech determined that ending the war and bringing peace was the goal when Samdech became Prime Minister in 1985.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructed the youth to catch what must be caught and to strengthen their ability to rise as a nation on an equal footing with other nations.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen responds to prisoner Sam Rainsy, never changing his position because he is worried about foreign pressure as they expected.
* Samdech Techo reiterated that in order to achieve the goal, it is necessary to know the opportunities, create opportunities and seize the opportunities properly.
* Samdech Techo reprimanded the youth to continue to contribute to the protection of peace, political stability, not to let the past come back, no matter what the value, so that the color revolution does not happen in Cambodia.
* The Prime Minister calls on the youth to continue to work together to help develop the economy and society and not to trade national sovereignty for aid.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued that do not be afraid of the opposition, because if not the opposition is not the name of the opposition, but must respect the interests of the people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces to stop correspondence with prisoner Sam Rainsy, despite being bitten by Samdech.
