The 4th General Assembly of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia was also held on the 40th anniversary of its birth. The General Assembly was attended by about 1,300 leaders and members from all 25 capitals and provinces. The General Assembly was held with a focus on summarizing the work of 2012-2018 and the work direction for 2018-2020, as well as the election of members with the discussion and approval of the amendment of the statute of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia. Well.
At the General Assembly yesterday, the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia decided to add 15 more members of the Standing Committee of the Central Committee to strengthen the leadership of the 40-year-old organization.
Currently, the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia has a total of 142 members of the Central Committee, 43 newly elected members, and a total of 20 members of the Standing Committee of the Central Committee. Adding 15 new members, the number of members of the Standing Committee of the Central Committee increased to 35.
The Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia is a comprehensive front of the Cambodian Youth, which has continued the mission of the United National Rescue Youth Association of Cambodia and the Cambodian Youth Association, which was established on December 2, 1978 with the main goal of gathering young people everywhere as a united force in Contributing to building Cambodia with independence, peace, freedom, democracy and social progress.
To this day, the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia continues the spirit of unity, uniting forces to act for the benefit of Cambodian society and contribute to the Royal Government in building human resources and Cambodian society.
Speaking at the opening ceremony of the General Assembly, Mr. HUN Many, President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, emphasized that the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia will continue to participate positively to the Cambodian society, especially to continue to participate with the Royal Government, organizations, institutions, partners and individuals with a heart and mission. Together to build a stronger and more recognized Cambodia, both nationally and internationally.
