(Phnom Penh): While the authorities and the prosecutor's office charged two thieves, who are adults, with aggravated theft, when the case was sent to Mr. Ouk Sovannarith, Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, this judge Decided to change the age to 17 years (minor). This age adjustment is suspected to have taken place in order to obtain parole during the trial proceedings.
Heng Meng Hong, a male transgender judge who had just been released from prison, was arrested by Chamkar Mon district police along with another male accomplice, Pov Neou, in connection with the theft case, court officials and authorities said. The aggravating circumstance (bag seizure) was in front of the house No. 77, Street 193, corner of Street 402, Group 20, Village 3, Sangkat Tumnup Teuk, Khan Chamkar Mon, Phnom Penh on November 23, 2018.
Remarkably, after his arrest, Heng Meng Hong was charged by Deputy Prosecutor Kuch Kimlong with aggravated theft, claiming that he was 18 years old and a minor. The accused was sent to Judge Ouk Sovannarith and was suddenly transferred from 18 to 17 years old as a minor, while the other defendant was kept by Judge Ouk Sovannarith at the age of 19. .
As for Article 164 of the Penal Code, "Benefits of the Prosecution", the Prosecution shall apply to minors. If the court decides to have a minimum sentence of punishment for a minor for a felony or misdemeanor, it shall be reduced to the following separate scales:
1. If the minimum sentence of imprisonment is equal to or more than 10 years, the minimum shall be reduced to 1 year.
2. If the minimum sentence of imprisonment is equal to or more than 5 years and less than 10 years, the minimum shall be reduced to 6 months.
4. If the minimum sentence of imprisonment is equal to or more than 6 months and less than 2 years, the minimum shall be reduced to 1 day.
5: The minimum fine shall be reduced by half.
Pursuant to Articles 163 and 164 of the Penal Code, Heng Meng Hong was fortunate to be assisted by Judge Ouk Sovannarith at the age of 17 (a minor), contrary to a police report. And the closing order submitting the case for investigation by the representative of the prosecution.
It should be noted that when the police sent Heng Meng Hong to court, the parents of the accused protested and insulted the police who dared to handcuff their favorite children until they had a word with the police. Phnom Penh Municipal Court and there are photographers posting on Facebook.
Officials at the Phnom Penh Municipal Court revealed that Heng Meng Hong, who was arrested by the police during the robbery, had a large work ethic and called a court official to help him because he was hit by his niece. CamControl Increases Food Safety Restrictions in Markets Across Cambodia
