(Geneva, Switzerland): Senior Minister Ly Thuch, on behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, expressed his willingness and commitment to clear mines and explosive remnants of war by 2025.
Senior Minister Ly Thuch, on behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Chairman of the Mine Action Authority, led a Cambodian delegation to the 17th Meeting of the States Parties to the Convention on the Prohibition of Mine Action in Geneva, Switzerland on the 26th. November 2018.
At the meeting, the Senior Minister briefed the member countries of the Ottawa Convention on Mine Action and the commitment of the Royal Government of Cambodia under the wise leadership and long-term vision of Samdech Techo PM on demining and Explosive remnants of war by 2025.
At the same time, the Senior Minister also held bilateral meetings with donor countries and development partners such as: Australia, Canada, etc. To mobilize more resources to contribute to the Royal Government of Cambodia in clearing mines and explosive remnants in Cambodia.
In addition, the Senior Minister, on behalf of the Prime Minister, would like to express his deep gratitude to all donor countries and development partners for providing humanitarian demining assistance and support for the Cambodian Mine Action Plan by 2025. Royal Government of Cambodia.
