According to the auction house, the "wood and stone" painting will be one of the most important works in the history of the auction.
The exhibition features about 60 works of art, a mix of traditional and contemporary, as well as a variety of ceramics and handicrafts. Organizers say Chinese bidders have become more interested in contemporary art in recent years.
All the artwork as well as some jewelry will be auctioned from November 23 to 25 in Hong Kong. (China's CCTV)
The statement of the Minister of Defense of Cambodia was made this morning, November 26, 2018, on the occasion that Samdech led the team to continue to inspect the construction process of the Victory Monument in Sangkat Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh.
Samdech Picheay Sena stated that the construction of the Victory Monument will be a place to store intellectual property and historical knowledge to be kept in this monument for the Cambodian people, youth and scholars to know. Heard, looked at win-win politics as well.
Please be informed that the construction of this win-win monument started in February 2016 on an area of 8 hectares in Chroy Changva district, Phnom Penh. The construction of this win-win monument is a symbol of the peace that Cambodia has achieved after the end of decades of civil war.
In addition, this monument will be a legacy for future generations. This was further confirmed by General Nem Sovath, Chairman of the Win-Win Monument Construction Team, who worked hard to lead the team to build this historic monument under the guidance and guidance of Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh.
The Stung Sreng Dam is 2,800 meters long and connects Phnom Kambor to Phnom Rong Dek with a storage capacity of 259 million cubic meters. This dam is located in Srah Keo village, Pong Ror commune, Chong Kal district, Oddar Meanchey province. Stung Sreng Dam, which plays a role in reducing flooding and can supply water to supply more than 25,000 hectares of farmland in three provinces, including Oddar Meanchey, Banteay Meanchey and Siem Reap. The dam was completed in March 2017.
At the beginning of the construction process of this dam, there were also various movements to prevent this construction under the pretext of affecting the community forest land. However, seeing the necessary benefits of extracting water for irrigation and consumption of the people, the Royal Government did not overcome the construction of this dam.
Currently, this dam is playing an important role in providing water sources for the people. Mr. Seng Song, a resident of Anlong Veng district since the 1980s, expressed his enthusiasm and happiness for this achievement.
He pointed out that since he lived here, there has never been such a big dam, and people often face the problem of lack of water for use and irrigation. But after the Royal Government built this dam, the people no longer face all those problems and have helped to improve their lives.
Siem Reap CamControl Officers Inspected Goods at Samdech Techo Doeum Kralanh Market, Found Squid Containing Prohibited Chemicals and Confiscated
(Siem Reap): Officials of Camkotrol Siem Reap Branch and Siem Reap International Airport this morning, November 26, 2018, in cooperation with the officials of the Department of Commerce, the Market Commission inspected the goods displayed in Samdech Techo Doeum Kralanh Market. Located in Trapeang Ses Village, Kork Chak Commune, Siem Reap District, Siem Reap Province.
At the same time, officials have advised traders to be aware of food safety, especially not to produce or sell substandard goods or contain banned chemicals for sale, as it may affect the health of consumers. "People's Struggle: Cambodia Revived" Title of the book on the struggle for the national cause and people of Samdech Heng Samrin
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Heng Samrin's book on the struggle for the national cause and the people, entitled "People's struggle: Cambodia revived" was released this morning, November 26, 2018. A book describing the mission in the cause of the nation and the people that Samdech spent most of his life, Samdech is recorded in this book in English.
The inauguration and dissemination of this historic book was attended by more than 100 members of the National Assembly, the Senate, government officials, officials of the General Secretariat of the National Assembly and the Senate, as well as students and librarians of public and private educational institutions.
"People's Struggle: Reviving Cambodia" will reveal the reality of the Cambodian war to readers and the next generation of Cambodians who want to learn about Cambodian history. The history of the national liberation struggle of patriotic elites and the restoration of Cambodia after the genocidal regime of Pol Pot 40 years ago.
Born into a peasant family in a rural area in Kampong Cham province in 1934, Samdech Heng Samrin was the founding president of a large mass movement called the "Kampuchean United Front for National Salvation", which was later renamed the "United Front for the Development of Motherland Cambodia". Established at a congress in Kratie province on December 2, 1978. Starting from Kratie province, Samdech Heng Samrin announced 11 plans to overthrow the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
After January 7, 1979, Samdech Heng Samrin became the Head of State of the People's Republic of Cambodia and Secretary General of the Cambodian People's Revolutionary Party. Samdech Heng Samrin is currently the National Assembly President and Honorary President of the Cambodian People's Party, as well as the rotating chair of the Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Forum (APPF), while the Cambodian Parliament will host the 27th Annual Meeting of the Parliamentary Forum at In January 2019.
Samdech Heng Samrin is one of the 14 surviving leaders of the Cambodian National Salvation United Front, such as Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian People's Party. The Cambodian People's Party and Senator Mr. Ros Samay, Senior Advisor to the Royal Government and Mr. Chan Ven, former Secretary General of the National Assembly.
The United Front for National Salvation of Cambodia will celebrate the 40th anniversary of the founding of the Front at the Memorial in Snuol District, Kratie Province on December 2, 2018. Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin will preside over the event, which will be attended by tens of thousands of people.
* Selected lectures in the book
So Phim's death: The death of So Phim, Commander of the Eastern Zone of the Cambodian People's Revolutionary Army, is something that the national and international community wants to know. The book "People's Struggle: Reviving Cambodia" will detail So Phim's death.
At one point, Samdech Heng Samrin told the author, recalling the last meeting with a sick former commander at a pagoda in Prey Salit commune, Pearang district, Prey Veng province, in 1978, shortly after the bodyguards Some of So Phim was killed by Pol Pot forces near Phnom Penh.
"He was in a state of despair," Samdech explained, explaining why So Phim had agreed to leave Pol Pot's forces for Srey Santhor district, Kampong Cham province. "In Srey Santhor district, there are 300 soldiers standing ready to intervene in any situation that may occur."
Samdech Heng Samrin continued, "The enemy soldiers took So Phim's body as evidence and accused him of being a real traitor and he was dead." Chhean, the party secretary of Area 22, and Sarun, the director of Eastern Logistics, were also killed.
* Clash with Ta Mok forces
"People's Struggle: Reviving Cambodia" also recalls the first clashes with the Ta Mok-led southwest forces as revolutionary forces were fighting to overthrow the Lon Nol regime.
Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin called the first clash with Ta Mok involved the disappearance of 10 troops from the eastern part of the Chiso Mountains, including a platoon commander.
Later, there were clashes again in the border areas of Saang and Prey Kabas districts around Prek Ambel. That was a large-scale clash between the infantry forces of the two regions until a confrontation with a mortar.
* Withdrawal from Phnom Penh
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin said that his forces in the eastern region had been in control of Phnom Penh for a month before being replaced by the Central Forces in order to leave. "Central forces are strict and decisive." Whenever an order is issued, the work must be decided without fail. Samdech recalled.
* Publishing and Advertising
