(Phnom Penh): Mr. Song Saran, President of the Cambodian Pepper and Spice Federation, which was just born in early November, described that the establishment of the Pepper Federation not only benefits farmers but also helps establish a pepper market. Well.
Mr. Song Saran said that according to the data of the Ministry of Agriculture of Cambodia, nearly 20,000 tons of pepper was produced separately, based on data in Vietnam, it is confirmed that Vietnam orders 25,000 tons of pepper from Cambodia per year, this amount. There is also uncertainty that requires the federation to collect specific data.
"After the Federation of Pepper and Spices, Cambodia will no longer be completely dependent on the Vietnamese market, as there are many market options, such as the European Union, Dubai, the United Arab Emirates and the United States," he said. "These markets play a very important role in the global pepper consumption movement, accounting for more than 80 percent of the total pepper market."
He added that another emerging market is the Chinese market and a growing new market of pepper.
"I believe that China will turn its attention to the Cambodian pepper market and order pepper from Cambodia," he said. "In order to import pepper into China, Cambodia needs to have a strategy that the federation will discuss with its members."
He said that Cambodia's pepper has great potential, which is considered a pepper with high quality and high safety for consumers.
