Kampong Cham Provincial Commissioner Tells Police Administration Post to Disseminate and Educate Citizens More on Safe Village and Commune Policy
(Kampong Cham): Major General Em Kosal, Provincial Police Commissioner of Kampong Cham Province, held a meeting on November 26, 2018.
Summarize the situation, results of social security operations and implement the work of the police and community in November and the direction of the December tasks to prepare for security, social order, safety for the people.
The meeting was also attended by 14 Deputy Commissioners for Planning, 7 Deputy Chiefs of Planning, 32 Chiefs of Offices, 97 Deputy Chiefs of Offices, 10 District Police Inspectors, and Deputy Inspectors. 54 people and 109 administrative police chiefs.
Lt. Gen. Em Kosal ordered the administrative police officers to educate the people about the law and the safe village-commune policy of the Royal Government.
According to the General Commissioner, the people must be mobilized to participate in the protection of the people in each village to increase and solve the remaining crimes to maintain security, safety and public order in accordance with their respective skills. 27-year-old HelloTrust liberates 287 square kilometers of land and clears nearly half a million mines
(Phnom Penh): From 1991 to 2018, the humanitarian demining organization HelloTrust cleared 287 square kilometers of land safe and destroyed nearly half a million mines and unexploded ordnance, while on average Every month, the organization clears 760 mines and munitions, benefiting nearly one million Cambodians.
HelloTrust currently has a total of nearly 1,200 staff in the demining operations in Pursat, Battambang, Pailin, Banteay Meanchey, Oddar Meanchey, Preah Vihear, Siem Reap and Koh Kong, about 50 percent of whom are women.
In fact, in order to increase the efficiency of this humanitarian work, in early November 2018, the humanitarian demining organization HelloTrust opened a training course for 124 new demining staff, and the expansion of the additional staff due to the increase in support from Donor countries to support the National Strategic Plan for Mine Action, which aims to target Cambodia without mines by 2025.
Damian O'Brien, Program Director for HelloTrust Cambodia, stated that it is important and encouraging that donor countries, including the United Kingdom, Germany, the United States and Ireland, continue to recognize the value of Demining in Cambodia, and support from these countries, has enabled organizations to deploy more demining forces in mine-affected areas.
Ms. Eng Kunthea, a new employee who is receiving training, said that she joined HelloTrust because she wanted to have a job in Cambodia and she could contribute to the country through demining, and HelloTrust is a humanitarian organization. Clear mines to save lives.
She claims she also trained as a paramedic and learned how to rescue victims when they were in a minefield accident.
