(Takeo): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, through Chip Mong Company, provided a concrete road to the people of Traing and Borey Chulsar districts in Takeo province. This road starts from National Road 2 at Trapeang Leuk village, 8 Mom commune, Traing district to Kampong Touk and Kampong Ampil villages, Borey Chulsar commune, Borey Chulsar district at a cost of 6 million US dollars.
The groundbreaking ceremony was held this morning, November 26, 2018, with the participation of Deputy Prime Minister Binh Chin, Minister in Charge of the Office of the Council of Ministers, Mr. Oknha Leang Khun, General Director of Chip Mong and Mr. Ouch Phea, Provincial Governor. Takeo.
Mr. Oknha Leang Khun stated that he was very pleased to be honored to bring the high and precious bonds of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to all the people of Takeo Province through Preparation for the construction of an 18-kilometer stretch of road.
He said that Chip Mong Company will arrange for the construction of an 18-kilometer-long concrete road with a width of 8 meters and a one-and-a-half-meter-long red dirt road from National Road No. 2 at Trapeang Leuk commune. 8 corner of Traing district to Kampong Touk, Kampong Ampil, Borey Chulsar commune, Borey Chulsar district. The construction of this concrete road will cost 6 million US dollars.
Deputy Prime Minister Binh Chin expressed his deep gratitude to Mr. Leang Khun, General Director of Chip Mong Company and on behalf of all the philanthropists who helped build this concrete road, boats for people to use in Traing and Srok districts. Borey Chulsar, where these activities have made a significant contribution to the Royal Government's policy on poverty reduction.
