Foreign direct investment in mainland China continued to grow steadily in the first 10 months of this year, while foreign direct investment outside of China's financial sector continued to grow steadily. Also. This is according to a new announcement from the Chinese Ministry of Commerce.
China's foreign direct investment rose 3.3 percent to 1.77 billion US dollars from January to October this year. This growth is due to strong investment in manufacturing and modern technology.
Compared to the previous year, the number of new companies with foreign investment increased sharply by 89.3 percent to 495,545 companies.
The manufacturing sector received about 31.16 billion US dollars in foreign investment, up 12.4 percent from the same period last year. The high-tech sector grew by 11.4 percent, accounting for 22.4 percent of total foreign direct investment.
Investment from the United Kingdom rose 175.9 percent, the largest source of investment for China. Investment from countries along the One Belt One Road infrastructure project grew 11.9 percent.
The ministry's report also showed that China's foreign direct investment in non-financial sectors rose 3.8 percent to 89.57 billion US dollars in the first quarter. In the first 10 months of 2018. Domestic investment was invested in 4,905 foreign companies in 155 countries and regions from January to October this year.
New investment in countries participating in the One Belt One Road project rose 6.4 percent to about $ 12 billion in the first 10 months of this year.
Meanwhile, Chinese companies have also signed additional contracts to cover large projects outside China in the first 10 months of this year. And the money invested in those projects amounted to more than 89 billion US dollars.
From January to October this year, most of China's overseas investment was in services, manufacturing, mining and retail business.
(Phnom Penh): In 2019, the minimum wage of workers will be increased in accordance with the minimum wage law, and in order to implement this work effectively, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training in collaboration with the International Labor Organization (ILO) organized a workshop. A high on minimum wage monitoring.
He said that the systematic economic enterprises registered with the Ministry of Labor and Training has a total of more than 12,000 and a total of nearly 1.5 million workers, and a total of nearly 600,000 informal economic enterprises. More than 2.4 million workers, more than 4 million in the agricultural sector, about 1.2 million overseas workers and more than 500,000 public officials.
Meanwhile, the minimum wage for the textile, garment and footwear sector will continue to increase from $ 40 per month in 1997 to $ 182 per month in 2019, plus additional benefits. In addition, a worker can earn an average of 199-210 US dollars per month, which helps to improve the living standards of workers.
