Following technology trends, especially with the launch of Apple's new iPhone, Metfone has worked hard to become the first mobile phone company in Cambodia to introduce eSIM technology. This is according to the information provided by the representative of Metfone.
The eSIM, also known as the Electronic SIM, is a good replacement for the conventional SIM card that has been used for decades and is also considered the next step in the development of the telecommunications sector.
eSIM has many benefits, such as it is not as fragile and fragile as a regular SIM card, and users can change the network at will without having to change the SIM card.
Currently, this technology can be used by only a few operators in 10 countries around the world, and most are developed countries. If Metfone succeeds in launching this technology, it is a great achievement of Cambodia's ICT sector.
(Dubai): The Minister of Commerce, Mr. Pan Sosak, announced to the leaders and senior officials of the United Arab Emirates Government, country leaders and representatives of international organizations that Cambodia is ready to participate in the World Expo to be held in the city. Dubai for 6 months from October 20, 2020 to April 10, 2021.
The Minister's announcement was made on the occasion of attending the 3rd IPM Welcome Dinner on Sunday night, November 25, 2018 in Dubai, United Arab Emirates for the purpose of meeting, discussing and monitoring progress. Work to organize the Dubai World Expo 2020.
On that occasion, Minister Pan Sosak highlighted Cambodia's active participation in the World and International Expo in the past, as well as the progress of the General Department of Trade Promotion, which is the staff of the Ministry of Commerce. Responsible for Cambodia's participation in various exhibition events.
"Cambodia is now ready to participate in the Dubai World Expo 2020, and we will surely be as successful as participating in the World Expo in Shanghai in 2010 and in Italy in 2015." The minister added.
At the same time, the Minister also met and exchanged views with leaders of countries and representatives of international organizations present in the program to strengthen economic cooperation and bilateral and multilateral trade relations, especially to ensure market share for Cambodian goods in the global trading system.
