National Assembly Launches New Book "Revival of the Cambodian People" by Samdech Heng Samrin
(Phnom Penh): On November 26, 2018, the National Assembly of Cambodia inaugurated and disseminated a diary on the struggle of Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly in the process of liberating the country from the Pol Pot regime, including participating in the restoration. And re-develop the nation after the fire of war.
The mission in the cause of the nation and the people that Samdech has spent most of his life is recorded in the book "The Struggle of the Cambodian People Revived" in English, which was inaugurated and disseminated at the National Assembly today.
The inauguration and dissemination of this historic book was attended by more than 100 members of the National Assembly, the Senate, government officials, officials of the General Secretariat of the National Assembly and the Senate, as well as students and librarians of public and private educational institutions.
The book "The Struggle of the Cambodian Resurrection" shows the reality of the war in Cambodia to the readers and the next generation of Cambodians who want to learn about Cambodian history. A history of patriotic elites' struggle for national liberation and the restoration of Cambodia after the fall of the Pol Pot genocidal regime 40 years ago.
Born into a peasant family in a rural area in Kampong Cham province in 1934, Samdech Heng Samrin was the founding president of a large mass movement called the "Kampuchean United Front for National Salvation", which was later renamed the "United Front for the Development of Motherland Cambodia". Established at a congress in Kratie province on December 2, 1978. Starting from Kratie province, Samdech Heng Samrin announced 11 plans to overthrow the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
Samdech Heng Samrin is one of the 14 surviving leaders of the Cambodian National Salvation Front movement, including Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian People's Party. Standing Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Senator Mr. Ros Samay, Senior Advisor to the Royal Government and Mr. Chan Ven, former Secretary General of the National Assembly.
The United Front for National Salvation of Cambodia will celebrate the 40th anniversary of the founding of the Front at the Memorial in Snuol District, Kratie Province on December 2, 2018. Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin will preside over the event, which was attended by tens of thousands of people.
