(Phnom Penh): On the morning of November 28, 2018, the Senate will hold a meeting of the Standing Committee of the Senate to review five important agendas. The meeting will be held at the Senate Palace under the chairmanship of Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate of Cambodia.
The agenda that the Standing Committee of the Senate will discuss and approve includes the following:
First, review and decide on the request of the Second Committee of the Senate to submit the draft law on finance for management in 2019 in the agenda of the second session of the Senate for the fourth term.
Second, to review and decide on the request of the Second Committee of the Senate to submit the draft law on the payment of the general state budget for the 2017 administration in the agenda of the second session of the Senate for the fourth term.
Fourth, to review and decide on the request of the Sixth Committee of the Senate to submit the draft law on the ratification of the extradition treaty between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Russian Federation in the agenda of the second session of the Senate for the fourth term.
Fifth: Determining the agenda and date of the resumption of the second session of the Senate of the fourth legislature.
