Minister of Tourism: Big work to organize the sea festival in Koh Kong province is ready
(Koh Kong): With only 19 days left, the 7th Sea Festival (Round 2) in Koh Kong Province is approaching, and the big work in organizing this tourism event is ready. This is according to Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, on the occasion that he, together with Ms. Mithona Phuthong, Governor of Koh Kong Province, chaired a meeting to prepare for the Sea Festival at Koh Kong Provincial Hall on November 25, 2018.
The meeting mentioned some of the work that has been prepared for the upcoming Sea Festival, including:
* National Road No. 48 from Sre Ambel roundabout to Koh Kong province is being repaired by the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and the Engineering Corps.
* For travel to and from Koh Kong-Trat province, the Minister requested the Cambodian side to contact the Thai side to allow people to drive from Cambodia to Trat or from Trat to Koh Kong easily. More than a normal day and should request to open 24 hours during the three-day festival as in the previous Sea Festival.
* Koh Kong Provincial Decoration Sub-Committee and Administration must accelerate the improvement of some public places in Khemarak Phoumin City and at all the designated destinations. Others are also ready.
* For the preparation of tourism, trade and food exhibition booths are also ready, which currently has more than 400 booths. The art parade is also ready. So far, art groups from friendly countries have confirmed their participation: Thailand, Vietnam, India, Indonesia. National and international sports programs and sports activities are also ready.
* Mangrove planting ceremony and beautiful beach workshop on the morning of December 13 (which also includes the CEO of the most beautiful beach club in the world) and a certificate of appreciation. For business owners who have excelled in tourism in the coastal provinces of Cambodia (Koh Kong, Sihanoukville, Kampot and Kep) is ready.
* The Sub-Committee on Security, Order, Sanitation and Health has also prepared a plan. The provincial administration has set up adequate public mobile toilets.
Separately, for the golf tournament at Koh Sdach, a big event to celebrate the Sea Festival is also ready. The Minister reminded to educate and control all traders in Koh Kong Province, please do not increase the service fee excessively. The Minister also asked people to come and enjoy the Sea Festival.
Tomorrow morning, the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia opens its 4th General Assembly on the 40th anniversary of its birth.
(Phnom Penh): The Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia (UYFC), chaired by Hun Many, will hold its 4th National Congress tomorrow, November 26, 2018. Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh. Tomorrow's opening of the General Assembly will be presided over by Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate and Vice President of the Cambodian People's Party.
The 4th General Assembly of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia was also held on the 40th anniversary of its birth. The General Assembly will be attended by approximately 1,300 leaders, members and members from 25 capitals and provinces.
According to the announcement of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, the General Assembly will be held for two days, from 26 to 27 November 2018. The statement affirmed that the General Assembly will be held with a focus on summarizing the work of 2012-2018 and the work direction for 2018-2020, as well as the election of members with the discussion and approval of Amendments to the statute of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia.
It should be noted that the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia is a comprehensive front of the Cambodian Youth, which continued the mission of the Cambodian National Rescue Youth Association and the Cambodian Youth Association, which was established on December 2, 1978 with the most important goal to gather young people everywhere. Solidarity in contributing to the building of Cambodia with independence, peace, freedom, democracy and social progress.
