Two Vietnamese murderers who beat and tortured sex workers to death have been remanded in custody.
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of November 23, 2018, the Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, Mr. Long Vanna, issued an order to detain two male and female murderers at Prey Sar Prison, awaiting trial later in accordance with the case law. They tortured a sex worker to death and took her body to the Wat Teuk Thla crematorium.
The judge's decision came after prosecutors Ngin Pich completed an investigation into the perpetrators: Nguyen Yang Zhou and Nguyen Thi Yong alias Chen Sineth on charges of "intentional aggravated violence." Punishment due to the death of the victim ”which is punishable under Article 222 of the Penal Code.
It should be reminded that on the afternoon of November 20, 2018, Colonel Hour Meng Wang, Police Inspector of Sen Sok District, presented the suspects as two male and female murderers who tortured a sex worker to death. This also took the body of the victim to be dumped at the crematorium of Wat Teuk Thla on the night of November 15, 2018.
For that reason, the inspector said that it was caused by forcing the victim to have sex too much, but the victim refused and beat him to death.
Mr. Hour Meng Wang continued that last night, November 15, 2018, an unknown person took a 20-year-old Vietnamese woman in a tuk-tuk to the crematorium at Wat Teuk Thla crematorium. Tell Grandpa Acha to call the victim's relatives. The suspects later escaped.
On the afternoon of November 15, 2018, without seeing any relatives, the Acha reported to the competent authorities to come down to the morgue. Immediately after receiving this information, the district police went to check and contact the forensic experts of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police.
After the forensic experts arrived, they found that the body of the victim was beaten and tortured, causing bruises all over her body until she died.
Later, the police force of Sen Sok District Police Inspectorate cooperated with Phnom Penh Serious Criminal Police Force and Tuol Kork District Police Inspectorate to search for the suspect who was the brutal killer. Until the night of November 18, 2018, the police force of Sen Sok district arrested two male and female suspects for interrogation at the Sen Sok district inspector on suspicion of being involved in the torture of a sex worker to death.
After questioning the two suspects, on the morning of November 19, 2018, the Sen Sok District Police Force cooperated with the Tuol Kork District Police Force to search the location of a brothel under the brand name Massage. Street 598 in Sangkat Toek Laak 2, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh, where the woman was tortured. Meanwhile, the mastermind who is the mastermind of this house escaped.
