After visiting Cambodia, Mr. Tong Dai Chi noted that Cambodia has great potential and rapid development, especially in tourism and urban infrastructure. Secretary of State Hor Moniroth thanked the Chinese government and people for their full support of Cambodia's development.
It should be recalled that Cambodia has signed a Memorandum of Understanding on Urban-Urban Tourism Development, focusing on training human resources, connecting air and waterways, exchanging cultural visits between the two countries. Share experiences about tourism city development, community development, tourism and entrepreneurship.
Pursuant to this Memorandum of Understanding and with the financial support of the Government of China, Cambodia organized a workshop on the training of Mekong-Langchang trainers on ASEAN Tourism Community Standards in Siem Reap on 8-12 May 2018.
On behalf of the Ministry of Tourism, Mr. Hor Moniroth requested the forum to consider the establishment of the Mekong-Lang Chang Tourism Ministerial Meeting in conjunction with the next Sanya Forum on Tourism City Cooperation.
