Watch the video of the full interview: The King is the King during the Royal Salute Ceremony, Ok Ambok and Rain Smoke
(Phnom Penh): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, was born on Thursday, November 22, 2018. Royal ceremony to salute the moon and smoke the rain.
According to Facebook, "His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, the Mayor of Cambodia," who often posts his activities, said that his visit to the royal ceremony in the month of Ok Ambok and Raindrops are also accompanied by the royal family, nobles, officials of all ranks in the Royal Palace.
The King of Cambodia, as well as the royal family, nobles, officials of all ranks in the Royal Palace, pray to the sacred objects in the world, all the gods, the ten thousand deities, the demigods, the guardian deities, the umbrellas, the merciful ones, bless the gods. The Kingdom of Cambodia wishes peace, prosperity and prosperity to the people throughout the Kingdom.
Please be informed that according to the tradition of the Khmer nation, every year on the full moon night of the 15th day of the month of Khek Kdek, the Khmer people, men and women, always celebrate the worship of the moon and Ok Ambok in pagodas all over the country, and in the year of Samreth Sak, Buddhist year 2562 In the year 2018, the festival of worshiping the moon god and Ok Ambok is held on the night of November 22 (12 o'clock every year).
According to the traditions of the Khmer ancestors, this ceremony is held to ask for happiness and prosperity from the sacred objects in the world, please help nurture the people of Cambodia to experience peace and to contribute to the preservation of national traditions. In Kong Vong forever.
A brief history of the Moon Worship Ceremony and Ok Ambok goes on to say that according to the Pali canon, the Ashtaka Chariyapidak in Pali states that in the beginning of this kind, our bodhisattva was born as a sage (tattoo). On the full moon day, the sage prayed the Uposatha Sila and dedicated the sammasak as a bodhisattva gift to fulfill the bodhisattva material to attain enlightenment as a Buddha.
Indra knew this, so he became an old Brahmin and asked for food. The Bodhisattva asked the old Brahmin to light a fire while the fire was burning. The doctor shook his body three times to get the insects stuck to his hair out and jumped into the fire immediately.
Amazingly, the fire did not burn at all. Indra Brahmin rushed to bless the bodhisattva up to the center of the moon. Finally. By the power of the bodhisattva's bodhichitta and Indra's prayers, the image of the rabbit is still visible in the moon to this day.
