A large Chinese company that has been operating for more than 60 years has ambitions to invest in rice and cotton production in Cambodia
Noting that Cambodia has rich natural resources and high potential for agriculture, his company has been cooperating with a number of major institutes in China with high skills and technology to study, research and produce rice and seeds. Cotton with high yield quality suitable for soil and weather conditions to try to grow in Cambodia for export in the future.
The director of the company informed that his rice factory is built on an area of more than 10 hectares and is located near the river. At the same time, in order to contribute to the transportation of wet rice by the farming community after the harvest to the dry warehouse on time and cheaply, the Chinese government has helped dig an artificial canal from the river to connect to the factory.
In addition, with an annual government subsidy of approximately US $ 1.5 million to help ensure the value of agricultural products and expand production facilities, the rice mill is capable of grinding about 1,600 tons of rice per day. It has 390,000 tons of rice and can supply more than 200,000 tons of domestic market per year. At present, the company is able to contract with the farming community annually on about 20,000 hectares of rice fields.
