These inspections are aimed at examining the hygiene of product labels, expiration dates, and the use of banned chemicals used in such food products. As a result of the examination of the 24 samples, 6 samples were found to be dried trout containing the banned chemical porcine and the team recorded 2.60 kg to be destroyed.
At the same time, CamControl officers also distributed posters and advised traders, vendors and residents to check the hygiene, appropriateness of the display by separating the products containing toxic substances and food. And do not sell products, beverages that are exposed to the sun and beyond the expiration date or goods that contain banned chemicals that can harm the health of consumers.
