(Phnom Penh): The Director General of Health Technology of the Ministry of Health, Dr. O Vandin, stated that if a drug addict comes to see a doctor 20 times and follow the medical education without interruption in a year. Then he will be able to get addicted.
The statement was made during a visit to an educational tent on the effects and dangers of drugs under the theme "Together for Community-Based Drug Treatment" in collaboration with the National Authority. Fighting drugs organized for 3 days during the Royal Water Festival at Wat Phnom.
Dr. O Vandin said that every year, on the occasion of the Royal Water Festival, the Moon Festival and the Ok Ambok, the Royal Government of Cambodia always organizes educational campaigns on the effects and dangers of drugs to mainstream. Understand people about the effects and dangers of drug use.
The doctor said that the treatment of drug addicts is complicated, which requires multi-sectoral participation, and for this reason, the National Anti-Drug Authority, the Ministry of Health, law enforcement agencies and non-governmental organizations have made joint efforts. Collaborate and work closely to demonstrate the indispensable partnership and collaboration required in community-based drug treatment.
"We also want to send a message to the public to understand that families and communities also play an important role, and that the commitment and support of families and communities is key to keeping patients healthy," she said. Stay in treatment, ensuring effective treatment and preventing relapse.
The Director General of Health Technology also stated, "For drug addicts who want to get rid of it, they have to come to see a doctor 20 times a year and follow it regularly to be able to get rid of the addiction. "This treatment is free of charge at the expense of the state as stated in Article 100 on Drugs."
