The White House this week reaffirmed its stance on restricting the influx of asylum seekers from Central and Latin America by Donald Trump's new order earlier this month requiring All refugees enter the United States legally. This is according to the release by Sputnik on Wednesday morning, November 21, 2018.
On this issue, White House spokeswoman Sarah Sanders confirmed on Tuesday that "we are taking all possible steps to defend our legal position in response to the crisis on the southern border ... " The statement came after a U.S. court issued a ruling temporarily barring President Donald Trump's new order regarding asylum seekers in the United States.
On November 9, 2018, Donald Trump issued a decree stating that the United States would not grant legal asylum to refugees who did not enter US territory through proper or legal border crossings. By law, only those who come in the right way have legal asylum, but a US court has decided to suspend the order.
The new law was officially announced on November 10, which will remain in force for three months or until an agreement is reached that allows the United States to deport refugees. Laws are issued at the border with Mexico. Although the court issued a decision rejecting the order, the decision will be implemented from December 19 only.
The King issues a Royal Decree ordering the appointment and promotion of a total of 14 members of the Board of Directors and advisors to the Board of Directors of CMAC.
(Phnom Penh): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, has issued a Royal Decree appointing and appointing a total of 14 members of the National Mine Action Center (CMAC). With ranks from Under Secretary of State to Senior Minister.
