KABUL: At least 40 people have been killed in a suicide bomb attack near a wedding hall in Kabul, Afghan authorities said on Tuesday. This is according to the press release of Russian Today on Tuesday, November 20, 2018.
Another 60 people were injured, according to Afghan authorities. But no group has immediately claimed responsibility for the attack, as ISIS and Taliban militants often carry out such attacks in Afghanistan. In Kang Meas District, Kampong Cham Province
(Kampong Cham): Kampong Cham provincial police on November 20, 2018, continued to crack down on illegal fishing in Reay Pai commune, Kang Meas district, confiscating some crime evidences and releasing mixed fish into natural lakes.
According to the report of the Kampong Cham Provincial Police Commissioner, Major General Em Kosal, the operation was ordered by the Kang Meas District Police Inspector in cooperation with the Scattered Administrative Police Force, Commune Council and Boeung B6 Community, led by Mr. Hor Hin, Commune Council. Pointing out that Mr. Moeun Pha, the district governor, cracked down on illegal fishing at Prek point in Reay Pai village, Reay Pai commune, Kang Meas district, Kampong Cham province.
As a result of the crackdown, police confiscated 16 nets, 550-meter-long nets, 150 mixed poles and released 35 kilograms of mixed fish into natural lakes.
The exhibits were burned on the spot with the approval of the Prosecutor of Kampong Cham Provincial Court.
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - A U.S. federal judge on Tuesday ruled against President Donald Trump's ruling, which seeks to deny asylum to illegal immigrants crossing the southern US border. This was released by the BBC on Tuesday, November 20, 2018.
San Francisco U.S. District Judge Jon Tigar overturned Donald Trump's ruling after hearing claims from civil society groups. Donald Trump issued an order in early November aimed at curbing the influx of refugees from Central American countries trying to enter the United States.
