General Department of Taxation issues clarification on the case of a Facebook owner who accuses tax of suspending his company's business because tax officials are selfish
(Phnom Penh): The General Department of Taxation on the night of November 20 issued a letter clarifying the case of a Facebook owner who accused the tax to suspend his business because the tax officials are selfish but taxed Reject and claim that this statement is not based on the law and will damage the honor of tax officials and state institutions.
Read the full tax letter: The second provincial “E” boat race in Stung Treng province was successfully completed with over 40,000 spectators
(Stung Treng): On the afternoon of Tuesday, November 13, 2018, the second provincial “E” boat race in Stung Treng province to celebrate the Royal Water Festival Floating boats, lanterns and moon worship were successfully completed with more than 40,000 spectators.
The Closing Ceremony of "E" Boat Race was Presided over by Mr. Mom Saroeun, Governor of Stung Treng Province, Mr. Chhim Rachana, Chairman of Provincial Council, Provincial Leaders, Government Officials, Departments around the province, national and international guests, students and many people. Crowds.
In the three-day "E" boat race, there were 15 boats from cities, districts and departments around the province, with 409 riders and 101 reserve riders.
On the occasion of the closing ceremony, the provincial governor and provincial leaders presented prizes to the first-place boat with a budget of 1,000,000 Riels and a flag of honor, the second-place boat received a budget of 700,000 Riel and 1 honor flag, the 3rd place boat received 550,000 Riels and 1 honor flag, while the boat that was not ranked received 400,000 Riels and 1 honor flag.
It should be noted that the provincial “E” boat race in Stung Treng province has already been organized once in 2017 under the initiative of HE Mom Saroeun, Governor of Stung Treng Province and is considered as an event by the people in Stung Treng Province. History for the province, because in the past there was no such big "E" boat race event at the provincial level.
Sihanoukville Flower Boat Race Successfully Completed with Tens of Thousands of Visitors
(Preah Sihanouk): After suspending the boat race a few years ago, in 2018, Mr. Yon Min, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, decided to re-establish this flower boat race with 21 pairs of local boats happily participating. To celebrate the Royal Water Festival, float the lanterns and worship the moon with the support of many people.
The provincial governor said that the boat players who participated in the race must try their best to win from their partners. He said that this year, the province organized this ceremony to commemorate the heroes of the Navy who worked hard to protect the territory and national sovereignty and to celebrate the Royal Water Festival, floating lanterns and worshiping the moon, which is Our national tradition of Khmer.
At the same time, Mr. Yon Min reminded people to implement the policy of safe villages, communes, do not use drugs, do not gamble, big and small, and must obey traffic laws while driving.
According to the Organizing Committee of the Flower Boat Race, Mr. Det No, Director of the Sihanoukville Provincial Department of Culture, said that this year, 21 flower boats participated in the competition, including one women's boat and six pairs of snow boats. The two-day race is from November 19 to 20, 2018. In addition to night boat races, there will also be lanterns, floating lanterns, fireworks and live music.
On November 20, 2018, Samdech Techo Hun Sen shared one of the many experiences that Samdech used in his political life and leadership. The strategic experience that Samdech shared today is to "push the boat along the water". This word is Khmer, we diligently speak, and Samdech Techo Hun Sen also diligently mentions.
The Prime Minister added that these two factors are very important, as the first factor is time. Time is an opportunity, smart people know how to see opportunities, know how to use opportunities and create opportunities. If you push the boat along the water when the water level rises or the rainstorm, the boat will sink.
The second factor is not to push the boat down the stream without a goal. Some grandchildren and great-grandchildren have decided to pursue higher education or some professional career by pushing a boat along the water but not at the helm because they themselves do not know the destination. At this point, you need to plan your life by building a dream for your future that is full of realism.
Samdech stated that in his political life, Samdech has marked every step, every scenario. No one can guess the route, not even the people who have been walking with them since the war.
With this sharing, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also sent a message to the youth not to fall asleep, twist and turn, and replied that he took a lesson from the story of pushing a boat along the water that Samdech shared. Samdech Techo mentioned that there are two points to keep in mind:
Samdech Techo also reminded to have a strong will in the nation. The head of the Royal Government emphasized that in relation to the sovereignty, territorial integrity of Cambodia and the peace of the Cambodian people, not to mention pushing the boat along the water, even dragging the tank up the mountain must be done.
