(Phnom Penh): The nationwide campaign against illegal drugs for November 20, 2018 shows that law enforcement forces have cracked down on:
(Phnom Penh): The distributor of counterfeit and expired drugs "Cambodia Corporation Pharma" which the authorities cracked down on last week with the confiscation of up to 40 tons of drugs has been operating for more than 7 years. Despite the crackdown, the authorities have not yet arrested the company's boss, only one boss.
Speaking at a press conference on the afternoon of November 20, 2018, the General said, "The distributor for seven years is Cambodia Corporation Pharma. The company is registered, but only the company has not registered Some drugs are registered and the company has modified the status of the drug, and if the authorities do not have the skills to study thoroughly. They say theirs is legal. ”
The chairman of the Anti-Counterfeit Products Committee added that when the competent experts took all the drugs to check or enter the laboratory correctly, they found that the illegal drugs were behind the licensed drugs, that is, the owner of the location acted. So to cheat the authorities.
However, in connection with the operation to crack down on counterfeit and expired drugs, the police, in cooperation with the Ministry of Health, also arrested a general manager of the company located in Sangkat Teuk Thla, Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh, while the owner of the company is still investigating. .
Please be informed that on November 13, 2018, the Special Operations Team of the Anti-Counterfeit Products Committee cracked down on the crime of importing and storing illegal and substandard medicines at the above locations by temporarily confiscating 138 kinds of mixed medicinal products. Equivalent to 10,465 boxes, about 40 tons.
According to the inspection of the technical and pharmaceutical team, the preliminary conclusion was that: the delivery was not technically correct, 24 kinds of medicines (equivalent to 2,043 boxes), no registration certificate, 36 kinds of medicines (equivalent to 10,465 boxes) expired 138 items (equivalent to 2,298 boxes) without written instructions in Khmer. A city in Alaska begins darkness that will last 65 days in the polar regions. Earth
